https://revistas.ucr.ac.cr/index.php/rlm/issue/archive,Política de privacidad (sin licencia explícita),DEPENDE,"El texto proporcionado solo menciona ""Declaración de privacidad"" sin incluir cláusulas específicas sobre uso permitido, consentimiento o restricciones; se necesita el contenido real de la declaración para evaluar si el uso es permitido.","[{""categoria"": null, ""via"": ""crawl_candidato"", ""url_origen"": ""https://revistas.ucr.ac.cr/index.php/rlm/issue/archive"", ""markdown_path"": null, ""texto_inline"": ""# Declaración de privacidad"", ""veredicto"": ""DEPENDE"", ""justificacion"": ""El texto proporcionado solo menciona \""Declaración de privacidad\"" sin incluir cláusulas específicas sobre uso permitido, consentimiento o restricciones; se necesita el contenido real de la declaración para evaluar si el uso es permitido.""}]",1,"El texto solo es un título sin contenido sustancial, lo que impide evaluar si su uso es legalmente permitido; aunque no es incompatible por sí mismo, la falta de detalles lo hace probablemente no usable sin la versión completa."
https://revistas.ucr.ac.cr/index.php/matematica/issue/archive,Política de privacidad (sin licencia explícita),DEPENDE,"El texto proporcionado solo menciona ""Declaración de privacidad"" sin incluir el contenido real que detalle los términos de uso, permisos o restricciones; se necesita revisar la cláusula específica para determinar si el uso está permitido.","[{""categoria"": null, ""via"": ""crawl_candidato"", ""url_origen"": ""https://revistas.ucr.ac.cr/index.php/matematica/issue/archive"", ""markdown_path"": null, ""texto_inline"": ""# Declaración de privacidad"", ""veredicto"": ""DEPENDE"", ""justificacion"": ""El texto proporcionado solo menciona \""Declaración de privacidad\"" sin incluir el contenido real que detalle los términos de uso, permisos o restricciones; se necesita revisar la cláusula específica para determinar si el uso está permitido.""}]",1,"El texto solo contiene un título genérico sin contenido sustancial, lo que impide evaluar permisos o restricciones legales; por tanto, es probable que no se pueda usar sin información adicional."
https://revistas.ucr.ac.cr/index.php/medica/issue/archive,Política de privacidad (sin licencia explícita),DEPENDE,"El texto proporcionado solo menciona el título ""Declaración de privacidad"" sin incluir el contenido real que detalle los términos de uso, consentimiento o permisos otorgados; se requiere revisar las cláusulas específicas para determinar si el uso está permitido.","[{""categoria"": null, ""via"": ""crawl_candidato"", ""url_origen"": ""https://revistas.ucr.ac.cr/index.php/medica/issue/archive"", ""markdown_path"": null, ""texto_inline"": ""# Declaración de privacidad"", ""veredicto"": ""DEPENDE"", ""justificacion"": ""El texto proporcionado solo menciona el título \""Declaración de privacidad\"" sin incluir el contenido real que detalle los términos de uso, consentimiento o permisos otorgados; se requiere revisar las cláusulas específicas para determinar si el uso está permitido.""}]",1,"Solo tiene un título sin contenido sustancial, por lo que no permite evaluar si se pueden usar los términos, lo que lo hace probablemente inutilizable para fines legales."
https://revistas.ucr.ac.cr/index.php/RDMCP/issue/archive,Política de privacidad (sin licencia explícita),DEPENDE,"El texto proporcionado solo menciona ""Declaración de privacidad"" sin incluir el contenido real de la política, por lo que no se puede determinar si permite o restringe el uso del contenido; se requiere revisar las cláusulas específicas sobre uso, recolección o compartir datos.","[{""categoria"": null, ""via"": ""crawl_candidato"", ""url_origen"": ""https://revistas.ucr.ac.cr/index.php/RDMCP/issue/archive"", ""markdown_path"": null, ""texto_inline"": ""# Declaración de privacidad"", ""veredicto"": ""DEPENDE"", ""justificacion"": ""El texto proporcionado solo menciona \""Declaración de privacidad\"" sin incluir el contenido real de la política, por lo que no se puede determinar si permite o restringe el uso del contenido; se requiere revisar las cláusulas específicas sobre uso, recolección o compartir datos.""}]",1,"Solo se menciona el título sin contenido real, por lo que no hay información suficiente para evaluar permisos de uso, lo que lo hace probablemente no usable sin más detalles."
https://revistas.ucr.ac.cr/index.php/riea/issue/archive,Política de privacidad (sin licencia explícita),SI,"El texto establece que los datos personales (nombres y direcciones de correo) se usarán exclusivamente para los fines de la revista y no se proporcionarán a terceros, lo que permite su uso dentro de esos límites.","[{""categoria"": null, ""via"": ""crawl_candidato"", ""url_origen"": ""https://revistas.ucr.ac.cr/index.php/riea/issue/archive"", ""markdown_path"": null, ""texto_inline"": ""# Declaración de privacidad\n\n---\n\n## Acerca de – Declaración de privacidad\n\nLos nombres y las direcciones de correo electrónico introducidos en esta revista se usarán exclusivamente para los fines establecidos en ella y no se proporcionarán a terceros o para su uso con otros fines."", ""veredicto"": ""SI"", ""justificacion"": ""El texto establece que los datos personales (nombres y direcciones de correo) se usarán exclusivamente para los fines de la revista y no se proporcionarán a terceros, lo que permite su uso dentro de esos límites.""}]",,
https://revistas.ucr.ac.cr/index.php/sociales/issue/archive,Política de privacidad (sin licencia explícita),DEPENDE,"El texto proporcionado solo menciona ""Declaración de privacidad"" sin incluir el contenido real que detalle cómo se pueden usar, compartir o reproducir los datos o el contenido; se requiere revisar las cláusulas específicas sobre uso, consentimiento o licencias para determinar si el uso está permitido.","[{""categoria"": null, ""via"": ""crawl_candidato"", ""url_origen"": ""https://revistas.ucr.ac.cr/index.php/sociales/issue/archive"", ""markdown_path"": null, ""texto_inline"": ""# Declaración de privacidad"", ""veredicto"": ""DEPENDE"", ""justificacion"": ""El texto proporcionado solo menciona \""Declaración de privacidad\"" sin incluir el contenido real que detalle cómo se pueden usar, compartir o reproducir los datos o el contenido; se requiere revisar las cláusulas específicas sobre uso, consentimiento o licencias para determinar si el uso está permitido.""}]",1,"El texto solo es un título sin contenido sustancial, por lo que no permite evaluar permisos de uso; sin información sobre cláusulas de licencia o consentimiento, es probable que no se pueda usar legalmente."
https://revistas.ucr.ac.cr/index.php/wimblu/issue/archive,Política de privacidad (sin licencia explícita),DEPENDE,"El texto proporcionado solo menciona el título ""Declaración de privacidad"" sin incluir el contenido real que detalle los términos de uso, consentimiento o permisos otorgados; se necesita revisar las cláusulas específicas para determinar si el uso está permitido.","[{""categoria"": null, ""via"": ""crawl_candidato"", ""url_origen"": ""https://revistas.ucr.ac.cr/index.php/wimblu/issue/archive"", ""markdown_path"": null, ""texto_inline"": ""# Declaración de privacidad"", ""veredicto"": ""DEPENDE"", ""justificacion"": ""El texto proporcionado solo menciona el título \""Declaración de privacidad\"" sin incluir el contenido real que detalle los términos de uso, consentimiento o permisos otorgados; se necesita revisar las cláusulas específicas para determinar si el uso está permitido.""}]",1,"El texto solo contiene un título sin contenido sustancial, por lo que no permite evaluar si se pueden usar los términos de privacidad; falta información crítica para cualquier uso legal, lo que lo hace probablemente no usable."
https://www.museonacional.gov.co,No encontrada,SIN_TEXTO,No se detectó texto de licencia/términos/privacidad en el sitio.,[],,
https://revistas.ucr.ac.cr/index.php/antropologia/issue/archive,Política de privacidad (sin licencia explícita),DEPENDE,"El texto solo contiene la estructura de un sitio web de Creative Commons, sin especificar los términos de uso del contenido en cuestión; se requiere identificar la licencia específica aplicable al contenido original para determinar su uso permitido.","[{""categoria"": null, ""via"": ""crawl_candidato"", ""url_origen"": ""https://revistas.ucr.ac.cr/index.php/antropologia/issue/archive"", ""markdown_path"": null, ""texto_inline"": ""# Declaración de privacidad\n\n---\n\n# [Creative Commons](/)\n\nMenu\n\n* [Who We Are](/who-we-are)\n  Expand\n  + [Strategic Plan](/strategic-plan)\n  + [Team](/team)\n  + [Governance](/governance)\n  + [Opportunities](/opportunities)\n  + [Annual Reports & Financials](/annual-reports/)\n  + [History](/history/)\n  + [Press](/press)\n* [What We Do](/what-we-do)\n  Expand\n  + [Build   \n    Open Infrastructure](/build/)\n\n    Expand\n    - [CC Licenses](/cc-licenses)\n    - [CC Signals](/cc-signals)\n    - [Public Domain](/public-domain)\n    - [Chooser](/chooser)\n    - [FAQs](/faq)\n  + [Implement   \n    the Commons](/implement/)\n\n    Expand\n    - [Where CC Makes An Impact](/impact)\n    - [Resources](/resources)\n    - [Search the Commons](https://search.creativecommons.org)\n  + [Engage   \n    the People](/engage/)\n\n    Expand\n    - [Training + Webinars](/training-and-webinars)\n    - [Advocacy](/advocacy)\n    - [Community](/community)\n    - [Events](/events)\n* [Blog](/blog)\n* [Support Us](/support)\n  Expand\n  + [Make a Gift](https://giving.gofundme.com/campaign/778218/donate)\n  + [Open Infrastructure Circle](/support/oic)\n  + [Donor FAQ](/support/donor-faq)\n* [Donate](https://giving.gofundme.com/campaign/778218/donate)"", ""veredicto"": ""DEPENDE"", ""justificacion"": ""El texto solo contiene la estructura de un sitio web de Creative Commons, sin especificar los términos de uso del contenido en cuestión; se requiere identificar la licencia específica aplicable al contenido original para determinar su uso permitido.""}]",1,"El texto solo es una estructura de menú de un sitio web, sin contener el contenido protegido ni la licencia aplicable, por lo que no permite determinar si su uso es legal; es poco útil y potencialmente engañoso si se asume que es contenido usable."
https://revistas.ucr.ac.cr/index.php/dialogos/issue/archive,Política de privacidad (sin licencia explícita),DEPENDE,"El texto proporcionado solo menciona ""Declaración de privacidad"" sin incluir cláusulas específicas sobre uso permitido, consentimiento o restricciones; se necesita más contenido para determinar si el uso es autorizado.","[{""categoria"": null, ""via"": ""crawl_candidato"", ""url_origen"": ""https://revistas.ucr.ac.cr/index.php/dialogos/issue/archive"", ""markdown_path"": null, ""texto_inline"": ""# Declaración de privacidad"", ""veredicto"": ""DEPENDE"", ""justificacion"": ""El texto proporcionado solo menciona \""Declaración de privacidad\"" sin incluir cláusulas específicas sobre uso permitido, consentimiento o restricciones; se necesita más contenido para determinar si el uso es autorizado.""}]",1,"El texto es extremadamente limitado y no contiene cláusulas sustantivas sobre uso, consentimiento o restricciones, lo que lo hace prácticamente inútil para su uso legal; sin embargo, podría servir como plantilla base si se expande significativamente."
https://revistas.ucr.ac.cr/index.php/eciencias/issue/archive,Licencia mencionada (ver comentarios),DEPENDE,"El texto corresponde a la licencia CC BY-NC-ND 3.0, que permite compartir el material con atribución y sin fines comerciales ni modificaciones, pero su uso depende de si se cumplen estas condiciones específicas (atribución, no comercial, sin derivados).","[{""categoria"": null, ""via"": ""rel_license"", ""url_origen"": ""https://revistas.ucr.ac.cr/index.php/eciencias/issue/archive"", ""markdown_path"": null, ""texto_inline"": ""[Skip to content](#main-content-marker)\n\n\nLanguages available\n\naragonés\n\nAzərbaycanca\n\nBahasa Indonesia\n\nBasque\n\ncatalà\n\ndansk\n\nDeutsch\n\neesti\n\nEnglish\n\nespañol\n\nEsperanto\n\nfrançais\n\nfrysk\n\nGaeilge\n\ngalego\n\nHrvatski\n\nitaliano\n\nlatviešu\n\nLietuviškai\n\nMagyar\n\nMelayu\n\nNederlands\n\nnorsk\n\npolski\n\nPortuguês\n\nPortuguês Brasileiro\n\nRomână\n\nSlovensky\n\nSlovenščina\n\nsrpski (latinica)\n\nsuomi\n\nsvenska\n\nTürkçe\n\nÍslenska\n\nčesky\n\nΕλληνικά\n\nбеларуская\n\nбългарски\n\nРусский\n\nУкраїнська\n\nالعربيّة\n\nفارسی\n\nहिंदी\n\nবাংলা\n\n日本語\n\n简体中文\n\n繁體中文\n\n한국어\n\n\n\n## Notice\n\nThis is an older version of this license. Compared to previous\nversions, the 4.0 versions of all CC licenses are\n[more user-friendly and more internationally robust](/version4/). If you are  [licensing your own work](/choose/), we\nstrongly recommend the use of the 4.0 license instead:\n[Deed - Attribution-NonCommercial-NoDerivatives 4.0\nInternational](../4.0/deed.en)\n\n## Canonical URL\n\n<https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/3.0/>\n\n[See the legal code](legalcode.en)\n\n## You are free to:\n\n1. **Share** — copy and redistribute the material in any\n   medium or format\n2. The licensor cannot revoke these freedoms as long as you follow\n   the license terms.\n\n## Under the following terms:\n\n1. **Attribution** — You must give\n   [appropriate credit](#ref-appropriate-credit), provide a link to the license, and\n   [indicate if changes were made](#ref-indicate-changes). You may do so in any reasonable manner, but not in any way that\n   suggests the licensor endorses you or your use.\n2. **NonCommercial** — You may not use the material for\n   [commercial purposes](#ref-commercial-purposes).\n3. **NoDerivatives** — If you\n   [remix, transform, or build upon](#ref-some-kinds-of-mods)\n   the material, you may not distribute the modified material.\n4. **No additional restrictions** — You may not apply\n   legal terms or\n   [technological measures](#ref-technological-measures)\n   that legally restrict others from doing anything the license\n   permits.\n\n## Notices:\n\nYou do not have to comply with the license for elements of the\nmaterial in the public domain or where your use is permitted by an\napplicable\n[exception or limitation](#ref-exception-or-limitation).\n\nNo warranties are given. The license may not give you all of the\npermissions necessary for your intended use. For example, other\nrights such as\n[publicity, privacy, or moral rights](#ref-publicity-privacy-or-moral-rights)\nmay limit how you use the material.\n\nCreative Commons is the nonprofit behind the open licenses and other\nlegal tools that allow creators to share their work. Our legal tools\nare free to use.\n\n* [Learn more about our work](/about/)\n* **[Learn more about CC Licensing](/share-your-work/cclicenses/)**\n* [Support our work](/donate/)\n* [Use the license for your own material.](/choose/)\n* [Licenses List](/licenses/list.en)\n* [Public Domain List](/publicdomain/list.en)\n\n\n---\n\n[Skip to content](#main-content-marker)\n\n**Stay informed. Sign up for [CC’s newsletter](https://mail.creativecommons.org/subscribe).**\n\n![]()\n\n\n\n1. Do you know which license you need?\n\n\n   Yes\n\n   No\n2. Which license do you need?\n   License\n\n   —choose a license—\n   CC0 1.0\n   CC-BY 4.0\n   CC-BY-SA 4.0\n   CC-BY-ND 4.0\n   CC-BY-NC 4.0\n   CC-BY-NC-SA 4.0\n   CC-BY-NC-ND 4.0\n3. Require attribution for your work?\n\n   Yes\n\n   No\n4. Allow others to use your work commercially?\n\n   Yes\n\n   No\n5. Allow others to remix, adapt, or build upon your work?\n\n   Yes\n\n   No\n6. Require adaptions of your work to be licensed under the same CC license?\n\n   Yes\n\n   No\n7. Waive your copyright\n\n\n   I hereby waive all copyright and related or neighboring rights together with all associated claims and causes of action with respect to this work to the extent possible under the law.\n\n   I have read and understand the terms and intended legal effect of CC0, and hereby voluntarily elect to apply it to this work.\n8. Confirm that CC Licensing is appropriate\n\n   I own or have authority to license the work.\n\n   I have read and understand the terms of the license.\n\n   I understand that CC licensing is not revocable.\n\n---\n\n9. Attribution details (optional)\n   This helps others attribute your work to you, and fills in machine-readable code.\n\n   Title of work\n\n   Creator of work\n\n   Link to work\n\n   Link to Creator Profile\n\n   Year of creation\n\n   ---\n\n   Title of recommended tool (read only)\n\n   URL of recommended tool (read only)\n\n\n\nWaiting for required fields...\n\n## Recommended Choice\n\nWebsite\n\nIf you are licensing or marking one work, paste the code next to it. If you are licensing or marking the whole page or blog, you can paste the code at the bottom of the page.\n\nRich Text\n\n[contextually formatted mark here]\n\nHTML\n[contextually formatted mark here]\n\n\nPrint Work or Media\n\nCopy the text below and paste it on the title and/or copyright page of your print work or presentation, or in the credits of your media.\n\nPlain Text\n\n[contextually formatted mark here]\n\n## Confused? Need Help?\n\nWhat are Creative Commons licenses?\n\nCreative Commons licenses are legal tools that help you grant copyright permissions to the general public. Our CC legal tools include [six different licenses](https://creativecommons.org/licenses/) and [one public domain dedication tool](https://creativecommons.org/share-your-work/public-domain/cc0/). It is important to specify which one of the 7 legal tools you are applying to your material. The license chooser can help you decide which license is right for you.\n\nCC licenses may be applied to any type of copyrightable work. The only types of works for which CC does not recommend its licenses are computer software and hardware, where we recommend a standard free software license instead. For works that are already in the public domain we recommend that you mark them with the [Public Domain Mark](https://creativecommons.org/about/pdm). If you hold the rights to a work but would like to place it into the public domain, you can use the Chooser to select CC0.\n\n\nHow to apply a Creative Commons license\n\nYou can license your work by marking it with the specific CC license you choose. This marking can be as simple as a bit of text stating the license in a copyright notice, or as complex as embedding the license information on your website using the HTML code associated with the particular license. We strongly recommend including a link to the applicable license (e.g., <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/>).\n\n\nWhat should I consider?\n\nAs a creator licensing a work, among [other considerations](https://wiki.creativecommons.org/wiki/Considerations_for_licensors_and_licensees#Considerations_for_licensors), you should:\n\n* [Remember that once you have applied a CC license, you cannot revoke it](https://wiki.creativecommons.org/wiki/Considerations_for_licensors_and_licensees#Remember_the_license_may_not_be_revoked.).\n* [Choose your license based on how you want the material to be used](https://wiki.creativecommons.org/wiki/Considerations_for_licensors_and_licensees#Think_about_how_you_want_the_material_to_be_used.).\n* [Let people know how to credit you (or whether you want credit at all)](https://wiki.creativecommons.org/wiki/Considerations_for_licensors_and_licensees#Specify_attribution_information_if_desired.).\n\nWhat do the icons mean?\n\nThe icons represent key features of the different CC license options:\n\nAttribution Required (BY)\n:   Credit must be given to you, the creator.\n\nCommercial Use Not Allowed (NC/NonCommercial)\n:   Only noncommercial use of your work is permitted.\n    *Noncommercial means not primarily intended for or directed towards commercial advantage or monetary compensation.*\n\nDistributed on Same Terms (SA/ShareAlike)\n:   Adaptations must be shared under the same terms.\n\nModifying Not Allowed (ND/NoDerivatives)\n:   No derivatives or adaptations of your work are permitted.\n\n\nWhat if I have other questions?\n\nYou can find a full list of our [frequently asked questions](https://creativecommons.org/faq/) on our site.\n\nIf you would like peer support in learning the best way to utilize this resource or choosing the best legal tool for you, you can become a part of CC’s Community by filling out the [Creative Commons Community Intake Form](https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSf2HY_wHq5SlgP_0U0ZWQKGXKwocNhm_vCPY34bUQrQ_hWoAQ/viewform?usp=dialog). You should receive an invitation to our chat platform, Zulip, in 5-10 business days..\n\n\n---\n\n[Skip to content](#main-content-marker)\n\n\nLanguages available\n\naragonés\n\nAzərbaycanca\n\nBahasa Indonesia\n\nBasque\n\ncatalà\n\ndansk\n\nDeutsch\n\neesti\n\nEnglish\n\nespañol\n\nEsperanto\n\nfrançais\n\nfrysk\n\nGaeilge\n\ngalego\n\nHrvatski\n\nitaliano\n\nlatviešu\n\nLietuviškai\n\nMagyar\n\nMelayu\n\nNederlands\n\nnorsk\n\npolski\n\nPortuguês\n\nPortuguês Brasileiro\n\nRomână\n\nSlovensky\n\nSlovenščina\n\nsrpski (latinica)\n\nsuomi\n\nsvenska\n\nTürkçe\n\nÍslenska\n\nčesky\n\nΕλληνικά\n\nбеларуская\n\nбългарски\n\nРусский\n\nУкраїнська\n\nالعربيّة\n\nفارسی\n\nहिंदी\n\nবাংলা\n\n日本語\n\n简体中文\n\n繁體中文\n\n한국어\n\n\n\n## Notice\n\nThis is an older version of this license. Compared to previous\nversions, the 4.0 versions of all CC licenses are\n[more user-friendly and more internationally robust](/version4/). If you are  [licensing your own work](/choose/), we\nstrongly recommend the use of the 4.0 license instead:\n[Deed - Attribution-NonCommercial-NoDerivatives 4.0\nInternational](../4.0/deed.en)\n\n## Canonical URL\n\n<https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/3.0/>\n\n[See the legal code](legalcode.en)\n\n## You are free to:\n\n1. **Share** — copy and redistribute the material in any\n   medium or format\n2. The licensor cannot revoke these freedoms as long as you follow\n   the license terms.\n\n## Under the following terms:\n\n1. **Attribution** — You must give\n   [appropriate credit](#ref-appropriate-credit), provide a link to the license, and\n   [indicate if changes were made](#ref-indicate-changes). You may do so in any reasonable manner, but not in any way that\n   suggests the licensor endorses you or your use.\n2. **NonCommercial** — You may not use the material for\n   [commercial purposes](#ref-commercial-purposes).\n3. **NoDerivatives** — If you\n   [remix, transform, or build upon](#ref-some-kinds-of-mods)\n   the material, you may not distribute the modified material.\n4. **No additional restrictions** — You may not apply\n   legal terms or\n   [technological measures](#ref-technological-measures)\n   that legally restrict others from doing anything the license\n   permits.\n\n## Notices:\n\nYou do not have to comply with the license for elements of the\nmaterial in the public domain or where your use is permitted by an\napplicable\n[exception or limitation](#ref-exception-or-limitation).\n\nNo warranties are given. The license may not give you all of the\npermissions necessary for your intended use. For example, other\nrights such as\n[publicity, privacy, or moral rights](#ref-publicity-privacy-or-moral-rights)\nmay limit how you use the material.\n\nCreative Commons is the nonprofit behind the open licenses and other\nlegal tools that allow creators to share their work. Our legal tools\nare free to use.\n\n* [Learn more about our work](/about/)\n* **[Learn more about CC Licensing](/share-your-work/cclicenses/)**\n* [Support our work](/donate/)\n* [Use the license for your own material.](/choose/)\n* [Licenses List](/licenses/list.en)\n* [Public Domain List](/publicdomain/list.en)\n\n\n---\n\n[Skip to content](#main-content-marker)\n\n**Stay informed. Sign up for [CC’s newsletter](https://mail.creativecommons.org/subscribe).**\n\n![]()\n\n\n\nEstablished in 2002, the CC licenses make it possible for everyone around the world to share knowledge, creativity, and culture, legally and freely.\n\n![](https://creativecommons.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/Group-39.png)\n\n## Licenses for the global public good\n\nCC licenses are a global [digital public good](https://www.digitalpublicgoods.net/r/creative-commons-legal-tools) and part of the essential infrastructure that makes sharing online possible. Today, there are tens of billions of CC-licensed works across the internet, spanning education, science, culture, and art, and more.\n\nCC licenses do more than function legally—they express values. The CC icons, now recognized around the world, represent openness, collaboration, and participation. For example, the CC logo is so ubiquitous it is part of the permanent design collection at The Museum of Modern Art in New York.\n\nLike the public infrastructure we rely on every day, such as roads and public schools, the legal and technical infrastructure behind CC licenses requires ongoing maintenance, updates, and support. Unlike most public infrastructure, however, CC licenses are not funded by taxes or user fees. As a public good, they depend on the support of the community that relies on them.\n\nHelp support the CC licenses infrastructure.\n\n[Donate Today](https://giving.gofundme.com/campaign/778218/donate)\n\n![](https://creativecommons.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/Group-40.png)\n\n## Used by leading platforms and institutions worldwide\n\n![Logos of organizations who utilize CC licenses. Logos shown: Flickr, YouTube, Internet Archive, Free Music Archive, Vimeo, MIT Open Courseware, Europeana Think Culture, Wikipedia, Bandcamp, Sketchfab, Wikimedia Commons, Tribe of Noise, and Skills Commons.](https://creativecommons.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/Untitled-design.png)\n\n## Why Use a CC License\n\nWithout CC licenses, copyright offers only two extremes: “all rights reserved” or “no rights reserved.” That doesn’t reflect the many ways creators want their work to be shared.\n\nCreative Commons licenses offer a standardized, legally-sound way to grant permission in advance, so that creators can clearly communicate how their work may be used, without negotiating individual permissions every time. This enables access to knowledge by offering a “some rights reserved” option for content that would otherwise be closed off.\n\nMost creators share a basic belief: that knowledge and creativity grow through sharing, not locking it away.\n\nIn the age of AI, much of how content is used by AI systems falls outside what our licenses can govern, because this use often sits outside what copyright, and therefore any CC license, was built to address. We’ve published [Guidance on CC Licensing in an AI ecosystem](https://creativecommons.org/cc-license-guidance/) to explain exactly what our licenses can and can’t do in this environment. That gap is also part of why we’re building [CC Signals](https://creativecommons.org/cc-signals/), a framework to give licensors more granular control over how their work is used by machines.\n\n![](https://creativecommons.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/Group-41.png)\n\n## The CC Licenses\n\nThere are six different license types, listed from most to least permissive here:\n\n* ### [CC BY](https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/)\n\n  ![](https://creativecommons.org/wp-content/themes/vocabulary-theme/vocabulary/svg/cc/license_badges/big/by.svg)\n\n  This license enables reusers to distribute, remix, adapt, and build upon the material in any medium or format, so long as attribution is given to the creator. The license allows for commercial use. CC BY includes the following elements:\n\n  BY\n  :   Credit must be given to you, the creator.\n* ### [CC BY-SA](https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/)\n\n  ![](https://creativecommons.org/wp-content/themes/vocabulary-theme/vocabulary/svg/cc/license_badges/big/by_sa.svg)\n\n  This license enables reusers to distribute, remix, adapt, and build upon the material in any medium or format, so long as attribution is given to the creator. The license allows for commercial use. If you remix, adapt, or build upon the material, you must license the modified material under  the same or a compatible license. CC BY-SA includes the following elements:\n\n  BY\n  :   Credit must be given to you, the creator.\n\n  SA\n  :   Adaptations must be shared under the same terms.\n* ### [CC BY-ND](https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nd/4.0/)\n\n  ![](https://creativecommons.org/wp-content/themes/vocabulary-theme/vocabulary/svg/cc/license_badges/big/by_nd.svg)\n\n  This license enables reusers to copy and distribute the material in any medium or format in unadapted form only, and only so long as attribution is given to the creator. The license allows for commercial use. CC BY-ND includes the following elements:\n\n  BY\n  :   Credit must be given to you, the creator.\n\n  ND\n  :   No derivatives or adaptations of your work are permitted.\n* ### [CC BY-NC](https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/)\n\n  ![](https://creativecommons.org/wp-content/themes/vocabulary-theme/vocabulary/svg/cc/license_badges/big/by_nc.svg)\n\n  This license enables reusers to distribute, remix, adapt, and build upon the material in any medium or format for noncommercial purposes only, and only so long as attribution is given to the creator. CC BY-NC includes the following elements:\n\n  BY\n  :   Credit must be given to you, the creator.\n\n  NC\n  :   Only noncommercial use of your work is permitted.\n      *Noncommercial means not primarily intended for or directed towards commercial advantage or monetary compensation.*\n* ### [CC BY-NC-SA](https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/)\n\n  ![](https://creativecommons.org/wp-content/themes/vocabulary-theme/vocabulary/svg/cc/license_badges/big/by_nc_sa.svg)\n\n  This license enables reusers to distribute, remix, adapt, and build upon the material in any medium or format for noncommercial purposes only if attribution is given to the creator. If you remix, adapt, or build upon the material, you must license the modified material under the same or a compatible license. CC BY-NC-SA includes the following elements:\n\n  BY\n  :   Credit must be given to you, the creator.\n\n  NC\n  :   Only noncommercial use of your work is permitted.\n      *Noncommercial means not primarily intended for or directed towards commercial advantage or monetary compensation.*\n\n  SA\n  :   Adaptations must be shared under the same terms.\n* ### [CC BY-NC-ND](https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/)\n\n  ![](https://creativecommons.org/wp-content/themes/vocabulary-theme/vocabulary/svg/cc/license_badges/big/by_nc_nd.svg)\n\n  This license enables reusers to copy and distribute the material in any medium or format in unadapted form only, for noncommercial purposes only, and only if attribution is given to the creator. CC BY-NC-ND includes the following elements:\n\n  BY\n  :   Credit must be given to you, the creator.\n\n  NC\n  :   Only noncommercial use of your work is permitted.\n      *Noncommercial means not primarily intended for or directed towards commercial advantage or monetary compensation.*\n\n  ND\n  :   No derivatives or adaptations of your work are permitted.\n\n## Multilingual Support\n\nThe deeds and legal codes of the CC licenses are translated into over 45 languages.\n\n## Get the latest CC news, updates, events, resources, and more right to your inbox!\n\n[Sign up for CC’s Newsletter](https://mail.creativecommons.org/subscribe)\n\n![](https://creativecommons.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/Untitled-design-1.png)\n\n\n---\n\n[Skip to content](#main-content-marker)\n\n\nLanguages available\n\naragonés\n\nAzərbaycanca\n\nBahasa Indonesia\n\nBasque\n\ncatalà\n\ndansk\n\nDeutsch\n\neesti\n\nEnglish\n\nespañol\n\nEsperanto\n\nfrançais\n\nfrysk\n\nGaeilge\n\ngalego\n\nHrvatski\n\nitaliano\n\nlatviešu\n\nLietuviškai\n\nMagyar\n\nMelayu\n\nNederlands\n\nnorsk\n\npolski\n\nPortuguês\n\nPortuguês Brasileiro\n\nRomână\n\nSlovensky\n\nSlovenščina\n\nsrpski (latinica)\n\nsuomi\n\nsvenska\n\nTürkçe\n\nÍslenska\n\nčesky\n\nΕλληνικά\n\nбеларуская\n\nбългарски\n\nРусский\n\nУкраїнська\n\nالعربيّة\n\nفارسی\n\nहिंदी\n\nবাংলা\n\n日本語\n\n简体中文\n\n繁體中文\n\n한국어\n\n\n\n\n\nCreative Commons is the nonprofit behind the open licenses and other\nlegal tools that allow creators to share their work. Our legal tools\nare free to use.\n\n* [Learn more about our work](/about/)\n* **[Learn more about CC Licensing](/share-your-work/cclicenses/)**\n* [Support our work](/donate/)\n* [Use the license for your own material.](/choose/)\n* [Public Domain List](/publicdomain/list.en)\n\n## 4.0 Licenses\n\n### 4.0 International\n\n| Language | Legal Tools | | | | | |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `by` | `by-nc` | `by-nc-nd` | `by-nc-sa` | `by-nd` | `by-sa` |\n| Bahasa Indonesia | [Deed](by/4.0/deed.id)  [Legal Code](by/4.0/legalcode.id) | [Deed](by-nc/4.0/deed.id)  [Legal Code](by-nc/4.0/legalcode.id) | [Deed](by-nc-nd/4.0/deed.id)  [Legal Code](by-nc-nd/4.0/legalcode.id) | [Deed](by-nc-sa/4.0/deed.id)  [Legal Code](by-nc-sa/4.0/legalcode.id) | [Deed](by-nd/4.0/deed.id)  [Legal Code](by-nd/4.0/legalcode.id) | [Deed](by-sa/4.0/deed.id)  [Legal Code](by-sa/4.0/legalcode.id) |\n| Basque | [Deed](by/4.0/deed.eu)  [Legal Code](by/4.0/legalcode.eu) | [Deed](by-nc/4.0/deed.eu)  [Legal 