\n\nEl Usuario responderá de los daños y perjuicios de todo tipo, directos o indirectos, que NESTLÉ, otros Usuarios o terceros puedan sufrir como consecuencia de la infracción, por parte del Usuario, de cualquiera de los términos a que éste se obliga mediante los presentes Términos y Condiciones de Uso, o de la infracción a las normas vigentes aplicables.\n\nSin perjuicio de lo anterior, si como consecuencia de un incumplimiento del Usuario de estos Términos y Condiciones de Uso, NESTLÉ fuere obligada a pagar multas, indemnizaciones u otro tipo de compensaciones, que resulten de la aplicación de una medida administrativa o de una resolución judicial, el Usuario deberá reembolsar a NESTLÉ la totalidad de los montos pagados por tal motivo, incluyendo honorarios de asesores.\n\n## **9.- EXCLUSIÓN DE GARANTÍAS**\n\nNESTLÉ ha realizado de buena fe este Sitio para ofrecer a sus consumidores y público en general Servicios y Materiales de calidad, confiables y seguros.\n\nEl Usuario reconoce y acepta que, por su naturaleza, la prestación de servicio de este Sitio, sus Servicios y Materiales, conlleva riesgos, contingencias o eventualidades de imposible o difícil detección y control por parte de NESTLÉ, y que eventualmente pueden causar perjuicios al Usuario.\n\nEn consecuencia, el Usuario acepta la prestación del servicio de este Sitio, sus Servicios y Materiales, en las condiciones en que efectivamente se entreguen y asume personalmente las consecuencias de su decisión de hacer uso del mismo.\n\nNESTLÉ no garantiza en caso alguno:\n\n1. La exactitud o veracidad de cualquier información contenida en el Sitio, los Servicios o los Materiales.  \n 2. La disponibilidad, continuidad, accesibilidad, funcionamiento, operatividad o calidad del Sitio, los Servicios o los Materiales.\n\n3. La licitud, fiabilidad, calidad, utilidad o veracidad de la información, ausencia de virus u otros elementos perjudiciales de los Servicios o Materiales del Sitio.  \n 4. La veracidad o vigencia o autenticidad de la información de los datos personales proporcionados por los Usuarios.\n\n5. El cumplimiento, por parte de los Usuarios, de la ley, los Términos y Condiciones de Uso, la moral, las buenas costumbres o el orden público, en el acceso o utilización que hagan del Sitio, los Servicios y los Materiales.\n\n## **10.- RESPONSABILIDAD DE NESTLÉ**\n\nNESTLÉ no se hace responsable por los daños o perjuicios, de cualquier naturaleza que estos sean, directos o indirectos, que se produzcan como consecuencia de o con ocasión o en relación con el uso que el Usuario haga del Sitio, los Servicios o los Materiales.\n\nLa información, sugerencias o consejos que aparezcan en el Sitio pretenden ser una guía general con fines de información y ayuda, y en ningún caso sustituye el consejo profesional en materias personales, médicas, legales, fiscales, contables, financieras ni de ningún otro tipo. El Usuario debe consultar a un profesional adecuado para obtener información específica de acuerdo a su situación personal.\n\nAsimismo, los enlaces y vínculos no implican responsabilidad alguna para la Empresa ni aprobación por parte de ésta respecto de la información contenida en los mismos; los enlaces e hiperconexiones con otros medios de Internet son a su propio riesgo; NESTLÉ no investiga, no verifica, no controla ni respalda el contenido, exactitud, legalidad y opiniones expresadas en otras conexiones suministradas por estos medios.\n\nNESTLÉ CHILE garantiza la confidencialidad de la información personal del Usuario, la cual sólo será usada para los efectos propios de sus promociones.\n\n## **11.- DERECHOS DE PROPIEDAD INTELECTUAL E INDUSTRIAL DE PROPIEDAD DE NESTLÉ**\n\nLa totalidad de la información que contiene este Sitio, será considerada para todos los efectos legales de propiedad de NESTLÉ CHILE S.A., sin perjuicio de que ella, como licenciataria de Société des Produits Nestlé S.A., con domicilio en Vevey, Suiza, establezca lo contrario, pudiendo utilizar con cualquier fin toda idea, concepto, conocimiento o técnica incluidas en la información que proporcione un visitante a través de este Sitio.\n\nNESTLÉ no estará sujeto a obligación alguna en cuanto a la confidencialidad de la información presentada, salvo acuerdo en contrario entre la empresa y sus clientes, proveedores y asociados, y las exigencias legales que rigen actualmente al respecto y las que se incorporen en el futuro.\n\nLos derechos de propiedad intelectual de estas páginas, de las pantallas que muestran estas páginas, de la información y material que aparecen en las mismas y de su disposición, pertenecen a NESTLÉ, salvo lo indicado en el punto 12 siguiente.\n\nEste Sitio y los contenidos que alberga se encuentran protegidos por las leyes de Propiedad Industrial e Intelectual, y por los tratados internacionales suscritos y ratificados por Chile. Estos contenidos no podrán ser objeto de explotación, reproducción, distribución, modificación, comunicación pública, cesión o transformación, ni de ningún otro acto jurídico por parte de un tercero no autorizado expresamente y por escrito por NESTLÉ. El acceso a este Sitio no otorga a los usuarios derecho, ni titularidad alguna sobre los derechos de propiedad intelectual de los contenidos que alberga este Sitio.\n\nEl contenido de este Sitio puede ser descargado al terminal del usuario (download) siempre que sea para su uso privado inmediato y sin ningún fin comercial. Por lo tanto el Usuario no podrá explotar, reproducir, distribuir, modificar, comunicar públicamente, ceder, transformar o usar el contenido de este Sitio con fines públicos o comerciales.\n\nNESTLÉ no transfiere a los Usuarios la propiedad de su software. El Usuario es el propietario del soporte en el cual es software es grabado. NESTLÉ retiene todos los derechos de propiedad industrial e intelectual incluyendo el software. Si el Usuario transfiere software de este Sitio a su terminal, no podrá diseccionarlo para su estudio, o descompilarlo, traducir la versión del código objeto original o su lenguaje a otro código o lenguaje.\n\nTodas las marcas, logotipos, diseños, frases de propaganda, y en general todos los signos distintivos mostrados en este Sitio son propiedad de NESTLÉ o de terceros o empresas ligadas que han autorizado el uso de los mismos a NESTLÉ. Se prohíbe a los Usuarios y a terceros usar estos signos distintivos, descargarlos permanentemente, copiarlos o distribuirlos por cualquier medio sin el permiso escrito de NESTLÉ o de la tercera empresa titular de los derechos.\n\n## **12.- APORTES DE TERCEROS**\n\nLa legitimidad de los derechos de propiedad intelectual o industrial correspondientes a los contenidos aportados por Usuarios o por terceros es de la exclusiva responsabilidad de los mismos. A los efectos de preservar los posibles derechos de propiedad intelectual, en el caso de\n\nque cualquier Usuario o un tercero considere que se ha producido una violación de sus legítimos derechos por la introducción de un determinado contenido en el Sitio, deberá notificar dicha circunstancia, por escrito, a Nestlé Chile S.A.\n\nSin perjuicio de lo anterior, al momento de acceder o registrarse en el Sitio, y por lo tanto aceptar los Términos y Condiciones de Uso señaladas en este texto, el Usuario se compromete a hacer un uso adecuado de los Materiales y Servicios que son ofrecidos a través del Sitio, y a no emplearlos para (a) incurrir en actividades ilícitas, ilegales o contrarias a la buena fe y al orden público; ni (b) difundir contenidos o propaganda de carácter racista, xenófobo, pornográfico, de apología del terrorismo o atentatorio contra los derechos humanos; ni (c) provocar daños en los sistemas físicos y lógicos de NESTLÉ o sus empresas asociadas, de sus proveedores o de terceras personas, introducir o difundir en la red virus informáticos o cualesquiera otros sistemas físicos o lógicos que sean susceptibles de provocar los daños anteriormente mencionados; ni (d) difundir contenidos que atenten contra la imagen y reputación de NESTLÉ o de terceros.\n\nEl Usuario declara y garantiza a NESTLÉ que posee todos los derechos de Propiedad Intelectual sobre los mensajes y contenidos que introduzca en el Sitio.\n\nEl Usuario acepta conforme que se utilice tanto su imagen, su voz y su nombre de manera pública , dentro del Sitio, para cualquier nota periodística, cobertura promocional, u otras publicaciones relacionadas con el Sitio, sin exigir por ello suma de dinero correspondiente a derechos de imagen, de su voz o de su nombre, ni de ningún otro tipo. Por este medio, el Usuario cede los derechos de imagen en forma permanente a favor de NESTLÉ, pero solo para los efectos antes indicados.\n\n## **13.- CESIÓN DE DERECHOS**\n\nCon el mero envío de un trabajo, colaboración, receta, imagen, comentario, entre otros, el Usuario faculta a NESTLÉ, además de a incluirlo en el Sitio, para, por sí misma o mediante su cesión a terceros, proceder a su reproducción, distribución y comunicación pública, en versión completa, condensada, adaptada o abreviada, gratuita u onerosamente, en todo el mundo, en todos los idiomas, en otros productos que realice, y para todo tipo de usos. Los derechos cedidos podrán ser ejercitados en formato impreso, en cualesquiera modalidades de edición, en soporte electrónico (óptico, magnético, magnético-óptico o digital) u otros soportes tecnológicamente adaptables al formato solicitado por este Sitio.\n\nLa inclusión en el Sitio de elementos proporcionados por los Usuarios no implica respaldo, patrocinio o recomendación alguna de NESTLÉ sobre los mismos, por lo que NESTLÉ no será responsable en absoluto respecto de su contenido y licitud.\n\nNESTLÉ tendrá plena libertad de decisión sobre si las colaboraciones y mensajes enviados son finalmente publicadas en el Sitio o no, quedando facultada para retirarlos cuando estime oportuno, pudiendo publicar los contenidos suministrados por el Usuario de forma parcial, resumida o abreviada, sin ulterior responsabilidad.\n\n## **14.- POLÍTICA DE PROTECCIÓN DE DATOS PERSONALES**\n\nLa Política de Protección de Datos Personales de este Sitio ha sido establecida según las disposiciones de la Ley 19.628 sobre Protección de la Vida Privada Datos y la Política de Protección de Datos Personales de Nestlé. Esta política tiene como objetivo la protección y el respeto de los derechos de las personas naturales a tener su vida privada y familiar, correspondencia privada y comunicaciones. Esto incluye el derecho a ser informado y tomar decisiones respecto del procesamiento de sus datos personales.\n\nConforme a lo anterior, se entenderá por:\n\n* -  Datos personales: Cualquier información relativa a una persona natural identificada o identificable.\n* -  Datos sensibles: Aquellos datos personales que se refieren a las características físicas o morales de las personas o a hechos o circunstancias de su vida privada o intimidad, tales como lo hábitos personales, el origen racial, las ideologías y opiniones políticas, las creencias o convicciones religiosas, los estados de salud físicos o psíquicos, la vida sexual, la pertenencia a sindicatos, y la información relativa a la comisión o la sospecha de comisión de ofensas o delitos, y los resultados de los respectivos procesos judiciales o de otro tipo.\n* -  Titular de los datos: La persona natural identificada o identificable a la que se refieren los datos personales.\n* -  Controlador de datos: La compañía o persona que, por sí misma o junto con otros, es competente de acuerdo con la ley chilena para determinar el propósito y medios de procesamiento de los datos personales.\n* -  Receptor: cualquier persona natural o jurídica, autoridad pública, agencia o cualquier otra entidad a quien se le revelen los datos personales, sea o no un tercero. Sin embargo, las autoridades que puedan recibir datos personales en el marco de una consulta particular no serán consideradas receptores.\n* -  Procesamiento de datos personales: cualquier operación o conjunto de operaciones que se realice respecto de los datos personales, sea o no por medios automatizados, que permitan recolectar, almacenar, grabar, organizar, elaborar, adaptar, alterar, seleccionar, usar, extraer, consultar, confrontar, interconectar, disociar, comunicar, ceder, transferir, revelar, diseminar, transmitir, alinear, cancelar, bloquear, borrar o destruir datos personales, o utilizarlos en cualquier otra forma.\n* -  Transferencia de datos personales: Cualquier transferencia de datos personales que sean objeto de procesamiento o que se pretendan procesar después de su transferencia a través de límites nacionales.\n* -  Base de datos: Conjunto organizado de datos personales, sea automatizado o no, cualquiera sea la forma o modalidad de su creación u organización, que permita relacionar los datos entre sí, así como realizar todo tipo de procesamiento de datos.\n\nLa visita a este Sitio no supone que el Usuario esté obligado a proporcionar a NESTLÉ sus datos personales. En el caso de que el Usuario proporcione sus datos personales, dichos datos personales recogidos en este Sitio serán utilizados con el propósito, en la forma y con las limitaciones y derechos que recoge la Ley 19.628 sobre Protección de la Vida Privada.\n\nEl propósito y el uso de los datos personales que el Usuario proporcione a NESTLÉ están recogidos en el texto legal del respectivo formulario que el Usuario complete en este Sitio. Los datos personales suministrados por los Usuarios no serán procesados de ninguna manera incompatible\n\ncon los propósitos especificados inicialmente, sin informarles a, y obtener nuevamente autorización de, los Usuarios/titulares de los datos personales respectivos.\n\nLos datos personales solicitados por NESTLÉ sus Usuarios serán adecuados, relevantes y no serán excesivos en relación con el propósito específico para el cual fueron solicitados. NESTLÉ procederá a la cancelación o eliminación de los datos personales recogidos cuando éstos dejen de ser necesarios o pertinentes para el propósito para el que hubiesen sido recabados o registrados.\n\nAl momento de recabar o recolectar datos personales, el titular de los mismos recibirá la siguiente información de parte de NESTLÉ o de la persona natural o jurídica que NESTLÉ designe para estos efectos, antes de que los datos sean procesados:\n\n* -  La identidad del controlador de datos.\n* -  El (los) propósito(s) específico(s) para los cuales se pretenden procesar los datos\n\n  personales.\n* -  Las categorías de datos personales implicadas.\n* -  Si la respuesta a cada una de las preguntas incluidas en el formulario de recolección de\n\n  datos es voluntaria o es obligatoria, así como las posibles consecuencias de no contestar\n\n  una pregunta.\n* -  La existencia del derecho de acceso a y del derecho a rectificar los datos personales\n\n  relativos al titular.\n\nEl titular debe recibir esta información en el mismo momento en que se requiera su consentimiento (y en todo caso antes de que otorgue su consentimiento).\n\nAl momento de recabar datos personales, el titular de los mismos debe dar a NESTLÉ, o a la persona natural o jurídica designada por NESTLÉ, su consentimiento inequívoco antes de que sus datos personales sean procesados. Este consentimiento puede ser obtenido por medios electrónicos, siempre que el mismo sea gratuito e inequívoco. Hacer clic en los botones “proceder”, “aceptar” o “continuar” en la pantalla será suficiente para entender que el consentimiento ha sido otorgado de manera inequívoca, siempre que también esté el botón “cancelar”.\n\nLos Usuarios que faciliten sus datos personales, consienten inequívocamente la incorporación de los mismos en una base de datos de la que será responsable NESTLÉ, o una persona natural o jurídica designada por NESTLÉ, así como del procesamiento o no de los datos personales. Esta información será tratada con sumo cuidado y con la mayor seguridad posible y sólo se utilizará de acuerdo a los límites establecidos en este documento.\n\nLos datos personales deberán ser veraces. NESTLÉ sólo reúne datos personales cuando estos son proporcionados directamente por los Usuarios del Sitio.\n\nEn el caso de que los datos recogidos se utilizasen para una finalidad distinta para la cual hubiesen sido recabados o recogidos se requerirá el consentimiento previo de los interesados.\n\nNESTLÉ utiliza los datos personales proporcionados por sus Usuarios para los fines directos por los cuales se entregan y para difundir ofertas de productos o de servicios, para informar novedades de\n\nproductos o servicios que podrían ser de utilidad e interés y para personalizar y mejorar la relación con sus clientes.\n\nAl entregar sus datos personales, el Usuario autoriza automáticamente a NESTLÉ a utilizarlos de acuerdo a las políticas establecidas en este documento, con la seguridad y privacidad requeridas. Cada vez que el Usuario ingresa sus datos personales, deberá aceptar o rechazar el uso en futuras comunicaciones. Al completar cualquier formulario si no está de acuerdo con esto, el Usuario deberá desactivar la opción respectiva. Si elige mantenerla activada, se entiende que el Usuario autoriza a NESTLÉ al uso de los datos personales para los fines y con los propósitos expuestos.\n\nLos datos sensibles no serán procesados por NESTLÉ excepto si el titular de los mismos da su consentimiento expreso para ello, y cuando (i) sean requeridos conforme a la ley aplicable, en particular para dar cumplimiento con normas de carácter laboral; (ii) cuando dicho procesamiento de datos sensibles sea necesario para proteger intereses vitales del titular de los mismos o de otra persona; (iii) cuando el procesamiento se refiera a datos personales sean revelados públicamente por su titular; o (iv) cuando el procesamiento sea necesario para el establecimiento, ejercicio o defensa de demandas legales. Este consentimiento explícito respecto de datos sensibles significa en la práctica la obtención de la firma del titular de estos datos, antes de su procesamiento.\n\nNESTLÉ ha adoptado las medidas técnicas y organizativas necesarias para garantizar la seguridad e integridad de los datos personales, así como para evitar su alteración, pérdida accidental, destrucción, tratamiento o acceso no autorizado. Las medidas adoptadas por NESTLÉ serán proporcionales a los riesgos involucrados en el procesamiento de los datos personales. No obstante, en la actualidad ningún sistema es completamente seguro o libre de ataques.\n\nLos Usuarios cuyos datos personales sean objeto de tratamiento podrán ejercer gratuitamente los siguientes derechos:\n\n1.- Derecho de acceso: Incluye el derecho a obtener confirmación respecto a si sus datos personales están siendo procesados e información relativa a la naturaleza del procesamiento; el derecho a ser informado del detalle de los datos personales que están siendo procesados y de cualquier información disponible respecto de su fuente; y el derecho a ser informado respecto del “conocimiento de la lógica” involucrado en el procesamiento.\n\n2.- Derecho de rectificación, eliminación y bloqueo: El titular de los datos personales tiene derecho a rectificar, eliminar o bloquear los datos personales, cuyo procesamiento no cumpla con la ley aplicable y/o con las Políticas de Protección de Datos Personales de NESTLÉ, sus estándares y pautas. El controlador de datos notificará a terceros a quienes se le hayan revelado los datos personales de cualquier solicitud de rectificación, eliminación o bloqueo de los mismos por parte de su titular, a menos de que esto sea imposible o implique un esfuerzo desproporcionado.\n\n3.- Derecho de objeción: Este derecho incluye el derecho del titular de los datos personales a objetar el procesamiento de los mismos basado en fundamentos legítimos o si es ara marketing directo; el derecho a estar informado antes de que sus datos personales sean revelados a cualquier tercero, o usados en su nombre para propósitos de marketing directo; y el derecho a que expresamente se le ofrezca la oportunidad de objetar, de manera gratuita, dichas revelaciones o uso de datos personales.\n\nTodos estos derechos, más los que concede la Ley N° 19.628, se conceden sin efectos retroactivos en los términos especificados en dicha ley, conforme al procedimiento legalmente establecido. Estos derechos podrán ser ejercitados dirigiendo comunicación vía e-mail a NESTLÉ a la casilla de correo electrónico magdalena.neira@cl.nestle.com, o mediante carta enviada a Servicios al Consumidor Nestlé, (Av. Las Condes N° 11.287, Las Condes, Santiago), o a través de nuestro propio Sitio a través del envío de la solicitud que se encuentra en el menú Contáctanos, dirigiendo su solicitud al destinatario Webmaster.\n\nEn el momento de proceder a la recogida de los datos personales, se indicará el carácter voluntario u obligatorio de los datos personales objeto de recogida.\n\nEl acceso a este Sitio puede implicar la utilización de cookies. Las cookies son pequeñas cantidades de información que se almacenan en el navegador utilizado por cada Usuario para que el servidor recuerde cierta información que posteriormente únicamente el servidor que la implementó leerá. Las cookies tienen, generalmente, una duración limitada en el tiempo. Ninguna cookie de este Sitio permite que pueda contactarse con el número de teléfono del Usuario, su dirección de correo electrónico o con cualesquiera otro medio de contacto. Ninguna cookie de este Sitio puede extraer información del disco duro del Usuario o robar información personal. La única manera, en este Sitio, de que la información privada de un Usuario forme parte del archivo cookie es que el Usuario dé personalmente esa información al servidor. Aquellos Usuarios que no deseen recibir cookies o quieran ser informados de su fijación pueden configurar su navegador a tal efecto.\n\n[Back](javascript: modal.close();)\n\n## iRegístrate para obtener la mejor experiencia!\n\nTe enviaremos un recetario especial a tu correo, además\npodrás acceder a clases exclusivas en línea, promociones\ny muchas sorpresas más\n\n[Regístrate](/perfilador)\n\n  [Back](javascript: modal.close();) \n\n![{{ 'Recetas Nestlé'|t }}](/themes/custom/cookit/Content/img/svgs/v5-logo.svg)\n\n## \n\nPara una mejor experiencia, haga clic en los 3 puntos de lado superior derecho y luego abra en el navegador predeterminado\n\n  [Back](javascript: modal.close();)\n\n![Recetas Nestlé](/themes/custom/cookit/Content/img/svgs/v5-logo.svg)\n\n## ¡Disfruta de una experiencia completa!\n\nCrea recetarios, guarda recetas, accede a cursos, planifica tus comidas y mucho más\n\n[Regístrate](/perfilador?destination=/terminos-y-condiciones)[Inicia sessión](/login?destination=/terminos-y-condiciones)\n\n![Modal Image](/themes/custom/cookit/Content/img/img-modal-login.webp)\n\n \n\n[Back](javascript: modal.close();)\n\nCargando... ¡Espera!\n\n\n---\n\n[Pasar al contenido principal](#main-content)\n\nVolver\n\n## Regístrate y disfruta de los benefícios de Recetas Nestlé:\n\n* Guarda tus recetas\n* Planear tú menú\n\nVolver\n\n* [Aviso de privacidad](/aviso-de-privacidad \""Link Aviso de privacidad\"")\n* [Términos y condiciones](/terminos-y-condiciones \""Link Términos y condiciones\"")\n* Configuración de cookies\n\n[Back](javascript: modal.close();)\n\n## iRegístrate para obtener la mejor experiencia!\n\nTe enviaremos un recetario especial a tu correo, además\npodrás acceder a clases exclusivas en línea, promociones\ny muchas sorpresas más\n\n[Regístrate](/perfilador)\n\n  [Back](javascript: modal.close();) \n\n![{{ 'Recetas Nestlé'|t }}](/themes/custom/cookit/Content/img/svgs/v5-logo.svg)\n\n## \n\nPara una mejor experiencia, haga clic en los 3 puntos de lado superior derecho y luego abra en el navegador predeterminado\n\n  [Back](javascript: modal.close();)\n\n![Recetas Nestlé](/themes/custom/cookit/Content/img/svgs/v5-logo.svg)\n\n## ¡Disfruta de una experiencia completa!\n\nCrea recetarios, guarda recetas, accede a cursos, planifica tus comidas y mucho más\n\n[Regístrate](/perfilador?destination=/perfilador)[Inicia sessión](/login?destination=/perfilador)\n\n![Modal Image](/themes/custom/cookit/Content/img/img-modal-login.webp)\n\n \n\n[Back](javascript: modal.close();)\n\nCargando... ¡Espera!\n\n\n---\n\n[Pasar al contenido principal](#main-content)\n\nVolver\n\n## Regístrate y disfruta de los benefícios de Recetas Nestlé:\n\n* Guarda tus recetas\n* Planear tú menú\n\nVolver\n\n* [Aviso de privacidad](/aviso-de-privacidad \""Link Aviso de privacidad\"")\n* [Términos y condiciones](/terminos-y-condiciones \""Link Términos y condiciones\"")\n* Configuración de cookies\n\n[Back](javascript: modal.close();)\n\n## iRegístrate para obtener la mejor experiencia!\n\nTe enviaremos un recetario especial a tu correo, además\npodrás acceder a clases exclusivas en línea, promociones\ny muchas sorpresas más\n\n[Regístrate](/perfilador)\n\n  [Back](javascript: modal.close();) \n\n![{{ 'Recetas Nestlé'|t }}](/themes/custom/cookit/Content/img/svgs/v5-logo.svg)\n\n## \n\nPara una mejor experiencia, haga clic en los 3 puntos de lado superior derecho y luego abra en el navegador predeterminado\n\n  [Back](javascript: modal.close();)\n\n![Recetas Nestlé](/themes/custom/cookit/Content/img/svgs/v5-logo.svg)\n\n## ¡Disfruta de una experiencia completa!\n\nCrea recetarios, guarda recetas, accede a cursos, planifica tus comidas y mucho más\n\n[Regístrate](/perfilador?destination=/login)[Inicia sessión](/login?destination=/login)\n\n![Modal Image](/themes/custom/cookit/Content/img/img-modal-login.webp)\n\n \n\n[Back](javascript: modal.close();)\n\nCargando... ¡Espera!"", ""veredicto"": ""DEPENDE"", ""justificacion"": ""El texto es un aviso de privacidad, no una licencia de uso del contenido; permite el uso del sitio y aplicaciones bajo condiciones de privacidad, pero no autoriza explícitamente la reproducción, distribución o reutilización del contenido del sitio, lo cual dependerá de términos no incluidos aquí.""}]",2,"El texto es un aviso de privacidad que regula el tratamiento de datos personales, no los derechos de uso del contenido del sitio; no autoriza ni prohíbe explícitamente la reproducción del texto, por lo que su usabilidad es incierta y depende de términos externos no mencionados."
https://www.idbinvest.org/en/news-media/news-archive,Términos y condiciones (sin licencia explícita),SI,"El texto permite el descarga, copia y reimpresión de la información para fines no comerciales, siempre que se cite a IDB Invest como fuente, lo que autoriza el uso con atribución en contextos no comerciales.","[{""categoria"": null, ""via"": ""footer"", ""url_origen"": ""https://www.idbinvest.org/en/news-media/news-archive"", ""markdown_path"": null, ""texto_inline"": ""[Skip to main content](#main-content)\n\n\nWelcome to IDB Invest web site (the “Web Site”). Please take a few minutes to review these Terms of Use (\""Terms\""). The Terms govern your use of this Web Site, applications and/or social media tools provided to you by IDB Invest. Therefore, by using this Web Site you agree to the Terms and any modifications thereto made by IDB Invest from time-to-time and posted on this Web Site. The use of the Web Site is governed by the Terms as set forth below.\n\nUse of our applications (\""Apps\"") are governed by the terms you accepted at the time you purchased or downloaded it, these Terms and the terms of your mobile service provider and mobile device operator. Our social media pages, which include but are not limited to Facebook, Twitter and LinkedIn (collectively \""Social Media\""), are delivered to you in accordance with these Terms and the terms of use of each of the Social Media operators.\n\nBy accessing and using this Website, the Apps and/or the Social Media you certify that you are of legal age to form a legally binding contract, and you further agree to such terms and conditions, as they may be modified by IDB Invest from time-to-time and posted on this Web Site.\n\n**Use**: IDB Invest maintains this Web Site, its Apps and Social Media primarily for information purposes. Users may download, copy and reprint information from the Web Site for the purpose of interacting with IDB Invest and for other non-commercial purposes, subject to any terms and conditions contained within materials expressly attributed to third parties, so long as IDB Invest is cited as the source of the originating material.\n\nUsers may not place \""frames\"" around or mirror material from the Web Site without the express written authorization of IDB Invest. Users may not reproduce, modify, copy, sell, create derivative works from, distribute, or publicly display any content from, or exploit for any commercial purposes, any material, information, content, code or data on or available through  the Web Site, its Apps and/or Social Media.\n\nThe contents of materials expressly attributed to third parties are the property and responsibility of such third parties and not of IDB Invest. Use of such information is subject to the legal terms and conditions set forth by the relevant third parties. Trade names, marks, logos and domains contained on the Web Site, Apps and/or Social Media are the intellectual property of their respective owners and are protected by intellectual property laws.\n\n**License**: IDB Invest grants you a limited, non-transferable, revocable license to access the Website and view the content on the Apps and Social Media on your personal computer or mobile device for your personal use only. Access to the Web Site, Apps and Social Media is licensed, not sold, to you, for use only under these Terms, the terms of your mobile service provider and mobile device operator, and the terms of use of each of the Social Media operators, as applicable. IDB Invest may revoke your license to access and/or use the Website, Apps and Social Media, at any time and for any reason without advance notice to you.\n\n**Links to/from Third Party Sites**: This Web Site, Apps and/or Social Media contain links to third-party web sites not under the control of IDB Invest. IDB Invest provides these links as a convenience for users of the Web Site, Apps and/or Social Media; IDB Invest is not responsible for their contents. The presence of a link does not imply endorsement or approval of its contents by IDB Invest. Likewise, no Third Party may link or deep link to any part of this Web Site, Apps and/or Social Media without IDB Invest’s prior written consent.\n\n**Use of Communications Facilities**: This Web Site, Apps and/or Social Media may contain bulletin boards, chat rooms, access to mailing lists or other message or communication facilities. You agree to use the communication facilities only to send and receive information and materials that is proper and relevant to the communication facility.\n\nWhen using the communication facilities you will not: defame, abuse, harass, threaten or otherwise violate the legal rights of others; publish, post or distribute any defamatory, infringing, obscene, indecent or unlawful material; upload or attach files that contain copyrighted material unless you own or control such copyright; upload or attach files that contain viruses or similar software; delete any author attributions or legal/proprietary notices in any file that is uploaded; advertise or offer goods or services, or conduct surveys, contests or chain letters; or download any file posted that you know, or reasonably should know, cannot be legally distributed in such manner.\n\nAny contribution you post to the Web Site, Apps and/or Social Media will be considered non-confidential and non-proprietary. By providing any contribution on the Web Site, Apps and/or Social Media, you grant IDB Invest, the Inter-American Development Bank Group members and IDB Invest’s service providers, and each of their, and our respective licensees, successors and assigns the right to use, reproduce, modify, perform, display, distribute and otherwise disclose to third parties any such material.\n\n**Personal Information and Cookies**: IDB Invest does not automatically collect personal information regarding your use of the Web Site, Apps and/or Social Media. However, if you submit any information through an interface of the Web Site, an App and/or Social Media including while registering for an event or inquiring about financing for your enterprise, or if you use a communications facility of the Web Site, App and/or Social Media you may be asked for personal information such as your name, place of employment and email address, or information related to your business such as number of employees, annual sales information, etc. Any reliance you place on such information is strictly at your own risk.\n\nWe disclaim all liability and responsibility arising from any reliance placed on such materials by you or any other visitor to the Web Site, Apps and/or Social Media, or by anyone who may be informed of any of its contents.  \nInformation provided by you through the Web Site, Apps and/or Social Media may be used by the Inter-American Investment Corporation (IDB Invest) and shared with the Inter-American Development Bank and other strategic partners of IDB Invest to determine eligibility for financial and nonfinancial products. Furthermore, by using this Web Site, you accept that the information you provide to IDB Invest through the Web Site will be treated in accordance with[IDB Invest's Disclosure of Information Policy](https://idbinvest.org/en/access-information-policy).\n\nThe Web Site, Apps and/or Social Media may set a cookie that enables the Web Site to remember you the next time you visit, so that you don’t have to re-enter information that you already typed in. Likewise, IDB Invest, through this Web Site, Apps and/or Social Media may collect and use technical data and related information, including but not limited to technical information about your mobile device, system and application software in order to provide support and services to you.  \nIn addition, the Web Site may record your IP address and information such as your browser type and operating system. This information helps IDB Invest learn about the geographical distribution of Web Site visitors. This information is never connected with the personal information you supply to IDB Invest through the Web Site or otherwise.\n\n**Disclaimer**: All information on the Web Site, the Apps and/or Social Media are provided \""AS IS\"", with no express or implied warranty of any kind, including but not limited to any warranty of merchantability, suitability, availability, non-infringement or fitness for any particular purpose. Use of this Web Site, Apps and/or Social Media is at user's sole risk. IDB Invest makes no warranty as to the accuracy, completeness, reliability or timeliness of any of the material or information on the Web Site, Apps and/or Social Media and under no circumstances, including but not limited to, negligence, shall IDB Invest be liable for any direct, indirect, incidental, special or consequential expenses or damages incurred by reason of its use, including expenses or damages arising from communication failure and/or computer malfunctions associated with use of the Web Site.\n\nInformation that relates to a particular date is offered only as of such date and IDB Invest undertakes no obligation to update any material on the Web Site, Apps and/or Social Media. IDB Invest may, in its discretion, periodically add, change, improve or update the materials on the Web Site, Apps and/or Social Media without notice, and reserves the right to limit or discontinue the Web Site, Apps and/or Social Media or deny any user access thereto without notice.\n\nAs a condition of use of the Web Site, Apps and/or Social Media, you agree to indemnify IDB Invest from and against any and all actions, claims, losses, damages, liabilities and expenses (including reasonable attorneys' fees) arising out of your use of the Web Site, Apps and/or Social Media, including without limitation any claims alleging facts that if true would constitute a breach by you of these terms and conditions.\n\nIf the user is dissatisfied with any material on the Web Site, Apps and/or Social Media or with any of terms and conditions of use of the Web Site, Apps and/or Social Media, such user's sole and exclusive remedy is to discontinue using the Web Site, Apps and/or Social Media.\n\nNothing in the Web Site, Apps and/or Social Media or any materials therein shall be construed, explicitly or implicitly, to contain any Investment recommendations. IDB Invest is not registered under the U.S. Investment Advisers Act of 1940. Accordingly, nothing in this Web Site, Apps and/or Social Media or in any materials therein constitutes an offer of or an invitation by or on behalf of IDB Invest to purchase or sell any securities, nor should it be considered Investment advice.  \nThe Web Site, Apps and Social Media are controlled, operated and administered by IDB Invest from its offices within the United States of America. IDB Invest makes no representation that materials at the Web Site, Apps and Social Media are appropriate or available for use at other locations outside of the United States of America.\n\nAccess to the materials on the Web Site, Apps and/or Social Media at any location where such content may be illegal is prohibited. If you access the Web Site, Apps and/or Social Media from a location outside of the United States of America, you are solely responsible for compliance with local laws.\n\nThe opinions and findings of authors or compilers contained herein are not necessarily those of IDB Invest or its member countries. Except as otherwise noted, the material on the Web Site, Apps and/or Social Media are the property of IDB Invest and is subject to the copyright, trademark and other intellectual property laws of the United States of America and other jurisdictions. All uses of the Web Site, Apps and/or Social Media are subject to these laws.\n\n**Export Regulation**:   The App may be subject to US export control laws, including the US Export Administration Act and its associated regulations. You shall not, directly or indirectly, export, re-export or release the App to, or make the App accessible from, any jurisdiction or country to which export, re-export or release is prohibited by law, rule or regulation.\n\nYou shall comply with all applicable federal laws, regulations and rules, and complete all required undertakings (including obtaining any necessary export license or other governmental approval), prior to exporting, re-exporting, releasing or otherwise making the App available outside the US. Nothing in this statement shall constitute or be considered to be a limitation upon or a waiver of the privileges and immunities of IDB Invest, which are specifically reserved.\n\n**Applicable Law**: These Terms will be governed, interpreted and enforced in accordance with the laws of the District of Columbia, United States of America, without giving effect to the conflict of laws provisions of that jurisdiction. Any legal action over the contents of the Web Site, Apps and Social Media shall be brought in the federal courts located in Washington, D.C.\n\nNo waiver by IDB Invest of any provision of these terms and conditions shall be binding except as set forth in writing signed by its duly authorized representative. Nothing in the Web Site, Apps and/or Social Media shall constitute or be considered to be a limitation upon or a waiver of the privileges and immunities of IDB Invest, which are specifically reserved.\n\n\n---\n\n[Skip to main content](#main-content)\n\n\n*Last updated on: March 18, 2026*\n\n###### **Overview**\n\nThe Inter-American Investment Corporation (“IDB Invest”, “we”, “us” and “our”) is an international organization founded by international treaty in 1986 and is a member of the Inter-American Development Bank Group (“IDB Group”). As such, it is not subject to any national or supranational laws.\n\nThis Privacy Notice (“Privacy Notice”) explains how IDB Invest collects, uses, stores, transfers or otherwise processes the Personal Data of individuals (other than our own personnel and their dependents) (“you”). For the purposes of this Privacy Notice, Personal Data means any information relating to an identified or identifiable individual, such as a person’s name, contact details, location data, or factors relating to their physical, economic, cultural or social identity, or any other information that may reasonably be linked to that individual.\n\nIf you are either (i) the direct or indirect beneficiary of IDB Invest [Products and Services](https://idbinvest.org/en/solutions), or (ii) a representative of, or otherwise associated with, businesses and other organizations currently or potentially benefiting from or participating in IDB Invest’s [Products or Services](https://idbinvest.org/en/solutions) (for example, employees, officers, shareholders, directors, beneficial owners, guarantors or key vendors or partners of such businesses or organizations), this Privacy Notice applies to the processing of your Personal Data.\n\nPersonal data is processed by IDB Invest in accordance with the [IDB Group Personal Data Privacy Policy](https://idbinvest.org/sites/default/files/2022-11/IDB%20Group%20Personal%20Data%20Privacy%20Policy.pdf) (the “Privacy Policy”). Such processing enables IDB Invest to carry out its mission, mandate and purpose as an international organization established by its member countries.\n\nPlease ensure that you read this Privacy Notice in its entirety, as amended from time to time.\n\n---\n\n###### **What Does this Privacy Notice Cover?**\n\nThis Privacy Notice relates to the Personal Data we collect and process from you, and covers the following aspects:\n\n(Click on the topic you want to read)\n\n* [The contexts in which we process your Personal Data;](#1)\n* [The types of Personal Data that we process about you;](#2)\n* [The sources from which IDB Invest obtain your Personal Data;](#3)\n* [How and why IDB Invest processes your Personal Data;](#4)\n* [How long we keep your Personal Data;](#5)\n* [How, why and to whom we transfer your Personal Data;](#6)\n* [How we protect your Personal Data;](#7)\n* [Changes to this Privacy Notice;](#8)\n* [Explains the application of our privileges and immunities;](#9) and\n* [Explains how you may contact us with queries or complaints.](#10)\n\n---\n\n###### **The Contexts in Which we Process your Personal Data**\n\nThe Personal Data processing activities we undertake will vary based on your relationship with IDB Invest.\n\n**I. Visitors to IDB Invest’s websites**\n\nIDB Invest does not automatically process Personal Data related to the visitors of its website, e.g. idbinvest.org, or official IDB Invest pages on other platforms. However, we will process Personal Data that you submit through any interface of the official websites (for example, when registering for an event). This Privacy Notice does not apply to third party websites. We encourage you to review the privacy notices of any third-party websites you visit.\n\n**II. Subscribers of IDB Invest newsletters or publications**\n\nIf you subscribe to an IDB Invest newsletter or publication, we process your Personal Data (for example, your name and e-mail address) so we can make sure that you receive it.\n\n**III. Registered attendees of IDB Invest events**\n\nIf you register to attend an IDB Invest event, we collect and process your Personal Data in connection with the organization and management of the event.\n\n**IV. Personal Data processed in the course of providing our Products and Services**\n\nIn the course of providing our Products and Services IDB Invest processes Personal Data.\n\n**V. Personal Data in the context of recruitment**\n\nPersonal Data is required to manage job applications and recruitment processes. For detailed information, please refer to the privacy notice provided to job applicants during the application process ([available here](https://www.iadb.org/en/terms-conditions-and-notices/privacy-notice/job-applicant-privacy-notice)).\n\n**VI. Personal Data in the context of procurement**\n\nIn the course of providing our procurement activities, IDB Invest processes Personal Data.\n\n**VII. Business planning, client strategy, communications and analytics activities**\n\nIf you engage with IDB Invest as a business contact, prospective client, or external stakeholder (for example, through meetings, conferences, or professional networking), we may process your Personal Data for business development, client engagement, and institutional communications purposes.\n\n---\n\n###### **What Personal Data do we Process?**\n\nWe may collect and process the following Personal Data about you:\n\n* **Identification and contact data –** name, postal address(es), email address, phone number(s), signature specimen, passport/nationality identity documents (including embedded photographs), age and date of birth, citizenship status, office location, and limited biometric identifiers used for identity verification or security purposes;\n* **Operations data –** information about your involvement in, and/or the development impact on you of, our investment and advisory operations and activities;\n* **Financial data –** relevant financial information of how you benefit directly or indirectly from our Products and Services;\n* **Background data –** relevant background information used for anti-corruption and anti-fraud assessments in accordance with our applicable policies and procedures;\n* **Professional data –** job title, employer details or organizational affiliation, photograph in your CV, professional history, qualification details, information about your experience, participation in meetings, seminars, and conferences, information about your professional relationship with other individuals or institutions, language abilities, and other professional skills;\n* **Correspondence –** records of any correspondence we may have with you, records of your correspondence preferences (including subscription to our newsletters);\n* **Consent records –** records of preferences and permissions you provide to us, including records of consent opt-in/opt-out choices, where applicable. When maintained, such records are used solely to demonstrate compliance with applicable legal, contractual or governance obligations and to respect your stated preferences;\n* **Data relating to our websites –** technical data (device type, operating system, browser type and settings, IP address, language settings), usage and behavioral data, connection information (dates, times, location), analytics, and aggregate statistical information.\n* **Diversity and inclusion data –** salutations, gender identity, race / ethnicity, disability status;\n\nIn limited circumstances, IDB Invest may process special categories of Personal Data, such as information relating to an individual’s health, racial or ethnic origin, or other similarly sensitive characteristics. Such data will be processed only where strictly necessary and in accordance with applicable institutional policies and will be subject to enhanced safeguards designed to ensure an appropriate level of protection for the confidentiality, integrity, and security of the Personal Data.\n\n---\n\n###### **Where we Obtain your Personal Data?**\n\nWe may obtain or receive Personal Data about you from the following sources:\n\n* **Personal Data you or your employer provide to us –** Personal Data provided directly by you (e.g., job applications, correspondence you send us, information you provide to our investment officers, or when you complete an online form or survey), or that is provided to us by your employer or other organization with which you are associated, and information collected during meetings, events, and business interactions.\n* **Personal Data we collect by automated means –** As noted above, we may obtain certain information by automated means when you visit our websites.\n* **Personal Data we collect from third parties –** We may collect or obtain Personal Data from third parties (e.g., counterparties to a transaction, law enforcement authorities, relevant business contacts, specialized databases operated by the private sector, specialized external service providers, consultants or vendors).\n* **Personal Data you make public –** We may collect or obtain Personal Data that you manifestly choose to make public, including via social media (e.g., we may collect information from your social media profile(s), if you make a public post about us).\n\n---\n\n###### **Why we Process your Personal Data?**\n\nIDB Invest processes your Personal Data as reasonably necessary to conduct and manage our activities within the contexts listed above. This includes processing Personal Data for any of the following purposes:\n\n**I. To carry out IDB Invest’s investment, advisory and asset management activities**\n\n* Exploring investment opportunities and conducting due diligence;\n* Executing legal instruments related to investment, advisory and asset management activities;\n* Administering and managing our relationships with counterparties (and potential counterparties) in the context of our investment, advisory and asset management activities (or potential activities that may be of interest);\n* Understanding and monitoring the development impact of our activities;\n* Investigating and responding to complaints, and establishing, exercising, or defending IDB Invest’s legal rights and obligations;\n* Coordinating with other IDB Group Institutions; and,\n* Supporting equality, diversity and inclusion in our projects.\n\n**II. To comply with legal and policy obligations and manage risk**\n\n* Performing internal governance functions;\n* Conducting accounting and financial management;\n* Maintaining appropriate accounting, financial management and other records;\n* Fulfill our policy obligations, confirming and verifying your identity, and screening against government and/or law enforcement agency sanctions lists and other legal restrictions;\n* Carrying out our obligations, and exercising our rights, under applicable legal or regulatory requirements and any contracts entered into between you and IDB Invest;\n* Conducting credit and other risk assessment and control activities, including for the prevention and detection of corruption and fraud; and,\n* Training our staff and maintaining and improving the quality of our internal processes and arrangements.\n\n**III. To manage communications, stakeholder engagement and business development**\n\n* Disseminating information to further IDB Invest’s mission to improve lives in Latin America and the Caribbean, and providing research information;\n* Responding to your queries and feedback (for example, if you have asked a question or submitted feedback through our website);\n* Providing you with information, products or services you have requested or that may be of interest to you, unless you tell us otherwise; and,\n* Conducting business intelligence operations; and conducting business planning and client strategy activities, including organizing and managing events for clients and potential clients; conducting business analysis, planning and monitoring; preparing and disseminating marketing, institutional and business communications; defining communications strategies, guidelines and mechanisms; developing and communicating plans, strategies, strategic initiatives and updates to internal and external stakeholders; understanding client behavior through analytics to design and enhance client experiences; conducting impact evaluations and other in-depth studies (which may include surveys with project beneficiaries and other stakeholders); and supporting business development and client engagement initiatives.\n\n**IV. In connection with the management of IDB Invest’s websites, data analytics and IT security**\n\n* Providing access, maintaining and improving our websites and services;\n* Enabling you to participate in any interactive features of our websites and communicating with you, including through our newsletter, subject to your preferences;\n* Presenting website content in a manner suitable for the device you are accessing it from Undertaking data analytics to understand how users interact with our websites and online public-facing materials;\n* Monitoring and analyzing the use of our products and services for purposes of developing and improving them;\n* Managing and ensuring the security of our IT systems, including detecting and preventing misuse or abuse of our websites and services, and for backup and disaster recovery purposes; and,\n* We may also process Personal Data for any other purpose described to you at the time your data is collected.\n\nWe may also collect and process Personal Data of visitors to our premises, including for the purposes of ensuring safety and security at those premises, as further detailed in the notices available at our premises.\n\n---\n\n###### **How Long we Keep your Personal Data**\n\nYour Personal Data will be kept only as long as necessary for the purposes set out in this Privacy Notice and in accordance with IDB Invest’s applicable records retention and disposition schedules. The specific length of time will depend on the type of Personal Data, the reasons for which it is processed, and other obligations under IDB Invest’s policies and procedures.\n\n---\n\n###### **International Transfers of Personal Data**\n\nWhen you submit Personal Data to us by any means, that Personal Data may be transferred to a jurisdiction other than the one in which you live. In particular, Personal Data may be transferred to the United States. The data protection and other privacy laws of the United States may not afford the same level of protection as the laws of other countries.\n\n---\n\n###### **To whom we Disclose your Personal Data?**\n\nIDB Invest may disclose your Personal Data to the recipients described below, as reasonably necessary for the purposes outlined in this Privacy Notice.\n\n* IDB Group Institutions: We may disclose your Personal Data to other IDB Group institutions, such as the Inter-American Development Bank, as necessary for the purposes set out in this Privacy Notice.\n* Third parties: Unless otherwise noted below, and subject to contractually agreed conditions of confidentiality and security (where applicable), we may disclose your Personal Data to the categories of parties listed below:\n  + Service providers and suppliers who perform services, such as event vendors and organizers, consulting firms, among others, and providers that support compliance processes, including KYC screening and due diligence processes.\n  + Legal and other advisors that assist, advise or represent an IDB Group Institution as needed, such as attorneys, in connection with litigation, investigations, advising on contractual obligations, or enabling an IDB Group Institution to carry out its development mandate.\n  + Relevant legal, regulatory or administrative authorities, as we believe to be appropriate, for example, public registers involved in the execution and enforcement of relevant transaction documents, and other relevant authorities to protect and defend our rights and property, protect the interests of the IDB Group or others; or enable us to pursue available remedies or limit the damages that we may sustain; and,\n  + Other selected third parties: legal entities, including financial institutions, custodians, brokers, private companies, intermediaries, donors, partners and other organizations with which you are associated or involved (if any) in connection with our Products or Services; and peer researchers from academia, who carry out impact evaluations, among others.\n\nIDB Invest seeks to ensure that all partners and service providers processing Personal Data on its behalf implement appropriate technical and organizational safeguards to protect the privacy and security of such data.\n\n---\n\n###### **How to Request Information on your Personal Data Processed by IDB Invest**\n\nAs part of its data privacy framework, IDB Invest has established a procedure for individuals to request information regarding their Personal Data processed by IDB Invest and, when appropriate, to seek redress if they reasonably believe their Personal Data has not been processed in accordance with the IDB Group Personal Data Privacy Policy.\n\nYou may submit such a request using the webform [available here](https://forms.office.com/r/QAvQqSEBdy).\n\n---\n\n###### **How we Protect your Personal Data**\n\nWe have appropriate technical (e.g., firewalls, malware scans, anti-virus protection, encryption, physical locks) and organizational (e.g., policies and procedures, privacy assessments, due diligence, awareness, and training) safeguards in place to prevent unauthorized processing and accidental loss, damage, or destruction of Personal Data. These safeguards take into account the sensitivity of the data, as well as the current state of technology. We also have procedures in place to deal with data breaches, and we will notify you accordingly when appropriate.\n\n---\n\n###### **Changes to this Privacy Notice**\n\nThis Privacy Notice was last updated on the date listed above. If we change it, we will post the new version to this website.\n\n---\n\n###### **Queries and Complaints**\n\nIf you have any complaints or queries regarding your Personal Data, please contact [[email protected]](/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection#b0c0c2d9c6d1d3c9f0f9f4f2d9dec6d5c3c49edfc2d7).\n\n---\n\n###### **Privileges and Immunities**\n\nNothing contained in this Privacy Notice shall constitute or be considered to be a limitation upon or a waiver of the privileges and immunities of IDB Invest, which are specifically reserved.\n\n\n---\n\n# **<u>IDB GROUP PERSONAL DATA PRIVACY POLICY</u>**<sup>**1**</sup> \n\n# **I. PURPOSE AND APPLICATION** \n\nThis document sets out the Policy for the Processing of Personal Data by IDB Group Institutions. \n\nThis Policy applies to the Processing of Personal Data by, or on behalf of, IDB Group Institutions, and is intended to develop consistent practices across the IDB Group. \n\n# **II. DEFINITIONS** \n\nCapitalized terms or acronyms used in this Policy have the meaning set out below: \n\n**_1._ Board(s)** : the Boards of Executive Directors of IDB and IDB Invest, respectively. \n\n**_2._ Data Subject** : a natural, living person to whom Personal Data pertains, and whose Personal Data is Processed by an IDB Group Institution. Data Subjects may include, without limitation, any current or former: (i) IDB Group Institution staff member, director or their dependents; (ii) IDB Group Institution contractor or consultant; (iii) applicant for a vacancy at an IDB Group Institution; (iv) IDB Group Institution suppliers or vendors; (v) IDB Group Institution client or their representatives; (vi) respondents to IDB Group Institution surveys; or (vii) subscribers to an IDB Group Institution website. \n\n**_3._ IDB** : the Inter-American Development Bank. \n\n**_4._ IDB Group** : the Inter-American Development Bank Group. \n\n**_5._ IDB Group Institution** : any one of the IDB<sup>2</sup> and IDB Invest. \n\n**_6._ IDB Invest** : the Inter-American Investment Corporation. \n\n**_7._ Implementing Instruments** : has the meaning set forth in Section IV below. \n\n**_8._ Personal Data** : any information relating to an identified or identifiable Data Subject. An identifiable Data Subject is one who can be identified by reasonable means, directly or indirectly, by reference to an attribute or combination of attributes within the data, or combination of the data with other available information. Examples of attributes that can be used to identify an identifiable Data Subject include their name, identification number, location data, online identifier, metadata, and factors specific to their physical, physiological, genetic, mental, economic, cultural or social identity. \n\n**_9._ Policy** : this Personal Data Privacy Policy. \n\n**_10._ Principles** : the principles set out in Section III below. \n\n> 1 This Policy is not effective yet pursuant to Section IV below. \n\n> 2 The Multilateral Investment Fund (commercially known as IDB Lab) is a fund administered by the IDB and, therefore, any references to IDB Group Institution include IDB Lab.\n\n**_11._ Processing** : any action or set of actions, automated or not, which is performed on Personal Data, which may include, without limitation, its collection, recording, use, consultation, retrieval, disclosure by transmission, dissemination or otherwise making available, forwarding, organization, storage, structuring, adaptation or alteration, alignment or combination, restriction, erasure or destruction. \n\n**_12._ Processed** : having undertaken the act of Processing. \n\n**_13._ Third Party** or **Third Parties** : a legal person, other than IDB Group Institutions, or a natural person, other than IDB Group Institutions’ personnel and their dependents, as defined within their respective policies and procedures. \n\n# **III. PRINCIPLES** \n\nThe following Principles shall apply to all Processing of Personal Data by IDB Group Institutions: \n\n# **_1. Legitimate, Fair and Transparent Processing_** \n\nPersonal Data shall only be Processed for legitimate purposes and in a fair and transparent manner. Legitimate purposes for Processing mean any purpose: \n\n- a. for which the consent of a Data Subject is obtained, either at the time Personal Data are collected or subsequently; \n\n- b. that is in the vital or best interest of (i) the Data Subject or (ii) another person; \n\n- c. that is reasonably necessary for the performance of a contract; \n\n- d. that is reasonably necessary to enable an IDB Group Institution to satisfy an obligation or undertaking, or to comply with an IDB Group Institution’s policy or procedure; \n\n- e. that is reasonably necessary to establish, exercise or defend an IDB Group Institution’s right or interest; or \n\n- f. that is consistent with, or reasonably necessary to enable an IDB Group Institution to carry out its mission, mandate or purpose as an international organization established by its member countries. \n\n# **_2. Purpose Limitation_** \n\nPersonal Data shall be collected for one or more specific and legitimate purpose(s) listed in Principle 1 above and not further Processed in a manner that is incompatible with such purpose(s). Further Processing for archiving purposes, research, or statistical purposes shall not be considered incompatible with such purpose(s).\n\n# **_3. Data Minimization_** \n\nThe amount and type of Personal Data collected shall be reasonably necessary for, and proportionate to, the legitimate purpose(s) for which it is Processed. \n\n# **_4. Data Accuracy_** \n\nPersonal Data shall be recorded as accurately as possible and, where necessary, updated to fulfill the legitimate purpose(s) for which it is Processed. \n\n# **_5. Storage Limitation_** \n\nPersonal Data shall be kept in a form which permits identification of Data Subjects for no longer than is necessary for the legitimate purpose for which the Personal Data is collected, or for compatible further Processing, in accordance with this Policy. \n\n# **_6. Security_** \n\nPersonal Data shall be protected by appropriate and reasonable technical and organizational safeguards against unauthorized Processing and against accidental loss, destruction or damage. \n\n# **_7. Transfer of Personal Data_** \n\nPersonal Data shall only be transferred to a Third Party for legitimate purposes in accordance with this Policy and with appropriate regard for the protection of Personal Data. \n\n# **_8. Accountability and Review_** \n\nEach IDB Group Institution shall establish appropriate accountability and supervisory mechanism(s) to: \n\n- a) oversee compliance with this Policy: and \n\n- b) provide Data Subjects with a method, subject to reasonable limitations and conditions, to: \n\n   - i. request information regarding the Data Subject’s Personal Data Processed by or on behalf of such IDB Group Institution; and \n\n   - ii. seek redress if the Data Subject reasonably believes that the Data Subject’s Personal Data has been Processed in violation of this Policy. \n\n# **IV. MISCELLANEOUS** \n\n1. This Policy shall be implemented by each IDB Group Institution through guidelines, procedures, and other implementation measures, as applicable, tailored to each IDB Group Institution’s specific activities (the “ **Implementing Instruments** ”). \n\n2. This Policy shall become effective for each IDB Group Institution upon the earlier to occur of the following: (i) a declaration of effectiveness by the President of the IDB, in the case of the IDB, and the General Manager of IDB Invest, in the case of the IDB Invest, or such representative as each shall designate, to be issued upon adoption and effectiveness of Implementing Instruments; and (ii) three years from the date of approval of this Policy by the respective Board. \n\n3. This Policy shall not cover Personal Data collected before its effectiveness.\n\n4. The Processing of Personal Data in accordance with this Policy is without prejudice to the privileges and immunities of the IDB Group Institutions, which privileges and immunities are specifically reserved.\n\n---\n\n[Skip to main content](#main-content)\n\n\n*Last updated on: March 18, 2026*\n\n###### **Overview**\n\nThe Inter-American Investment Corporation (“IDB Invest”, “we”, “us” and “our”) is an international organization founded by international treaty in 1986 and is a member of the Inter-American Development Bank Group (“IDB Group”). As such, it is not subject to any national or supranational laws.\n\nThis Privacy Notice (“Privacy Notice”) explains how IDB Invest collects, uses, stores, transfers or otherwise processes the Personal Data of individuals (other than our own personnel and their dependents) (“you”). For the purposes of this Privacy Notice, Personal Data means any information relating to an identified or identifiable individual, such as a person’s name, contact details, location data, or factors relating to their physical, economic, cultural or social identity, or any other information that may reasonably be linked to that individual.\n\nIf you are either (i) the direct or indirect beneficiary of IDB Invest [Products and Services](https://idbinvest.org/en/solutions), or (ii) a representative of, or otherwise associated with, businesses and other organizations currently or potentially benefiting from or participating in IDB Invest’s [Products or Services](https://idbinvest.org/en/solutions) (for example, employees, officers, shareholders, directors, beneficial owners, guarantors or key vendors or partners of such businesses or organizations), this Privacy Notice applies to the processing of your Personal Data.\n\nPersonal data is processed by IDB Invest in accordance with the [IDB Group Personal Data Privacy Policy](https://idbinvest.org/sites/default/files/2022-11/IDB%20Group%20Personal%20Data%20Privacy%20Policy.pdf) (the “Privacy Policy”). Such processing enables IDB Invest to carry out its mission, mandate and purpose as an international organization established by its member countries.\n\nPlease ensure that you read this Privacy Notice in its entirety, as amended from time to time.\n\n---\n\n###### **What Does this Privacy Notice Cover?**\n\nThis Privacy Notice relates to the Personal Data we collect and process from you, and covers the following aspects:\n\n(Click on the topic you want to read)\n\n* [The contexts in which we process your Personal Data;](#1)\n* [The types of Personal Data that we process about you;](#2)\n* [The sources from which IDB Invest obtain your Personal Data;](#3)\n* [How and why IDB Invest processes your Personal Data;](#4)\n* [How long we keep your Personal Data;](#5)\n* [How, why and to whom we transfer your Personal Data;](#6)\n* [How we protect your Personal Data;](#7)\n* [Changes to this Privacy Notice;](#8)\n* [Explains the application of our privileges and immunities;](#9) and\n* [Explains how you may contact us with queries or complaints.](#10)\n\n---\n\n###### **The Contexts in Which we Process your Personal Data**\n\nThe Personal Data processing activities we undertake will vary based on your relationship with IDB Invest.\n\n**I. Visitors to IDB Invest’s websites**\n\nIDB Invest does not automatically process Personal Data related to the visitors of its website, e.g. idbinvest.org, or official IDB Invest pages on other platforms. However, we will process Personal Data that you submit through any interface of the official websites (for example, when registering for an event). This Privacy Notice does not apply to third party websites. We encourage you to review the privacy notices of any third-party websites you visit.\n\n**II. Subscribers of IDB Invest newsletters or publications**\n\nIf you subscribe to an IDB Invest newsletter or publication, we process your Personal Data (for example, your name and e-mail address) so we can make sure that you receive it.\n\n**III. Registered attendees of IDB Invest events**\n\nIf you register to attend an IDB Invest event, we collect and process your Personal Data in connection with the organization and management of the event.\n\n**IV. Personal Data processed in the course of providing our Products and Services**\n\nIn the course of providing our Products and Services IDB Invest processes Personal Data.\n\n**V. Personal Data in the context of recruitment**\n\nPersonal Data is required to manage job applications and recruitment processes. For detailed information, please refer to the privacy notice provided to job applicants during the application process ([available here](https://www.iadb.org/en/terms-conditions-and-notices/privacy-notice/job-applicant-privacy-notice)).\n\n**VI. Personal Data in the context of procurement**\n\nIn the course of providing our procurement activities, IDB Invest processes Personal Data.\n\n**VII. Business planning, client strategy, communications and analytics activities**\n\nIf you engage with IDB Invest as a business contact, prospective client, or external stakeholder (for example, through meetings, conferences, or professional networking), we may process your Personal Data for business development, client engagement, and institutional communications purposes.\n\n---\n\n###### **What Personal Data do we Process?**\n\nWe may collect and process the following Personal Data about you:\n\n* **Identification and contact data –** name, postal address(es), email address, phone number(s), signature specimen, passport/nationality identity documents (including embedded photographs), age and date of birth, citizenship status, office location, and limited biometric identifiers used for identity verification or security purposes;\n* **Operations data –** information about your involvement in, and/or the development impact on you of, our investment and advisory operations and activities;\n* **Financial data –** relevant financial information of how you benefit directly or indirectly from our Products and Services;\n* **Background data –** relevant background information used for anti-corruption and anti-fraud assessments in accordance with our applicable policies and procedures;\n* **Professional data –** job title, employer details or organizational affiliation, photograph in your CV, professional history, qualification details, information about your experience, participation in meetings, seminars, and conferences, information about your professional relationship with other individuals or institutions, language abilities, and other professional skills;\n* **Correspondence –** records of any correspondence we may have with you, records of your correspondence preferences (including subscription to our newsletters);\n* **Consent records –** records of preferences and permissions you provide to us, including records of consent opt-in/opt-out choices, where applicable. When maintained, such records are used solely to demonstrate compliance with applicable legal, contractual or governance obligations and to respect your stated preferences;\n* **Data relating to our websites –** technical data (device type, operating system, browser type and settings, IP address, language settings), usage and behavioral data, connection information (dates, times, location), analytics, and aggregate statistical information.\n* **Diversity and inclusion data –** salutations, gender identity, race / ethnicity, disability status;\n\nIn limited circumstances, IDB Invest may process special categories of Personal Data, such as information relating to an individual’s health, racial or ethnic origin, or other similarly sensitive characteristics. Such data will be processed only where strictly necessary and in accordance with applicable institutional policies and will be subject to enhanced safeguards designed to ensure an appropriate level of protection for the confidentiality, integrity, and security of the Personal Data.\n\n---\n\n###### **Where we Obtain your Personal Data?**\n\nWe may obtain or receive Personal Data about you from the following sources:\n\n* **Personal Data you or your employer provide to us –** Personal Data provided directly by you (e.g., job applications, correspondence you send us, information you provide to our investment officers, or when you complete an online form or survey), or that is provided to us by your employer or other organization with which you are associated, and information collected during meetings, events, and business interactions.\n* **Personal Data we collect by automated means –** As noted above, we may obtain certain information by automated means when you visit our websites.\n* **Personal Data we collect from third parties –** We may collect or obtain Personal Data from third parties (e.g., counterparties to a transaction, law enforcement authorities, relevant business contacts, specialized databases operated by the private sector, specialized external service providers, consultants or vendors).\n* **Personal Data you make public –** We may collect or obtain Personal Data that you manifestly choose to make public, including via social media (e.g., we may collect information from your social media profile(s), if you make a public post about us).\n\n---\n\n###### **Why we Process your Personal Data?**\n\nIDB Invest processes your Personal Data as reasonably necessary to conduct and manage our activities within the contexts listed above. This includes processing Personal Data for any of the following purposes:\n\n**I. To carry out IDB Invest’s investment, advisory and asset management activities**\n\n* Exploring investment opportunities and conducting due diligence;\n* Executing legal instruments related to investment, advisory and asset management activities;\n* Administering and managing our relationships with counterparties (and potential counterparties) in the context of our investment, advisory and asset management activities (or potential activities that may be of interest);\n* Understanding and monitoring the development impact of our activities;\n* Investigating and responding to complaints, and establishing, exercising, or defending IDB Invest’s legal rights and obligations;\n* Coordinating with other IDB Group Institutions; and,\n* Supporting equality, diversity and inclusion in our projects.\n\n**II. To comply with legal and policy obligations and manage risk**\n\n* Performing internal governance functions;\n* Conducting accounting and financial management;\n* Maintaining appropriate accounting, financial management and other records;\n* Fulfill our policy obligations, confirming and verifying your identity, and screening against government and/or law enforcement agency sanctions lists and other legal restrictions;\n* Carrying out our obligations, and exercising our rights, under applicable legal or regulatory requirements and any contracts entered into between you and IDB Invest;\n* Conducting credit and other risk assessment and control activities, including for the prevention and detection of corruption and fraud; and,\n* Training our staff and maintaining and improving the quality of our internal processes and arrangements.\n\n**III. To manage communications, stakeholder engagement and business development**\n\n* Disseminating information to further IDB Invest’s mission to improve lives in Latin America and the Caribbean, and providing research information;\n* Responding to your queries and feedback (for example, if you have asked a question or submitted feedback through our website);\n* Providing you with information, products or services you have requested or that may be of interest to you, unless you tell us otherwise; and,\n* Conducting business intelligence operations; and conducting business planning and client strategy activities, including organizing and managing events for clients and potential clients; conducting business analysis, planning and monitoring; preparing and disseminating marketing, institutional and business communications; defining communications strategies, guidelines and mechanisms; developing and communicating plans, strategies, strategic initiatives and updates to internal and external stakeholders; understanding client behavior through analytics to design and enhance client experiences; conducting impact evaluations and other in-depth studies (which may include surveys with project beneficiaries and other stakeholders); and supporting business development and client engagement initiatives.\n\n**IV. In connection with the management of IDB Invest’s websites, data analytics and IT security**\n\n* Providing access, maintaining and improving our websites and services;\n* Enabling you to participate in any interactive features of our websites and communicating with you, including through our newsletter, subject to your preferences;\n* Presenting website content in a manner suitable for the device you are accessing it from Undertaking data analytics to understand how users interact with our websites and online public-facing materials;\n* Monitoring and analyzing the use of our products and services for purposes of developing and improving them;\n* Managing and ensuring the security of our IT systems, including detecting and preventing misuse or abuse of our websites and services, and for backup and disaster recovery purposes; and,\n* We may also process Personal Data for any other purpose described to you at the time your data is collected.\n\nWe may also collect and process Personal Data of visitors to our premises, including for the purposes of ensuring safety and security at those premises, as further detailed in the notices available at our premises.\n\n---\n\n###### **How Long we Keep your Personal Data**\n\nYour Personal Data will be kept only as long as necessary for the purposes set out in this Privacy Notice and in accordance with IDB Invest’s applicable records retention and disposition schedules. The specific length of time will depend on the type of Personal Data, the reasons for which it is processed, and other obligations under IDB Invest’s policies and procedures.\n\n---\n\n###### **International Transfers of Personal Data**\n\nWhen you submit Personal Data to us by any means, that Personal Data may be transferred to a jurisdiction other than the one in which you live. In particular, Personal Data may be transferred to the United States. The data protection and other privacy laws of the United States may not afford the same level of protection as the laws of other countries.\n\n---\n\n###### **To whom we Disclose your Personal Data?**\n\nIDB Invest may disclose your Personal Data to the recipients described below, as reasonably necessary for the purposes outlined in this Privacy Notice.\n\n* IDB Group Institutions: We may disclose your Personal Data to other IDB Group institutions, such as the Inter-American Development Bank, as necessary for the purposes set out in this Privacy Notice.\n* Third parties: Unless otherwise noted below, and subject to contractually agreed conditions of confidentiality and security (where applicable), we may disclose your Personal Data to the categories of parties listed below:\n  + Service providers and suppliers who perform services, such as event vendors and organizers, consulting firms, among others, and providers that support compliance processes, including KYC screening and due diligence processes.\n  + Legal and other advisors that assist, advise or represent an IDB Group Institution as needed, such as attorneys, in connection with litigation, investigations, advising on contractual obligations, or enabling an IDB Group Institution to carry out its development mandate.\n  + Relevant legal, regulatory or administrative authorities, as we believe to be appropriate, for example, public registers involved in the execution and enforcement of relevant transaction documents, and other relevant authorities to protect and defend our rights and property, protect the interests of the IDB Group or others; or enable us to pursue available remedies or limit the damages that we may sustain; and,\n  + Other selected third parties: legal entities, including financial institutions, custodians, brokers, private companies, intermediaries, donors, partners and other organizations with which you are associated or involved (if any) in connection with our Products or Services; and peer researchers from academia, who carry out impact evaluations, among others.\n\nIDB Invest seeks to ensure that all partners and service providers processing Personal Data on its behalf implement appropriate technical and organizational safeguards to protect the privacy and security of such data.\n\n---\n\n###### **How to Request Information on your Personal Data Processed by IDB Invest**\n\nAs part of its data privacy framework, IDB Invest has established a procedure for individuals to request information regarding their Personal Data processed by IDB Invest and, when appropriate, to seek redress if they reasonably believe their Personal Data has not been processed in accordance with the IDB Group Personal Data Privacy Policy.\n\nYou may submit such a request using the webform [available here](https://forms.office.com/r/QAvQqSEBdy).\n\n---\n\n###### **How we Protect your Personal Data**\n\nWe have appropriate technical (e.g., firewalls, malware scans, anti-virus protection, encryption, physical locks) and organizational (e.g., policies and procedures, privacy assessments, due diligence, awareness, and training) safeguards in place to prevent unauthorized processing and accidental loss, damage, or destruction of Personal Data. These safeguards take into account the sensitivity of the data, as well as the current state of technology. We also have procedures in place to deal with data breaches, and we will notify you accordingly when appropriate.\n\n---\n\n###### **Changes to this Privacy Notice**\n\nThis Privacy Notice was last updated on the date listed above. If we change it, we will post the new version to this website.\n\n---\n\n###### **Queries and Complaints**\n\nIf you have any complaints or queries regarding your Personal Data, please contact [[email protected]](/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection#b0c0c2d9c6d1d3c9f0f9f4f2d9dec6d5c3c49edfc2d7).\n\n---\n\n###### **Privileges and Immunities**\n\nNothing contained in this Privacy Notice shall constitute or be considered to be a limitation upon or a waiver of the privileges and immunities of IDB Invest, which are specifically reserved.\n\n\n---\n\n# **<u>IDB GROUP PERSONAL DATA PRIVACY POLICY</u>**<sup>**1**</sup> \n\n# **I. PURPOSE AND APPLICATION** \n\nThis document sets out the Policy for the Processing of Personal Data by IDB Group Institutions. \n\nThis Policy applies to the Processing of Personal Data by, or on behalf of, IDB Group Institutions, and is intended to develop consistent practices across the IDB Group. \n\n# **II. DEFINITIONS** \n\nCapitalized terms or acronyms used in this Policy have the meaning set out below: \n\n**_1._ Board(s)** : the Boards of Executive Directors of IDB and IDB Invest, respectively. \n\n**_2._ Data Subject** : a natural, living person to whom Personal Data pertains, and whose Personal Data is Processed by an IDB Group Institution. Data Subjects may include, without limitation, any current or former: (i) IDB Group Institution staff member, director or their dependents; (ii) IDB Group Institution contractor or consultant; (iii) applicant for a vacancy at an IDB Group Institution; (iv) IDB Group Institution suppliers or vendors; (v) IDB Group Institution client or their representatives; (vi) respondents to IDB Group Institution surveys; or (vii) subscribers to an IDB Group Institution website. \n\n**_3._ IDB** : the Inter-American Development Bank. \n\n**_4._ IDB Group** : the Inter-American Development Bank Group. \n\n**_5._ IDB Group Institution** : any one of the IDB<sup>2</sup> and IDB Invest. \n\n**_6._ IDB Invest** : the Inter-American Investment Corporation. \n\n**_7._ Implementing Instruments** : has the meaning set forth in Section IV below. \n\n**_8._ Personal Data** : any information relating to an identified or identifiable Data Subject. An identifiable Data Subject is one who can be identified by reasonable means, directly or indirectly, by reference to an attribute or combination of attributes within the data, or combination of the data with other available information. Examples of attributes that can be used to identify an identifiable Data Subject include their name, identification number, location data, online identifier, metadata, and factors specific to their physical, physiological, genetic, mental, economic, cultural or social identity. \n\n**_9._ Policy** : this Personal Data Privacy Policy. \n\n**_10._ Principles** : the principles set out in Section III below. \n\n> 1 This Policy is not effective yet pursuant to Section IV below. \n\n> 2 The Multilateral Investment Fund (commercially known as IDB Lab) is a fund administered by the IDB and, therefore, any references to IDB Group Institution include IDB Lab.\n\n**_11._ Processing** : any action or set of actions, automated or not, which is performed on Personal Data, which may include, without limitation, its collection, recording, use, consultation, retrieval, disclosure by transmission, dissemination or otherwise making available, forwarding, organization, storage, structuring, adaptation or alteration, alignment or combination, restriction, erasure or destruction. \n\n**_12._ Processed** : having undertaken the act of Processing. \n\n**_13._ Third Party** or **Third Parties** : a legal person, other than IDB Group Institutions, or a natural person, other than IDB Group Institutions’ personnel and their dependents, as defined within their respective policies and procedures. \n\n# **III. PRINCIPLES** \n\nThe following Principles shall apply to all Processing of Personal Data by IDB Group Institutions: \n\n# **_1. Legitimate, Fair and Transparent Processing_** \n\nPersonal Data shall only be Processed for legitimate purposes and in a fair and transparent manner. Legitimate purposes for Processing mean any purpose: \n\n- a. for which the consent of a Data Subject is obtained, either at the time Personal Data are collected or subsequently; \n\n- b. that is in the vital or best interest of (i) the Data Subject or (ii) another person; \n\n- c. that is reasonably necessary for the performance of a contract; \n\n- d. that is reasonably necessary to enable an IDB Group Institution to satisfy an obligation or undertaking, or to comply with an IDB Group Institution’s policy or procedure; \n\n- e. that is reasonably necessary to establish, exercise or defend an IDB Group Institution’s right or interest; or \n\n- f. that is consistent with, or reasonably necessary to enable an IDB Group Institution to carry out its mission, mandate or purpose as an international organization established by its member countries. \n\n# **_2. Purpose Limitation_** \n\nPersonal Data shall be collected for one or more specific and legitimate purpose(s) listed in Principle 1 above and not further Processed in a manner that is incompatible with such purpose(s). Further Processing for archiving purposes, research, or statistical purposes shall not be considered incompatible with such purpose(s).\n\n# **_3. Data Minimization_** \n\nThe amount and type of Personal Data collected shall be reasonably necessary for, and proportionate to, the legitimate purpose(s) for which it is Processed. \n\n# **_4. Data Accuracy_** \n\nPersonal Data shall be recorded as accurately as possible and, where necessary, updated to fulfill the legitimate purpose(s) for which it is Processed. \n\n# **_5. Storage Limitation_** \n\nPersonal Data shall be kept in a form which permits identification of Data Subjects for no longer than is necessary for the legitimate purpose for which the Personal Data is collected, or for compatible further Processing, in accordance with this Policy. \n\n# **_6. Security_** \n\nPersonal Data shall be protected by appropriate and reasonable technical and organizational safeguards against unauthorized Processing and against accidental loss, destruction or damage. \n\n# **_7. Transfer of Personal Data_** \n\nPersonal Data shall only be transferred to a Third Party for legitimate purposes in accordance with this Policy and with appropriate regard for the protection of Personal Data. \n\n# **_8. Accountability and Review_** \n\nEach IDB Group Institution shall establish appropriate accountability and supervisory mechanism(s) to: \n\n- a) oversee compliance with this Policy: and \n\n- b) provide Data Subjects with a method, subject to reasonable limitations and conditions, to: \n\n   - i. request information regarding the Data Subject’s Personal Data Processed by or on behalf of such IDB Group Institution; and \n\n   - ii. seek redress if the Data Subject reasonably believes that the Data Subject’s Personal Data has been Processed in violation of this Policy. \n\n# **IV. MISCELLANEOUS** \n\n1. This Policy shall be implemented by each IDB Group Institution through guidelines, procedures, and other implementation measures, as applicable, tailored to each IDB Group Institution’s specific activities (the “ **Implementing Instruments** ”). \n\n2. This Policy shall become effective for each IDB Group Institution upon the earlier to occur of the following: (i) a declaration of effectiveness by the President of the IDB, in the case of the IDB, and the General Manager of IDB Invest, in the case of the IDB Invest, or such representative as each shall designate, to be issued upon adoption and effectiveness of Implementing Instruments; and (ii) three years from the date of approval of this Policy by the respective Board. \n\n3. This Policy shall not cover Personal Data collected before its effectiveness.\n\n4. The Processing of Personal Data in accordance with this Policy is without prejudice to the privileges and immunities of the IDB Group Institutions, which privileges and immunities are specifically reserved.\n\n---\n\n[Skip to main content](#main-content)\n\n\n*Last updated on: March 18, 2026*\n\n###### **Overview**\n\nThe Inter-American Investment Corporation (“IDB Invest”, “we”, “us” and “our”) is an international organization founded by international treaty in 1986 and is a member of the Inter-American Development Bank Group (“IDB Group”). As such, it is not subject to any national or supranational laws.\n\nThis Privacy Notice (“Privacy Notice”) explains how IDB Invest collects, uses, stores, transfers or otherwise processes the Personal Data of individuals (other than our own personnel and their dependents) (“you”). For the purposes of this Privacy Notice, Personal Data means any information relating to an identified or identifiable individual, such as a person’s name, contact details, location data, or factors relating to their physical, economic, cultural or social identity, or any other information that may reasonably be linked to that individual.\n\nIf you are either (i) the direct or indirect beneficiary of IDB Invest [Products and Services](https://idbinvest.org/en/solutions), or (ii) a representative of, or otherwise associated with, businesses and other organizations currently or potentially benefiting from or participating in IDB Invest’s [Products or Services](https://idbinvest.org/en/solutions) (for example, employees, officers, shareholders, directors, beneficial owners, guarantors or key vendors or partners of such businesses or organizations), this Privacy Notice applies to the processing of your Personal Data.\n\nPersonal data is processed by IDB Invest in accordance with the [IDB Group Personal Data Privacy Policy](https://idbinvest.org/sites/default/files/2022-11/IDB%20Group%20Personal%20Data%20Privacy%20Policy.pdf) (the “Privacy Policy”). Such processing enables IDB Invest to carry out its mission, mandate and purpose as an international organization established by its member countries.\n\nPlease ensure that you read this Privacy Notice in its entirety, as amended from time to time.\n\n---\n\n###### **What Does this Privacy Notice Cover?**\n\nThis Privacy Notice relates to the Personal Data we collect and process from you, and covers the following aspects:\n\n(Click on the topic you want to read)\n\n* [The contexts in which we process your Personal Data;](#1)\n* [The types of Personal Data that we process about you;](#2)\n* [The sources from which IDB Invest obtain your Personal Data;](#3)\n* [How and why IDB Invest processes your Personal Data;](#4)\n* [How long we keep your Personal Data;](#5)\n* [How, why and to whom we transfer your Personal Data;](#6)\n* [How we protect your Personal Data;](#7)\n* [Changes to this Privacy Notice;](#8)\n* [Explains the application of our privileges and immunities;](#9) and\n* [Explains how you may contact us with queries or complaints.](#10)\n\n---\n\n###### **The Contexts in Which we Process your Personal Data**\n\nThe Personal Data processing activities we undertake will vary based on your relationship with IDB Invest.\n\n**I. Visitors to IDB Invest’s websites**\n\nIDB Invest does not automatically process Personal Data related to the visitors of its website, e.g. idbinvest.org, or official IDB Invest pages on other platforms. However, we will process Personal Data that you submit through any interface of the official websites (for example, when registering for an event). This Privacy Notice does not apply to third party websites. We encourage you to review the privacy notices of any third-party websites you visit.\n\n**II. Subscribers of IDB Invest newsletters or publications**\n\nIf you subscribe to an IDB Invest newsletter or publication, we process your Personal Data (for example, your name and e-mail address) so we can make sure that you receive it.\n\n**III. Registered attendees of IDB Invest events**\n\nIf you register to attend an IDB Invest event, we collect and process your Personal Data in connection with the organization and management of the event.\n\n**IV. Personal Data processed in the course of providing our Products and Services**\n\nIn the course of providing our Products and Services IDB Invest processes Personal Data.\n\n**V. Personal Data in the context of recruitment**\n\nPersonal Data is required to manage job applications and recruitment processes. For detailed information, please refer to the privacy notice provided to job applicants during the application process ([available here](https://www.iadb.org/en/terms-conditions-and-notices/privacy-notice/job-applicant-privacy-notice)).\n\n**VI. Personal Data in the context of procurement**\n\nIn the course of providing our procurement activities, IDB Invest processes Personal Data.\n\n**VII. Business planning, client strategy, communications and analytics activities**\n\nIf you engage with IDB Invest as a business contact, prospective client, or external stakeholder (for example, through meetings, conferences, or professional networking), we may process your Personal Data for business development, client engagement, and institutional communications purposes.\n\n---\n\n###### **What Personal Data do we Process?**\n\nWe may collect and process the following Personal Data about you:\n\n* **Identification and contact data –** name, postal address(es), email address, phone number(s), signature specimen, passport/nationality identity documents (including embedded photographs), age and date of birth, citizenship status, office location, and limited biometric identifiers used for identity verification or security purposes;\n* **Operations data –** information about your involvement in, and/or the development impact on you of, our investment and advisory operations and activities;\n* **Financial data –** relevant financial information of how you benefit directly or indirectly from our Products and Services;\n* **Background data –** relevant background information used for anti-corruption and anti-fraud assessments in accordance with our applicable policies and procedures;\n* **Professional data –** job title, employer details or organizational affiliation, photograph in your CV, professional history, qualification details, information about your experience, participation in meetings, seminars, and conferences, information about your professional relationship with other individuals or institutions, language abilities, and other professional skills;\n* **Correspondence –** records of any correspondence we may have with you, records of your correspondence preferences (including subscription to our newsletters);\n* **Consent records –** records of preferences and permissions you provide to us, including records of consent opt-in/opt-out choices, where applicable. When maintained, such records are used solely to demonstrate compliance with applicable legal, contractual or governance obligations and to respect your stated preferences;\n* **Data relating to our websites –** technical data (device type, operating system, browser type and settings, IP address, language settings), usage and behavioral data, connection information (dates, times, location), analytics, and aggregate statistical information.\n* **Diversity and inclusion data –** salutations, gender identity, race / ethnicity, disability status;\n\nIn limited circumstances, IDB Invest may process special categories of Personal Data, such as information relating to an individual’s health, racial or ethnic origin, or other similarly sensitive characteristics. Such data will be processed only where strictly necessary and in accordance with applicable institutional policies and will be subject to enhanced safeguards designed to ensure an appropriate level of protection for the confidentiality, integrity, and security of the Personal Data.\n\n---\n\n###### **Where we Obtain your Personal Data?**\n\nWe may obtain or receive Personal Data about you from the following sources:\n\n* **Personal Data you or your employer provide to us –** Personal Data provided directly by you (e.g., job applications, correspondence you send us, information you provide to our investment officers, or when you complete an online form or survey), or that is provided to us by your employer or other organization with which you are associated, and information collected during meetings, events, and business interactions.\n* **Personal Data we collect by automated means –** As noted above, we may obtain certain information by automated means when you visit our websites.\n* **Personal Data we collect from third parties –** We may collect or obtain Personal Data from third parties (e.g., counterparties to a transaction, law enforcement authorities, relevant business contacts, specialized databases operated by the private sector, specialized external service providers, consultants or vendors).\n* **Personal Data you make public –** We may collect or obtain Personal Data that you manifestly choose to make public, including via social media (e.g., we may collect information from your social media profile(s), if you make a public post about us).\n\n---\n\n###### **Why we Process your Personal Data?**\n\nIDB Invest processes your Personal Data as reasonably necessary to conduct and manage our activities within the contexts listed above. This includes processing Personal Data for any of the following purposes:\n\n**I. To carry out IDB Invest’s investment, advisory and asset management activities**\n\n* Exploring investment opportunities and conducting due diligence;\n* Executing legal instruments related to investment, advisory and asset management activities;\n* Administering and managing our relationships with counterparties (and potential counterparties) in the context of our investment, advisory and asset management activities (or potential activities that may be of interest);\n* Understanding and monitoring the development impact of our activities;\n* Investigating and responding to complaints, and establishing, exercising, or defending IDB Invest’s legal rights and obligations;\n* Coordinating with other IDB Group Institutions; and,\n* Supporting equality, diversity and inclusion in our projects.\n\n**II. To comply with legal and policy obligations and manage risk**\n\n* Performing internal governance functions;\n* Conducting accounting and financial management;\n* Maintaining appropriate accounting, financial management and other records;\n* Fulfill our policy obligations, confirming and verifying your identity, and screening against government and/or law enforcement agency sanctions lists and other legal restrictions;\n* Carrying out our obligations, and exercising our rights, under applicable legal or regulatory requirements and any contracts entered into between you and IDB Invest;\n* Conducting credit and other risk assessment and control activities, including for the prevention and detection of corruption and fraud; and,\n* Training our staff and maintaining and improving the quality of our internal processes and arrangements.\n\n**III. To manage communications, stakeholder engagement and business development**\n\n* Disseminating information to further IDB Invest’s mission to improve lives in Latin America and the Caribbean, and providing research information;\n* Responding to your queries and feedback (for example, if you have asked a question or submitted feedback through our website);\n* Providing you with information, products or services you have requested or that may be of interest to you, unless you tell us otherwise; and,\n* Conducting business intelligence operations; and conducting business planning and client strategy activities, including organizing and managing events for clients and potential clients; conducting business analysis, planning and monitoring; preparing and disseminating marketing, institutional and business communications; defining communications strategies, guidelines and mechanisms; developing and communicating plans, strategies, strategic initiatives and updates to internal and external stakeholders; understanding client behavior through analytics to design and enhance client experiences; conducting impact evaluations and other in-depth studies (which may include surveys with project beneficiaries and other stakeholders); and supporting business development and client engagement initiatives.\n\n**IV. In connection with the management of IDB Invest’s websites, data analytics and IT security**\n\n* Providing access, maintaining and improving our websites and services;\n* Enabling you to participate in any interactive features of our websites and communicating with you, including through our newsletter, subject to your preferences;\n* Presenting website content in a manner suitable for the device you are accessing it from Undertaking data analytics to understand how users interact with our websites and online public-facing materials;\n* Monitoring and analyzing the use of our products and services for purposes of developing and improving them;\n* Managing and ensuring the security of our IT systems, including detecting and preventing misuse or abuse of our websites and services, and for backup and disaster recovery purposes; and,\n* We may also process Personal Data for any other purpose described to you at the time your data is collected.\n\nWe may also collect and process Personal Data of visitors to our premises, including for the purposes of ensuring safety and security at those premises, as further detailed in the notices available at our premises.\n\n---\n\n###### **How Long we Keep your Personal Data**\n\nYour Personal Data will be kept only as long as necessary for the purposes set out in this Privacy Notice and in accordance with IDB Invest’s applicable records retention and disposition schedules. The specific length of time will depend on the type of Personal Data, the reasons for which it is processed, and other obligations under IDB Invest’s policies and procedures.\n\n---\n\n###### **International Transfers of Personal Data**\n\nWhen you submit Personal Data to us by any means, that Personal Data may be transferred to a jurisdiction other than the one in which you live. In particular, Personal Data may be transferred to the United States. The data protection and other privacy laws of the United States may not afford the same level of protection as the laws of other countries.\n\n---\n\n###### **To whom we Disclose your Personal Data?**\n\nIDB Invest may disclose your Personal Data to the recipients described below, as reasonably necessary for the purposes outlined in this Privacy Notice.\n\n* IDB Group Institutions: We may disclose your Personal Data to other IDB Group institutions, such as the Inter-American Development Bank, as necessary for the purposes set out in this Privacy Notice.\n* Third parties: Unless otherwise noted below, and subject to contractually agreed conditions of confidentiality and security (where applicable), we may disclose your Personal Data to the categories of parties listed below:\n  + Service providers and suppliers who perform services, such as event vendors and organizers, consulting firms, among others, and providers that support compliance processes, including KYC screening and due diligence processes.\n  + Legal and other advisors that assist, advise or represent an IDB Group Institution as needed, such as attorneys, in connection with litigation, investigations, advising on contractual obligations, or enabling an IDB Group Institution to carry out its development mandate.\n  + Relevant legal, regulatory or administrative authorities, as we believe to be appropriate, for example, public registers involved in the execution and enforcement of relevant transaction documents, and other relevant authorities to protect and defend our rights and property, protect the interests of the IDB Group or others; or enable us to pursue available remedies or limit the damages that we may sustain; and,\n  + Other selected third parties: legal entities, including financial institutions, custodians, brokers, private companies, intermediaries, donors, partners and other organizations with which you are associated or involved (if any) in connection with our Products or Services; and peer researchers from academia, who carry out impact evaluations, among others.\n\nIDB Invest seeks to ensure that all partners and service providers processing Personal Data on its behalf implement appropriate technical and organizational safeguards to protect the privacy and security of such data.\n\n---\n\n###### **How to Request Information on your Personal Data Processed by IDB Invest**\n\nAs part of its data privacy framework, IDB Invest has established a procedure for individuals to request information regarding their Personal Data processed by IDB Invest and, when appropriate, to seek redress if they reasonably believe their Personal Data has not been processed in accordance with the IDB Group Personal Data Privacy Policy.\n\nYou may submit such a request using the webform [available here](https://forms.office.com/r/QAvQqSEBdy).\n\n---\n\n###### **How we Protect your Personal Data**\n\nWe have appropriate technical (e.g., firewalls, malware scans, anti-virus protection, encryption, physical locks) and organizational (e.g., policies and procedures, privacy assessments, due diligence, awareness, and training) safeguards in place to prevent unauthorized processing and accidental loss, damage, or destruction of Personal Data. These safeguards take into account the sensitivity of the data, as well as the current state of technology. We also have procedures in place to deal with data breaches, and we will notify you accordingly when appropriate.\n\n---\n\n###### **Changes to this Privacy Notice**\n\nThis Privacy Notice was last updated on the date listed above. If we change it, we will post the new version to this website.\n\n---\n\n###### **Queries and Complaints**\n\nIf you have any complaints or queries regarding your Personal Data, please contact [[email protected]](/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection#b0c0c2d9c6d1d3c9f0f9f4f2d9dec6d5c3c49edfc2d7).\n\n---\n\n###### **Privileges and Immunities**\n\nNothing contained in this Privacy Notice shall constitute or be considered to be a limitation upon or a waiver of the privileges and immunities of IDB Invest, which are specifically reserved.\n\n\n---\n\n# **<u>IDB GROUP PERSONAL DATA PRIVACY POLICY</u>**<sup>**1**</sup> \n\n# **I. PURPOSE AND APPLICATION** \n\nThis document sets out the Policy for the Processing of Personal Data by IDB Group Institutions. \n\nThis Policy applies to the Processing of Personal Data by, or on behalf of, IDB Group Institutions, and is intended to develop consistent practices across the IDB Group. \n\n# **II. DEFINITIONS** \n\nCapitalized terms or acronyms used in this Policy have the meaning set out below: \n\n**_1._ Board(s)** : the Boards of Executive Directors of IDB and IDB Invest, respectively. \n\n**_2._ Data Subject** : a natural, living person to whom Personal Data pertains, and whose Personal Data is Processed by an IDB Group Institution. Data Subjects may include, without limitation, any current or former: (i) IDB Group Institution staff member, director or their dependents; (ii) IDB Group Institution contractor or consultant; (iii) applicant for a vacancy at an IDB Group Institution; (iv) IDB Group Institution suppliers or vendors; (v) IDB Group Institution client or their representatives; (vi) respondents to IDB Group Institution surveys; or (vii) subscribers to an IDB Group Institution website. \n\n**_3._ IDB** : the Inter-American Development Bank. \n\n**_4._ IDB Group** : the Inter-American Development Bank Group. \n\n**_5._ IDB Group Institution** : any one of the IDB<sup>2</sup> and IDB Invest. \n\n**_6._ IDB Invest** : the Inter-American Investment Corporation. \n\n**_7._ Implementing Instruments** : has the meaning set forth in Section IV below. \n\n**_8._ Personal Data** : any information relating to an identified or identifiable Data Subject. An identifiable Data Subject is one who can be identified by reasonable means, directly or indirectly, by reference to an attribute or combination of attributes within the data, or combination of the data with other available information. Examples of attributes that can be used to identify an identifiable Data Subject include their name, identification number, location data, online identifier, metadata, and factors specific to their physical, physiological, genetic, mental, economic, cultural or social identity. \n\n**_9._ Policy** : this Personal Data Privacy Policy. \n\n**_10._ Principles** : the principles set out in Section III below. \n\n> 1 This Policy is not effective yet pursuant to Section IV below. \n\n> 2 The Multilateral Investment Fund (commercially known as IDB Lab) is a fund administered by the IDB and, therefore, any references to IDB Group Institution include IDB Lab.\n\n**_11._ Processing** : any action or set of actions, automated or not, which is performed on Personal Data, which may include, without limitation, its collection, recording, use, consultation, retrieval, disclosure by transmission, dissemination or otherwise making available, forwarding, organization, storage, structuring, adaptation or alteration, alignment or combination, restriction, erasure or destruction. \n\n**_12._ Processed** : having undertaken the act of Processing. \n\n**_13._ Third Party** or **Third Parties** : a legal person, other than IDB Group Institutions, or a natural person, other than IDB Group Institutions’ personnel and their dependents, as defined within their respective policies and procedures. \n\n# **III. PRINCIPLES** \n\nThe following Principles shall apply to all Processing of Personal Data by IDB Group Institutions: \n\n# **_1. Legitimate, Fair and Transparent Processing_** \n\nPersonal Data shall only be Processed for legitimate purposes and in a fair and transparent manner. Legitimate purposes for Processing mean any purpose: \n\n- a. for which the consent of a Data Subject is obtained, either at the time Personal Data are collected or subsequently; \n\n- b. that is in the vital or best interest of (i) the Data Subject or (ii) another person; \n\n- c. that is reasonably necessary for the performance of a contract; \n\n- d. that is reasonably necessary to enable an IDB Group Institution to satisfy an obligation or undertaking, or to comply with an IDB Group Institution’s policy or procedure; \n\n- e. that is reasonably necessary to establish, exercise or defend an IDB Group Institution’s right or interest; or \n\n- f. that is consistent with, or reasonably necessary to enable an IDB Group Institution to carry out its mission, mandate or purpose as an international organization established by its member countries. \n\n# **_2. Purpose Limitation_** \n\nPersonal Data shall be collected for one or more specific and legitimate purpose(s) listed in Principle 1 above and not further Processed in a manner that is incompatible with such purpose(s). Further Processing for archiving purposes, research, or statistical purposes shall not be considered incompatible with such purpose(s).\n\n# **_3. Data Minimization_** \n\nThe amount and type of Personal Data collected shall be reasonably necessary for, and proportionate to, the legitimate purpose(s) for which it is Processed. \n\n# **_4. Data Accuracy_** \n\nPersonal Data shall be recorded as accurately as possible and, where necessary, updated to fulfill the legitimate purpose(s) for which it is Processed. \n\n# **_5. Storage Limitation_** \n\nPersonal Data shall be kept in a form which permits identification of Data Subjects for no longer than is necessary for the legitimate purpose for which the Personal Data is collected, or for compatible further Processing, in accordance with this Policy. \n\n# **_6. Security_** \n\nPersonal Data shall be protected by appropriate and reasonable technical and organizational safeguards against unauthorized Processing and against accidental loss, destruction or damage. \n\n# **_7. Transfer of Personal Data_** \n\nPersonal Data shall only be transferred to a Third Party for legitimate purposes in accordance with this Policy and with appropriate regard for the protection of Personal Data. \n\n# **_8. Accountability and Review_** \n\nEach IDB Group Institution shall establish appropriate accountability and supervisory mechanism(s) to: \n\n- a) oversee compliance with this Policy: and \n\n- b) provide Data Subjects with a method, subject to reasonable limitations and conditions, to: \n\n   - i. request information regarding the Data Subject’s Personal Data Processed by or on behalf of such IDB Group Institution; and \n\n   - ii. seek redress if the Data Subject reasonably believes that the Data Subject’s Personal Data has been Processed in violation of this Policy. \n\n# **IV. MISCELLANEOUS** \n\n1. This Policy shall be implemented by each IDB Group Institution through guidelines, procedures, and other implementation measures, as applicable, tailored to each IDB Group Institution’s specific activities (the “ **Implementing Instruments** ”). \n\n2. This Policy shall become effective for each IDB Group Institution upon the earlier to occur of the following: (i) a declaration of effectiveness by the President of the IDB, in the case of the IDB, and the General Manager of IDB Invest, in the case of the IDB Invest, or such representative as each shall designate, to be issued upon adoption and effectiveness of Implementing Instruments; and (ii) three years from the date of approval of this Policy by the respective Board. \n\n3. This Policy shall not cover Personal Data collected before its effectiveness.\n\n4. The Processing of Personal Data in accordance with this Policy is without prejudice to the privileges and immunities of the IDB Group Institutions, which privileges and immunities are specifically reserved.\n\n---\n\n[Skip to main content](#main-content)\n\n\n*Last updated on: March 18, 2026*\n\n###### **Overview**\n\nThe Inter-American Investment Corporation (“IDB Invest”, “we”, “us” and “our”) is an international organization founded by international treaty in 1986 and is a member of the Inter-American Development Bank Group (“IDB Group”). As such, it is not subject to any national or supranational laws.\n\nThis Privacy Notice (“Privacy Notice”) explains how IDB Invest collects, uses, stores, transfers or otherwise processes the Personal Data of individuals (other than our own personnel and their dependents) (“you”). For the purposes of this Privacy Notice, Personal Data means any information relating to an identified or identifiable individual, such as a person’s name, contact details, location data, or factors relating to their physical, economic, cultural or social identity, or any other information that may reasonably be linked to that individual.\n\nIf you are either (i) the direct or indirect beneficiary of IDB Invest [Products and Services](https://idbinvest.org/en/solutions), or (ii) a representative of, or otherwise associated with, businesses and other organizations currently or potentially benefiting from or participating in IDB Invest’s [Products or Services](https://idbinvest.org/en/solutions) (for example, employees, officers, shareholders, directors, beneficial owners, guarantors or key vendors or partners of such businesses or organizations), this Privacy Notice applies to the processing of your Personal Data.\n\nPersonal data is processed by IDB Invest in accordance with the [IDB Group Personal Data Privacy Policy](https://idbinvest.org/sites/default/files/2022-11/IDB%20Group%20Personal%20Data%20Privacy%20Policy.pdf) (the “Privacy Policy”). Such processing enables IDB Invest to carry out its mission, mandate and purpose as an international organization established by its member countries.\n\nPlease ensure that you read this Privacy Notice in its entirety, as amended from time to time.\n\n---\n\n###### **What Does this Privacy Notice Cover?**\n\nThis Privacy Notice relates to the Personal Data we collect and process from you, and covers the following aspects:\n\n(Click on the topic you want to read)\n\n* [The contexts in which we process your Personal Data;](#1)\n* [The types of Personal Data that we process about you;](#2)\n* [The sources from which IDB Invest obtain your Personal Data;](#3)\n* [How and why IDB Invest processes your Personal Data;](#4)\n* [How long we keep your Personal Data;](#5)\n* [How, why and to whom we transfer your Personal Data;](#6)\n* [How we protect your Personal Data;](#7)\n* [Changes to this Privacy Notice;](#8)\n* [Explains the application of our privileges and immunities;](#9) and\n* [Explains how you may contact us with queries or complaints.](#10)\n\n---\n\n###### **The Contexts in Which we Process your Personal Data**\n\nThe Personal Data processing activities we undertake will vary based on your relationship with IDB Invest.\n\n**I. Visitors to IDB Invest’s websites**\n\nIDB Invest does not automatically process Personal Data related to the visitors of its website, e.g. idbinvest.org, or official IDB Invest pages on other platforms. However, we will process Personal Data that you submit through any interface of the official websites (for example, when registering for an event). This Privacy Notice does not apply to third party websites. We encourage you to review the privacy notices of any third-party websites you visit.\n\n**II. Subscribers of IDB Invest newsletters or publications**\n\nIf you subscribe to an IDB Invest newsletter or publication, we process your Personal Data (for example, your name and e-mail address) so we can make sure that you receive it.\n\n**III. Registered attendees of IDB Invest events**\n\nIf you register to attend an IDB Invest event, we collect and process your Personal Data in connection with the organization and management of the event.\n\n**IV. Personal Data processed in the course of providing our Products and Services**\n\nIn the course of providing our Products and Services IDB Invest processes Personal Data.\n\n**V. Personal Data in the context of recruitment**\n\nPersonal Data is required to manage job applications and recruitment processes. For detailed information, please refer to the privacy notice provided to job applicants during the application process ([available here](https://www.iadb.org/en/terms-conditions-and-notices/privacy-notice/job-applicant-privacy-notice)).\n\n**VI. Personal Data in the context of procurement**\n\nIn the course of providing our procurement activities, IDB Invest processes Personal Data.\n\n**VII. Business planning, client strategy, communications and analytics activities**\n\nIf you engage with IDB Invest as a business contact, prospective client, or external stakeholder (for example, through meetings, conferences, or professional networking), we may process your Personal Data for business development, client engagement, and institutional communications purposes.\n\n---\n\n###### **What Personal Data do we Process?**\n\nWe may collect and process the following Personal Data about you:\n\n* **Identification and contact data –** name, postal address(es), email address, phone number(s), signature specimen, passport/nationality identity documents (including embedded photographs), age and date of birth, citizenship status, office location, and limited biometric identifiers used for identity verification or security purposes;\n* **Operations data –** information about your involvement in, and/or the development impact on you of, our investment and advisory operations and activities;\n* **Financial data –** relevant financial information of how you benefit directly or indirectly from our Products and Services;\n* **Background data –** relevant background information used for anti-corruption and anti-fraud assessments in accordance with our applicable policies and procedures;\n* **Professional data –** job title, employer details or organizational affiliation, photograph in your CV, professional history, qualification details, information about your experience, participation in meetings, seminars, and conferences, information about your professional relationship with other individuals or institutions, language abilities, and other professional skills;\n* **Correspondence –** records of any correspondence we may have with you, records of your correspondence preferences (including subscription to our newsletters);\n* **Consent records –** records of preferences and permissions you provide to us, including records of consent opt-in/opt-out choices, where applicable. When maintained, such records are used solely to demonstrate compliance with applicable legal, contractual or governance obligations and to respect your stated preferences;\n* **Data relating to our websites –** technical data (device type, operating system, browser type and settings, IP address, language settings), usage and behavioral data, connection information (dates, times, location), analytics, and aggregate statistical information.\n* **Diversity and inclusion data –** salutations, gender identity, race / ethnicity, disability status;\n\nIn limited circumstances, IDB Invest may process special categories of Personal Data, such as information relating to an individual’s health, racial or ethnic origin, or other similarly sensitive characteristics. Such data will be processed only where strictly necessary and in accordance with applicable institutional policies and will be subject to enhanced safeguards designed to ensure an appropriate level of protection for the confidentiality, integrity, and security of the Personal Data.\n\n---\n\n###### **Where we Obtain your Personal Data?**\n\nWe may obtain or receive Personal Data about you from the following sources:\n\n* **Personal Data you or your employer provide to us –** Personal Data provided directly by you (e.g., job applications, correspondence you send us, information you provide to our investment officers, or when you complete an online form or survey), or that is provided to us by your employer or other organization with which you are associated, and information collected during meetings, events, and business interactions.\n* **Personal Data we collect by automated means –** As noted above, we may obtain certain information by automated means when you visit our websites.\n* **Personal Data we collect from third parties –** We may collect or obtain Personal Data from third parties (e.g., counterparties to a transaction, law enforcement authorities, relevant business contacts, specialized databases operated by the private sector, specialized external service providers, consultants or vendors).\n* **Personal Data you make public –** We may collect or obtain Personal Data that you manifestly choose to make public, including via social media (e.g., we may collect information from your social media profile(s), if you make a public post about us).\n\n---\n\n###### **Why we Process your Personal Data?**\n\nIDB Invest processes your Personal Data as reasonably necessary to conduct and manage our activities within the contexts listed above. This includes processing Personal Data for any of the following purposes:\n\n**I. To carry out IDB Invest’s investment, advisory and asset management activities**\n\n* Exploring investment opportunities and conducting due diligence;\n* Executing legal instruments related to investment, advisory and asset management activities;\n* Administering and managing our relationships with counterparties (and potential counterparties) in the context of our investment, advisory and asset management activities (or potential activities that may be of interest);\n* Understanding and monitoring the development impact of our activities;\n* Investigating and responding to complaints, and establishing, exercising, or defending IDB Invest’s legal rights and obligations;\n* Coordinating with other IDB Group Institutions; and,\n* Supporting equality, diversity and inclusion in our projects.\n\n**II. To comply with legal and policy obligations and manage risk**\n\n* Performing internal governance functions;\n* Conducting accounting and financial management;\n* Maintaining appropriate accounting, financial management and other records;\n* Fulfill our policy obligations, confirming and verifying your identity, and screening against government and/or law enforcement agency sanctions lists and other legal restrictions;\n* Carrying out our obligations, and exercising our rights, under applicable legal or regulatory requirements and any contracts entered into between you and IDB Invest;\n* Conducting credit and other risk assessment and control activities, including for the prevention and detection of corruption and fraud; and,\n* Training our staff and maintaining and improving the quality of our internal processes and arrangements.\n\n**III. To manage communications, stakeholder engagement and business development**\n\n* Disseminating information to further IDB Invest’s mission to improve lives in Latin America and the Caribbean, and providing research information;\n* Responding to your queries and feedback (for example, if you have asked a question or submitted feedback through our website);\n* Providing you with information, products or services you have requested or that may be of interest to you, unless you tell us otherwise; and,\n* Conducting business intelligence operations; and conducting business planning and client strategy activities, including organizing and managing events for clients and potential clients; conducting business analysis, planning and monitoring; preparing and disseminating marketing, institutional and business communications; defining communications strategies, guidelines and mechanisms; developing and communicating plans, strategies, strategic initiatives and updates to internal and external stakeholders; understanding client behavior through analytics to design and enhance client experiences; conducting impact evaluations and other in-depth studies (which may include surveys with project beneficiaries and other stakeholders); and supporting business development and client engagement initiatives.\n\n**IV. In connection with the management of IDB Invest’s websites, data analytics and IT security**\n\n* Providing access, maintaining and improving our websites and services;\n* Enabling you to participate in any interactive features of our websites and communicating with you, including through our newsletter, subject to your preferences;\n* Presenting website content in a manner suitable for the device you are accessing it from Undertaking data analytics to understand how users interact with our websites and online public-facing materials;\n* Monitoring and analyzing the use of our products and services for purposes of developing and improving them;\n* Managing and ensuring the security of our IT systems, including detecting and preventing misuse or abuse of our websites and services, and for backup and disaster recovery purposes; and,\n* We may also process Personal Data for any other purpose described to you at the time your data is collected.\n\nWe may also collect and process Personal Data of visitors to our premises, including for the purposes of ensuring safety and security at those premises, as further detailed in the notices available at our premises.\n\n---\n\n###### **How Long we Keep your Personal Data**\n\nYour Personal Data will be kept only as long as necessary for the purposes set out in this Privacy Notice and in accordance with IDB Invest’s applicable records retention and disposition schedules. The specific length of time will depend on the type of Personal Data, the reasons for which it is processed, and other obligations under IDB Invest’s policies and procedures.\n\n---\n\n###### **International Transfers of Personal Data**\n\nWhen you submit Personal Data to us by any means, that Personal Data may be transferred to a jurisdiction other than the one in which you live. In particular, Personal Data may be transferred to the United States. The data protection and other privacy laws of the United States may not afford the same level of protection as the laws of other countries.\n\n---\n\n###### **To whom we Disclose your Personal Data?**\n\nIDB Invest may disclose your Personal Data to the recipients described below, as reasonably necessary for the purposes outlined in this Privacy Notice.\n\n* IDB Group Institutions: We may disclose your Personal Data to other IDB Group institutions, such as the Inter-American Development Bank, as necessary for the purposes set out in this Privacy Notice.\n* Third parties: Unless otherwise noted below, and subject to contractually agreed conditions of confidentiality and security (where applicable), we may disclose your Personal Data to the categories of parties listed below:\n  + Service providers and suppliers who perform services, such as event vendors and organizers, consulting firms, among others, and providers that support compliance processes, including KYC screening and due diligence processes.\n  + Legal and other advisors that assist, advise or represent an IDB Group Institution as needed, such as attorneys, in connection with litigation, investigations, advising on contractual obligations, or enabling an IDB Group Institution to carry out its development mandate.\n  + Relevant legal, regulatory or administrative authorities, as we believe to be appropriate, for example, public registers involved in the execution and enforcement of relevant transaction documents, and other relevant authorities to protect and defend our rights and property, protect the interests of the IDB Group or others; or enable us to pursue available remedies or limit the damages that we may sustain; and,\n  + Other selected third parties: legal entities, including financial institutions, custodians, brokers, private companies, intermediaries, donors, partners and other organizations with which you are associated or involved (if any) in connection with our Products or Services; and peer researchers from academia, who carry out impact evaluations, among others.\n\nIDB Invest seeks to ensure that all partners and service providers processing Personal Data on its behalf implement appropriate technical and organizational safeguards to protect the privacy and security of such data.\n\n---\n\n###### **How to Request Information on your Personal Data Processed by IDB Invest**\n\nAs part of its data privacy framework, IDB Invest has established a procedure for individuals to request information regarding their Personal Data processed by IDB Invest and, when appropriate, to seek redress if they reasonably believe their Personal Data has not been processed in accordance with the IDB Group Personal Data Privacy Policy.\n\nYou may submit such a request using the webform [available here](https://forms.office.com/r/QAvQqSEBdy).\n\n---\n\n###### **How we Protect your Personal Data**\n\nWe have appropriate technical (e.g., firewalls, malware scans, anti-virus protection, encryption, physical locks) and organizational (e.g., policies and procedures, privacy assessments, due diligence, awareness, and training) safeguards in place to prevent unauthorized processing and accidental loss, damage, or destruction of Personal Data. These safeguards take into account the sensitivity of the data, as well as the current state of technology. We also have procedures in place to deal with data breaches, and we will notify you accordingly when appropriate.\n\n---\n\n###### **Changes to this Privacy Notice**\n\nThis Privacy Notice was last updated on the date listed above. If we change it, we will post the new version to this website.\n\n---\n\n###### **Queries and Complaints**\n\nIf you have any complaints or queries regarding your Personal Data, please contact [[email protected]](/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection#b0c0c2d9c6d1d3c9f0f9f4f2d9dec6d5c3c49edfc2d7).\n\n---\n\n###### **Privileges and Immunities**\n\nNothing contained in this Privacy Notice shall constitute or be considered to be a limitation upon or a waiver of the privileges and immunities of IDB Invest, which are specifically reserved.\n\n\n---\n\n# **<u>IDB GROUP PERSONAL DATA PRIVACY POLICY</u>**<sup>**1**</sup> \n\n# **I. PURPOSE AND APPLICATION** \n\nThis document sets out the Policy for the Processing of Personal Data by IDB Group Institutions. \n\nThis Policy applies to the Processing of Personal Data by, or on behalf of, IDB Group Institutions, and is intended to develop consistent practices across the IDB Group. \n\n# **II. DEFINITIONS** \n\nCapitalized terms or acronyms used in this Policy have the meaning set out below: \n\n**_1._ Board(s)** : the Boards of Executive Directors of IDB and IDB Invest, respectively. \n\n**_2._ Data Subject** : a natural, living person to whom Personal Data pertains, and whose Personal Data is Processed by an IDB Group Institution. Data Subjects may include, without limitation, any current or former: (i) IDB Group Institution staff member, director or their dependents; (ii) IDB Group Institution contractor or consultant; (iii) applicant for a vacancy at an IDB Group Institution; (iv) IDB Group Institution suppliers or vendors; (v) IDB Group Institution client or their representatives; (vi) respondents to IDB Group Institution surveys; or (vii) subscribers to an IDB Group Institution website. \n\n**_3._ IDB** : the Inter-American Development Bank. \n\n**_4._ IDB Group** : the Inter-American Development Bank Group. \n\n**_5._ IDB Group Institution** : any one of the IDB<sup>2</sup> and IDB Invest. \n\n**_6._ IDB Invest** : the Inter-American Investment Corporation. \n\n**_7._ Implementing Instruments** : has the meaning set forth in Section IV below. \n\n**_8._ Personal Data** : any information relating to an identified or identifiable Data Subject. An identifiable Data Subject is one who can be identified by reasonable means, directly or indirectly, by reference to an attribute or combination of attributes within the data, or combination of the data with other available information. Examples of attributes that can be used to identify an identifiable Data Subject include their name, identification number, location data, online identifier, metadata, and factors specific to their physical, physiological, genetic, mental, economic, cultural or social identity. \n\n**_9._ Policy** : this Personal Data Privacy Policy. \n\n**_10._ Principles** : the principles set out in Section III below. \n\n> 1 This Policy is not effective yet pursuant to Section IV below. \n\n> 2 The Multilateral Investment Fund (commercially known as IDB Lab) is a fund administered by the IDB and, therefore, any references to IDB Group Institution include IDB Lab.\n\n**_11._ Processing** : any action or set of actions, automated or not, which is performed on Personal Data, which may include, without limitation, its collection, recording, use, consultation, retrieval, disclosure by transmission, dissemination or otherwise making available, forwarding, organization, storage, structuring, adaptation or alteration, alignment or combination, restriction, erasure or destruction. \n\n**_12._ Processed** : having undertaken the act of Processing. \n\n**_13._ Third Party** or **Third Parties** : a legal person, other than IDB Group Institutions, or a natural person, other than IDB Group Institutions’ personnel and their dependents, as defined within their respective policies and procedures. \n\n# **III. PRINCIPLES** \n\nThe following Principles shall apply to all Processing of Personal Data by IDB Group Institutions: \n\n# **_1. Legitimate, Fair and Transparent Processing_** \n\nPersonal Data shall only be Processed for legitimate purposes and in a fair and transparent manner. Legitimate purposes for Processing mean any purpose: \n\n- a. for which the consent of a Data Subject is obtained, either at the time Personal Data are collected or subsequently; \n\n- b. that is in the vital or best interest of (i) the Data Subject or (ii) another person; \n\n- c. that is reasonably necessary for the performance of a contract; \n\n- d. that is reasonably necessary to enable an IDB Group Institution to satisfy an obligation or undertaking, or to comply with an IDB Group Institution’s policy or procedure; \n\n- e. that is reasonably necessary to establish, exercise or defend an IDB Group Institution’s right or interest; or \n\n- f. that is consistent with, or reasonably necessary to enable an IDB Group Institution to carry out its mission, mandate or purpose as an international organization established by its member countries. \n\n# **_2. Purpose Limitation_** \n\nPersonal Data shall be collected for one or more specific and legitimate purpose(s) listed in Principle 1 above and not further Processed in a manner that is incompatible with such purpose(s). Further Processing for archiving purposes, research, or statistical purposes shall not be considered incompatible with such purpose(s).\n\n# **_3. Data Minimization_** \n\nThe amount and type of Personal Data collected shall be reasonably necessary for, and proportionate to, the legitimate purpose(s) for which it is Processed. \n\n# **_4. Data Accuracy_** \n\nPersonal Data shall be recorded as accurately as possible and, where necessary, updated to fulfill the legitimate purpose(s) for which it is Processed. \n\n# **_5. Storage Limitation_** \n\nPersonal Data shall be kept in a form which permits identification of Data Subjects for no longer than is necessary for the legitimate purpose for which the Personal Data is collected, or for compatible further Processing, in accordance with this Policy. \n\n# **_6. Security_** \n\nPersonal Data shall be protected by appropriate and reasonable technical and organizational safeguards against unauthorized Processing and against accidental loss, destruction or damage. \n\n# **_7. Transfer of Personal Data_** \n\nPersonal Data shall only be transferred to a Third Party for legitimate purposes in accordance with this Policy and with appropriate regard for the protection of Personal Data. \n\n# **_8. Accountability and Review_** \n\nEach IDB Group Institution shall establish appropriate accountability and supervisory mechanism(s) to: \n\n- a) oversee compliance with this Policy: and \n\n- b) provide Data Subjects with a method, subject to reasonable limitations and conditions, to: \n\n   - i. request information regarding the Data Subject’s Personal Data Processed by or on behalf of such IDB Group Institution; and \n\n   - ii. seek redress if the Data Subject reasonably believes that the Data Subject’s Personal Data has been Processed in violation of this Policy. \n\n# **IV. MISCELLANEOUS** \n\n1. This Policy shall be implemented by each IDB Group Institution through guidelines, procedures, and other implementation measures, as applicable, tailored to each IDB Group Institution’s specific activities (the “ **Implementing Instruments** ”). \n\n2. This Policy shall become effective for each IDB Group Institution upon the earlier to occur of the following: (i) a declaration of effectiveness by the President of the IDB, in the case of the IDB, and the General Manager of IDB Invest, in the case of the IDB Invest, or such representative as each shall designate, to be issued upon adoption and effectiveness of Implementing Instruments; and (ii) three years from the date of approval of this Policy by the respective Board. \n\n3. This Policy shall not cover Personal Data collected before its effectiveness.\n\n4. The Processing of Personal Data in accordance with this Policy is without prejudice to the privileges and immunities of the IDB Group Institutions, which privileges and immunities are specifically reserved.\n\n---\n\n[Skip to main content](#main-content)\n\n\n*Last updated on: March 18, 2026*\n\n###### **Overview**\n\nThe Inter-American Investment Corporation (“IDB Invest”, “we”, “us” and “our”) is an international organization founded by international treaty in 1986 and is a member of the Inter-American Development Bank Group (“IDB Group”). As such, it is not subject to any national or supranational laws.\n\nThis Privacy Notice (“Privacy Notice”) explains how IDB Invest collects, uses, stores, transfers or otherwise processes the Personal Data of individuals (other than our own personnel and their dependents) (“you”). For the purposes of this Privacy Notice, Personal Data means any information relating to an identified or identifiable individual, such as a person’s name, contact details, location data, or factors relating to their physical, economic, cultural or social identity, or any other information that may reasonably be linked to that individual.\n\nIf you are either (i) the direct or indirect beneficiary of IDB Invest [Products and Services](https://idbinvest.org/en/solutions), or (ii) a representative of, or otherwise associated with, businesses and other organizations currently or potentially benefiting from or participating in IDB Invest’s [Products or Services](https://idbinvest.org/en/solutions) (for example, employees, officers, shareholders, directors, beneficial owners, guarantors or key vendors or partners of such businesses or organizations), this Privacy Notice applies to the processing of your Personal Data.\n\nPersonal data is processed by IDB Invest in accordance with the [IDB Group Personal Data Privacy Policy](https://idbinvest.org/sites/default/files/2022-11/IDB%20Group%20Personal%20Data%20Privacy%20Policy.pdf) (the “Privacy Policy”). Such processing enables IDB Invest to carry out its mission, mandate and purpose as an international organization established by its member countries.\n\nPlease ensure that you read this Privacy Notice in its entirety, as amended from time to time.\n\n---\n\n###### **What Does this Privacy Notice Cover?**\n\nThis Privacy Notice relates to the Personal Data we collect and process from you, and covers the following aspects:\n\n(Click on the topic you want to read)\n\n* [The contexts in which we process your Personal Data;](#1)\n* [The types of Personal Data that we process about you;](#2)\n* [The sources from which IDB Invest obtain your Personal Data;](#3)\n* [How and why IDB Invest processes your Personal Data;](#4)\n* [How long we keep your Personal Data;](#5)\n* [How, why and to whom we transfer your Personal Data;](#6)\n* [How we protect your Personal Data;](#7)\n* [Changes to this Privacy Notice;](#8)\n* [Explains the application of our privileges and immunities;](#9) and\n* [Explains how you may contact us with queries or complaints.](#10)\n\n---\n\n###### **The Contexts in Which we Process your Personal Data**\n\nThe Personal Data processing activities we undertake will vary based on your relationship with IDB Invest.\n\n**I. Visitors to IDB Invest’s websites**\n\nIDB Invest does not automatically process Personal Data related to the visitors of its website, e.g. idbinvest.org, or official IDB Invest pages on other platforms. However, we will process Personal Data that you submit through any interface of the official websites (for example, when registering for an event). This Privacy Notice does not apply to third party websites. We encourage you to review the privacy notices of any third-party websites you visit.\n\n**II. Subscribers of IDB Invest newsletters or publications**\n\nIf you subscribe to an IDB Invest newsletter or publication, we process your Personal Data (for example, your name and e-mail address) so we can make sure that you receive it.\n\n**III. Registered attendees of IDB Invest events**\n\nIf you register to attend an IDB Invest event, we collect and process your Personal Data in connection with the organization and management of the event.\n\n**IV. Personal Data processed in the course of providing our Products and Services**\n\nIn the course of providing our Products and Services IDB Invest processes Personal Data.\n\n**V. Personal Data in the context of recruitment**\n\nPersonal Data is required to manage job applications and recruitment processes. For detailed information, please refer to the privacy notice provided to job applicants during the application process ([available here](https://www.iadb.org/en/terms-conditions-and-notices/privacy-notice/job-applicant-privacy-notice)).\n\n**VI. Personal Data in the context of procurement**\n\nIn the course of providing our procurement activities, IDB Invest processes Personal Data.\n\n**VII. Business planning, client strategy, communications and analytics activities**\n\nIf you engage with IDB Invest as a business contact, prospective client, or external stakeholder (for example, through meetings, conferences, or professional networking), we may process your Personal Data for business development, client engagement, and institutional communications purposes.\n\n---\n\n###### **What Personal Data do we Process?**\n\nWe may collect and process the following Personal Data about you:\n\n* **Identification and contact data –** name, postal address(es), email address, phone number(s), signature specimen, passport/nationality identity documents (including embedded photographs), age and date of birth, citizenship status, office location, and limited biometric identifiers used for identity verification or security purposes;\n* **Operations data –** information about your involvement in, and/or the development impact on you of, our investment and advisory operations and activities;\n* **Financial data –** relevant financial information of how you benefit directly or indirectly from our Products and Services;\n* **Background data –** relevant background information used for anti-corruption and anti-fraud assessments in accordance with our applicable policies and procedures;\n* **Professional data –** job title, employer details or organizational affiliation, photograph in your CV, professional history, qualification details, information about your experience, participation in meetings, seminars, and conferences, information about your professional relationship with other individuals or institutions, language abilities, and other professional skills;\n* **Correspondence –** records of any correspondence we may have with you, records of your correspondence preferences (including subscription to our newsletters);\n* **Consent records –** records of preferences and permissions you provide to us, including records of consent opt-in/opt-out choices, where applicable. When maintained, such records are used solely to demonstrate compliance with applicable legal, contractual or governance obligations and to respect your stated preferences;\n* **Data relating to our websites –** technical data (device type, operating system, browser type and settings, IP address, language settings), usage and behavioral data, connection information (dates, times, location), analytics, and aggregate statistical information.\n* **Diversity and inclusion data –** salutations, gender identity, race / ethnicity, disability status;\n\nIn limited circumstances, IDB Invest may process special categories of Personal Data, such as information relating to an individual’s health, racial or ethnic origin, or other similarly sensitive characteristics. Such data will be processed only where strictly necessary and in accordance with applicable institutional policies and will be subject to enhanced safeguards designed to ensure an appropriate level of protection for the confidentiality, integrity, and security of the Personal Data.\n\n---\n\n###### **Where we Obtain your Personal Data?**\n\nWe may obtain or receive Personal Data about you from the following sources:\n\n* **Personal Data you or your employer provide to us –** Personal Data provided directly by you (e.g., job applications, correspondence you send us, information you provide to our investment officers, or when you complete an online form or survey), or that is provided to us by your employer or other organization with which you are associated, and information collected during meetings, events, and business interactions.\n* **Personal Data we collect by automated means –** As noted above, we may obtain certain information by automated means when you visit our websites.\n* **Personal Data we collect from third parties –** We may collect or obtain Personal Data from third parties (e.g., counterparties to a transaction, law enforcement authorities, relevant business contacts, specialized databases operated by the private sector, specialized external service providers, consultants or vendors).\n* **Personal Data you make public –** We may collect or obtain Personal Data that you manifestly choose to make public, including via social media (e.g., we may collect information from your social media profile(s), if you make a public post about us).\n\n---\n\n###### **Why we Process your Personal Data?**\n\nIDB Invest processes your Personal Data as reasonably necessary to conduct and manage our activities within the contexts listed above. This includes processing Personal Data for any of the following purposes:\n\n**I. To carry out IDB Invest’s investment, advisory and asset management activities**\n\n* Exploring investment opportunities and conducting due diligence;\n* Executing legal instruments related to investment, advisory and asset management activities;\n* Administering and managing our relationships with counterparties (and potential counterparties) in the context of our investment, advisory and asset management activities (or potential activities that may be of interest);\n* Understanding and monitoring the development impact of our activities;\n* Investigating and responding to complaints, and establishing, exercising, or defending IDB Invest’s legal rights and obligations;\n* Coordinating with other IDB Group Institutions; and,\n* Supporting equality, diversity and inclusion in our projects.\n\n**II. To comply with legal and policy obligations and manage risk**\n\n* Performing internal governance functions;\n* Conducting accounting and financial management;\n* Maintaining appropriate accounting, financial management and other records;\n* Fulfill our policy obligations, confirming and verifying your identity, and screening against government and/or law enforcement agency sanctions lists and other legal restrictions;\n* Carrying out our obligations, and exercising our rights, under applicable legal or regulatory requirements and any contracts entered into between you and IDB Invest;\n* Conducting credit and other risk assessment and control activities, including for the prevention and detection of corruption and fraud; and,\n* Training our staff and maintaining and improving the quality of our internal processes and arrangements.\n\n**III. To manage communications, stakeholder engagement and business development**\n\n* Disseminating information to further IDB Invest’s mission to improve lives in Latin America and the Caribbean, and providing research information;\n* Responding to your queries and feedback (for example, if you have asked a question or submitted feedback through our website);\n* Providing you with information, products or services you have requested or that may be of interest to you, unless you tell us otherwise; and,\n* Conducting business intelligence operations; and conducting business planning and client strategy activities, including organizing and managing events for clients and potential clients; conducting business analysis, planning and monitoring; preparing and disseminating marketing, institutional and business communications; defining communications strategies, guidelines and mechanisms; developing and communicating plans, strategies, strategic initiatives and updates to internal and external stakeholders; understanding client behavior through analytics to design and enhance client experiences; conducting impact evaluations and other in-depth studies (which may include surveys with project beneficiaries and other stakeholders); and supporting business development and client engagement initiatives.\n\n**IV. In connection with the management of IDB Invest’s websites, data analytics and IT security**\n\n* Providing access, maintaining and improving our websites and services;\n* Enabling you to participate in any interactive features of our websites and communicating with you, including through our newsletter, subject to your preferences;\n* Presenting website content in a manner suitable for the device you are accessing it from Undertaking data analytics to understand how users interact with our websites and online public-facing materials;\n* Monitoring and analyzing the use of our products and services for purposes of developing and improving them;\n* Managing and ensuring the security of our IT systems, including detecting and preventing misuse or abuse of our websites and services, and for backup and disaster recovery purposes; and,\n* We may also process Personal Data for any other purpose described to you at the time your data is collected.\n\nWe may also collect and process Personal Data of visitors to our premises, including for the purposes of ensuring safety and security at those premises, as further detailed in the notices available at our premises.\n\n---\n\n###### **How Long we Keep your Personal Data**\n\nYour Personal Data will be kept only as long as necessary for the purposes set out in this Privacy Notice and in accordance with IDB Invest’s applicable records retention and disposition schedules. The specific length of time will depend on the type of Personal Data, the reasons for which it is processed, and other obligations under IDB Invest’s policies and procedures.\n\n---\n\n###### **International Transfers of Personal Data**\n\nWhen you submit Personal Data to us by any means, that Personal Data may be transferred to a jurisdiction other than the one in which you live. In particular, Personal Data may be transferred to the United States. The data protection and other privacy laws of the United States may not afford the same level of protection as the laws of other countries.\n\n---\n\n###### **To whom we Disclose your Personal Data?**\n\nIDB Invest may disclose your Personal Data to the recipients described below, as reasonably necessary for the purposes outlined in this Privacy Notice.\n\n* IDB Group Institutions: We may disclose your Personal Data to other IDB Group institutions, such as the Inter-American Development Bank, as necessary for the purposes set out in this Privacy Notice.\n* Third parties: Unless otherwise noted below, and subject to contractually agreed conditions of confidentiality and security (where applicable), we may disclose your Personal Data to the categories of parties listed below:\n  + Service providers and suppliers who perform services, such as event vendors and organizers, consulting firms, among others, and providers that support compliance processes, including KYC screening and due diligence processes.\n  + Legal and other advisors that assist, advise or represent an IDB Group Institution as needed, such as attorneys, in connection with litigation, investigations, advising on contractual obligations, or enabling an IDB Group Institution to carry out its development mandate.\n  + Relevant legal, regulatory or administrative authorities, as we believe to be appropriate, for example, public registers involved in the execution and enforcement of relevant transaction documents, and other relevant authorities to protect and defend our rights and property, protect the interests of the IDB Group or others; or enable us to pursue available remedies or limit the damages that we may sustain; and,\n  + Other selected third parties: legal entities, including financial institutions, custodians, brokers, private companies, intermediaries, donors, partners and other organizations with which you are associated or involved (if any) in connection with our Products or Services; and peer researchers from academia, who carry out impact evaluations, among others.\n\nIDB Invest seeks to ensure that all partners and service providers processing Personal Data on its behalf implement appropriate technical and organizational safeguards to protect the privacy and security of such data.\n\n---\n\n###### **How to Request Information on your Personal Data Processed by IDB Invest**\n\nAs part of its data privacy framework, IDB Invest has established a procedure for individuals to request information regarding their Personal Data processed by IDB Invest and, when appropriate, to seek redress if they reasonably believe their Personal Data has not been processed in accordance with the IDB Group Personal Data Privacy Policy.\n\nYou may submit such a request using the webform [available here](https://forms.office.com/r/QAvQqSEBdy).\n\n---\n\n###### **How we Protect your Personal Data**\n\nWe have appropriate technical (e.g., firewalls, malware scans, anti-virus protection, encryption, physical locks) and organizational (e.g., policies and procedures, privacy assessments, due diligence, awareness, and training) safeguards in place to prevent unauthorized processing and accidental loss, damage, or destruction of Personal Data. These safeguards take into account the sensitivity of the data, as well as the current state of technology. We also have procedures in place to deal with data breaches, and we will notify you accordingly when appropriate.\n\n---\n\n###### **Changes to this Privacy Notice**\n\nThis Privacy Notice was last updated on the date listed above. If we change it, we will post the new version to this website.\n\n---\n\n###### **Queries and Complaints**\n\nIf you have any complaints or queries regarding your Personal Data, please contact [[email protected]](/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection#b0c0c2d9c6d1d3c9f0f9f4f2d9dec6d5c3c49edfc2d7).\n\n---\n\n###### **Privileges and Immunities**\n\nNothing contained in this Privacy Notice shall constitute or be considered to be a limitation upon or a waiver of the privileges and immunities of IDB Invest, which are specifically reserved.\n\n\n---\n\n# **<u>IDB GROUP PERSONAL DATA PRIVACY POLICY</u>**<sup>**1**</sup> \n\n# **I. PURPOSE AND APPLICATION** \n\nThis document sets out the Policy for the Processing of Personal Data by IDB Group Institutions. \n\nThis Policy applies to the Processing of Personal Data by, or on behalf of, IDB Group Institutions, and is intended to develop consistent practices across the IDB Group. \n\n# **II. DEFINITIONS** \n\nCapitalized terms or acronyms used in this Policy have the meaning set out below: \n\n**_1._ Board(s)** : the Boards of Executive Directors of IDB and IDB Invest, respectively. \n\n**_2._ Data Subject** : a natural, living person to whom Personal Data pertains, and whose Personal Data is Processed by an IDB Group Institution. Data Subjects may include, without limitation, any current or former: (i) IDB Group Institution staff member, director or their dependents; (ii) IDB Group Institution contractor or consultant; (iii) applicant for a vacancy at an IDB Group Institution; (iv) IDB Group Institution suppliers or vendors; (v) IDB Group Institution client or their representatives; (vi) respondents to IDB Group Institution surveys; or (vii) subscribers to an IDB Group Institution website. \n\n**_3._ IDB** : the Inter-American Development Bank. \n\n**_4._ IDB Group** : the Inter-American Development Bank Group. \n\n**_5._ IDB Group Institution** : any one of the IDB<sup>2</sup> and IDB Invest. \n\n**_6._ IDB Invest** : the Inter-American Investment Corporation. \n\n**_7._ Implementing Instruments** : has the meaning set forth in Section IV below. \n\n**_8._ Personal Data** : any information relating to an identified or identifiable Data Subject. An identifiable Data Subject is one who can be identified by reasonable means, directly or indirectly, by reference to an attribute or combination of attributes within the data, or combination of the data with other available information. Examples of attributes that can be used to identify an identifiable Data Subject include their name, identification number, location data, online identifier, metadata, and factors specific to their physical, physiological, genetic, mental, economic, cultural or social identity. \n\n**_9._ Policy** : this Personal Data Privacy Policy. \n\n**_10._ Principles** : the principles set out in Section III below. \n\n> 1 This Policy is not effective yet pursuant to Section IV below. \n\n> 2 The Multilateral Investment Fund (commercially known as IDB Lab) is a fund administered by the IDB and, therefore, any references to IDB Group Institution include IDB Lab.\n\n**_11._ Processing** : any action or set of actions, automated or not, which is performed on Personal Data, which may include, without limitation, its collection, recording, use, consultation, retrieval, disclosure by transmission, dissemination or otherwise making available, forwarding, organization, storage, structuring, adaptation or alteration, alignment or combination, restriction, erasure or destruction. \n\n**_12._ Processed** : having undertaken the act of Processing. \n\n**_13._ Third Party** or **Third Parties** : a legal person, other than IDB Group Institutions, or a natural person, other than IDB Group Institutions’ personnel and their dependents, as defined within their respective policies and procedures. \n\n# **III. PRINCIPLES** \n\nThe following Principles shall apply to all Processing of Personal Data by IDB Group Institutions: \n\n# **_1. Legitimate, Fair and Transparent Processing_** \n\nPersonal Data shall only be Processed for legitimate purposes and in a fair and transparent manner. Legitimate purposes for Processing mean any purpose: \n\n- a. for which the consent of a Data Subject is obtained, either at the time Personal Data are collected or subsequently; \n\n- b. that is in the vital or best interest of (i) the Data Subject or (ii) another person; \n\n- c. that is reasonably necessary for the performance of a contract; \n\n- d. that is reasonably necessary to enable an IDB Group Institution to satisfy an obligation or undertaking, or to comply with an IDB Group Institution’s policy or procedure; \n\n- e. that is reasonably necessary to establish, exercise or defend an IDB Group Institution’s right or interest; or \n\n- f. that is consistent with, or reasonably necessary to enable an IDB Group Institution to carry out its mission, mandate or purpose as an international organization established by its member countries. \n\n# **_2. Purpose Limitation_** \n\nPersonal Data shall be collected for one or more specific and legitimate purpose(s) listed in Principle 1 above and not further Processed in a manner that is incompatible with such purpose(s). Further Processing for archiving purposes, research, or statistical purposes shall not be considered incompatible with such purpose(s).\n\n# **_3. Data Minimization_** \n\nThe amount and type of Personal Data collected shall be reasonably necessary for, and proportionate to, the legitimate purpose(s) for which it is Processed. \n\n# **_4. Data Accuracy_** \n\nPersonal Data shall be recorded as accurately as possible and, where necessary, updated to fulfill the legitimate purpose(s) for which it is Processed. \n\n# **_5. Storage Limitation_** \n\nPersonal Data shall be kept in a form which permits identification of Data Subjects for no longer than is necessary for the legitimate purpose for which the Personal Data is collected, or for compatible further Processing, in accordance with this Policy. \n\n# **_6. Security_** \n\nPersonal Data shall be protected by appropriate and reasonable technical and organizational safeguards against unauthorized Processing and against accidental loss, destruction or damage. \n\n# **_7. Transfer of Personal Data_** \n\nPersonal Data shall only be transferred to a Third Party for legitimate purposes in accordance with this Policy and with appropriate regard for the protection of Personal Data. \n\n# **_8. Accountability and Review_** \n\nEach IDB Group Institution shall establish appropriate accountability and supervisory mechanism(s) to: \n\n- a) oversee compliance with this Policy: and \n\n- b) provide Data Subjects with a method, subject to reasonable limitations and conditions, to: \n\n   - i. request information regarding the Data Subject’s Personal Data Processed by or on behalf of such IDB Group Institution; and \n\n   - ii. seek redress if the Data Subject reasonably believes that the Data Subject’s Personal Data has been Processed in violation of this Policy. \n\n# **IV. MISCELLANEOUS** \n\n1. This Policy shall be implemented by each IDB Group Institution through guidelines, procedures, and other implementation measures, as applicable, tailored to each IDB Group Institution’s specific activities (the “ **Implementing Instruments** ”). \n\n2. This Policy shall become effective for each IDB Group Institution upon the earlier to occur of the following: (i) a declaration of effectiveness by the President of the IDB, in the case of the IDB, and the General Manager of IDB Invest, in the case of the IDB Invest, or such representative as each shall designate, to be issued upon adoption and effectiveness of Implementing Instruments; and (ii) three years from the date of approval of this Policy by the respective Board. \n\n3. This Policy shall not cover Personal Data collected before its effectiveness.\n\n4. The Processing of Personal Data in accordance with this Policy is without prejudice to the privileges and immunities of the IDB Group Institutions, which privileges and immunities are specifically reserved.\n\n---\n\n[Skip to main content](#main-content)\n\n\n*Last updated on: March 18, 2026*\n\n###### **Overview**\n\nThe Inter-American Investment Corporation (“IDB Invest”, “we”, “us” and “our”) is an international organization founded by international treaty in 1986 and is a member of the Inter-American Development Bank Group (“IDB Group”). As such, it is not subject to any national or supranational laws.\n\nThis Privacy Notice (“Privacy Notice”) explains how IDB Invest collects, uses, stores, transfers or otherwise processes the Personal Data of individuals (other than our own personnel and their dependents) (“you”). For the purposes of this Privacy Notice, Personal Data means any information relating to an identified or identifiable individual, such as a person’s name, contact details, location data, or factors relating to their physical, economic, cultural or social identity, or any other information that may reasonably be linked to that individual.\n\nIf you are either (i) the direct or indirect beneficiary of IDB Invest [Products and Services](https://idbinvest.org/en/solutions), or (ii) a representative of, or otherwise associated with, businesses and other organizations currently or potentially benefiting from or participating in IDB Invest’s [Products or Services](https://idbinvest.org/en/solutions) (for example, employees, officers, shareholders, directors, beneficial owners, guarantors or key vendors or partners of such businesses or organizations), this Privacy Notice applies to the processing of your Personal Data.\n\nPersonal data is processed by IDB Invest in accordance with the [IDB Group Personal Data Privacy Policy](https://idbinvest.org/sites/default/files/2022-11/IDB%20Group%20Personal%20Data%20Privacy%20Policy.pdf) (the “Privacy Policy”). Such processing enables IDB Invest to carry out its mission, mandate and purpose as an international organization established by its member countries.\n\nPlease ensure that you read this Privacy Notice in its entirety, as amended from time to time.\n\n---\n\n###### **What Does this Privacy Notice Cover?**\n\nThis Privacy Notice relates to the Personal Data we collect and process from you, and covers the following aspects:\n\n(Click on the topic you want to read)\n\n* [The contexts in which we process your Personal Data;](#1)\n* [The types of Personal Data that we process about you;](#2)\n* [The sources from which IDB Invest obtain your Personal Data;](#3)\n* [How and why IDB Invest processes your Personal Data;](#4)\n* [How long we keep your Personal Data;](#5)\n* [How, why and to whom we transfer your Personal Data;](#6)\n* [How we protect your Personal Data;](#7)\n* [Changes to this Privacy Notice;](#8)\n* [Explains the application of our privileges and immunities;](#9) and\n* [Explains how you may contact us with queries or complaints.](#10)\n\n---\n\n###### **The Contexts in Which we Process your Personal Data**\n\nThe Personal Data processing activities we undertake will vary based on your relationship with IDB Invest.\n\n**I. Visitors to IDB Invest’s websites**\n\nIDB Invest does not automatically process Personal Data related to the visitors of its website, e.g. idbinvest.org, or official IDB Invest pages on other platforms. However, we will process Personal Data that you submit through any interface of the official websites (for example, when registering for an event). This Privacy Notice does not apply to third party websites. We encourage you to review the privacy notices of any third-party websites you visit.\n\n**II. Subscribers of IDB Invest newsletters or publications**\n\nIf you subscribe to an IDB Invest newsletter or publication, we process your Personal Data (for example, your name and e-mail address) so we can make sure that you receive it.\n\n**III. Registered attendees of IDB Invest events**\n\nIf you register to attend an IDB Invest event, we collect and process your Personal Data in connection with the organization and management of the event.\n\n**IV. Personal Data processed in the course of providing our Products and Services**\n\nIn the course of providing our Products and Services IDB Invest processes Personal Data.\n\n**V. Personal Data in the context of recruitment**\n\nPersonal Data is required to manage job applications and recruitment processes. For detailed information, please refer to the privacy notice provided to job applicants during the application process ([available here](https://www.iadb.org/en/terms-conditions-and-notices/privacy-notice/job-applicant-privacy-notice)).\n\n**VI. Personal Data in the context of procurement**\n\nIn the course of providing our procurement activities, IDB Invest processes Personal Data.\n\n**VII. Business planning, client strategy, communications and analytics activities**\n\nIf you engage with IDB Invest as a business contact, prospective client, or external stakeholder (for example, through meetings, conferences, or professional networking), we may process your Personal Data for business development, client engagement, and institutional communications purposes.\n\n---\n\n###### **What Personal Data do we Process?**\n\nWe may collect and process the following Personal Data about you:\n\n* **Identification and contact data –** name, postal address(es), email address, phone number(s), signature specimen, passport/nationality identity documents (including embedded photographs), age and date of birth, citizenship status, office location, and limited biometric identifiers used for identity verification or security purposes;\n* **Operations data –** information about your involvement in, and/or the development impact on you of, our investment and advisory operations and activities;\n* **Financial data –** relevant financial information of how you benefit directly or indirectly from our Products and Services;\n* **Background data –** relevant background information used for anti-corruption and anti-fraud assessments in accordance with our applicable policies and procedures;\n* **Professional data –** job title, employer details or organizational affiliation, photograph in your CV, professional history, qualification details, information about your experience, participation in meetings, seminars, and conferences, information about your professional relationship with other individuals or institutions, language abilities, and other professional skills;\n* **Correspondence –** records of any correspondence we may have with you, records of your correspondence preferences (including subscription to our newsletters);\n* **Consent records –** records of preferences and permissions you provide to us, including records of consent opt-in/opt-out choices, where applicable. When maintained, such records are used solely to demonstrate compliance with applicable legal, contractual or governance obligations and to respect your stated preferences;\n* **Data relating to our websites –** technical data (device type, operating system, browser type and settings, IP address, language settings), usage and behavioral data, connection information (dates, times, location), analytics, and aggregate statistical information.\n* **Diversity and inclusion data –** salutations, gender identity, race / ethnicity, disability status;\n\nIn limited circumstances, IDB Invest may process special categories of Personal Data, such as information relating to an individual’s health, racial or ethnic origin, or other similarly sensitive characteristics. Such data will be processed only where strictly necessary and in accordance with applicable institutional policies and will be subject to enhanced safeguards designed to ensure an appropriate level of protection for the confidentiality, integrity, and security of the Personal Data.\n\n---\n\n###### **Where we Obtain your Personal Data?**\n\nWe may obtain or receive Personal Data about you from the following sources:\n\n* **Personal Data you or your employer provide to us –** Personal Data provided directly by you (e.g., job applications, correspondence you send us, information you provide to our investment officers, or when you complete an online form or survey), or that is provided to us by your employer or other organization with which you are associated, and information collected during meetings, events, and business interactions.\n* **Personal Data we collect by automated means –** As noted above, we may obtain certain information by automated means when you visit our websites.\n* **Personal Data we collect from third parties –** We may collect or obtain Personal Data from third parties (e.g., counterparties to a transaction, law enforcement authorities, relevant business contacts, specialized databases operated by the private sector, specialized external service providers, consultants or vendors).\n* **Personal Data you make public –** We may collect or obtain Personal Data that you manifestly choose to make public, including via social media (e.g., we may collect information from your social media profile(s), if you make a public post about us).\n\n---\n\n###### **Why we Process your Personal Data?**\n\nIDB Invest processes your Personal Data as reasonably necessary to conduct and manage our activities within the contexts listed above. This includes processing Personal Data for any of the following purposes:\n\n**I. To carry out IDB Invest’s investment, advisory and asset management activities**\n\n* Exploring investment opportunities and conducting due diligence;\n* Executing legal instruments related to investment, advisory and asset management activities;\n* Administering and managing our relationships with counterparties (and potential counterparties) in the context of our investment, advisory and asset management activities (or potential activities that may be of interest);\n* Understanding and monitoring the development impact of our activities;\n* Investigating and responding to complaints, and establishing, exercising, or defending IDB Invest’s legal rights and obligations;\n* Coordinating with other IDB Group Institutions; and,\n* Supporting equality, diversity and inclusion in our projects.\n\n**II. To comply with legal and policy obligations and manage risk**\n\n* Performing internal governance functions;\n* Conducting accounting and financial management;\n* Maintaining appropriate accounting, financial management and other records;\n* Fulfill our policy obligations, confirming and verifying your identity, and screening against government and/or law enforcement agency sanctions lists and other legal restrictions;\n* Carrying out our obligations, and exercising our rights, under applicable legal or regulatory requirements and any contracts entered into between you and IDB Invest;\n* Conducting credit and other risk assessment and control activities, including for the prevention and detection of corruption and fraud; and,\n* Training our staff and maintaining and improving the quality of our internal processes and arrangements.\n\n**III. To manage communications, stakeholder engagement and business development**\n\n* Disseminating information to further IDB Invest’s mission to improve lives in Latin America and the Caribbean, and providing research information;\n* Responding to your queries and feedback (for example, if you have asked a question or submitted feedback through our website);\n* Providing you with information, products or services you have requested or that may be of interest to you, unless you tell us otherwise; and,\n* Conducting business intelligence operations; and conducting business planning and client strategy activities, including organizing and managing events for clients and potential clients; conducting business analysis, planning and monitoring; preparing and disseminating marketing, institutional and business communications; defining communications strategies, guidelines and mechanisms; developing and communicating plans, strategies, strategic initiatives and updates to internal and external stakeholders; understanding client behavior through analytics to design and enhance client experiences; conducting impact evaluations and other in-depth studies (which may include surveys with project beneficiaries and other stakeholders); and supporting business development and client engagement initiatives.\n\n**IV. In connection with the management of IDB Invest’s websites, data analytics and IT security**\n\n* Providing access, maintaining and improving our websites and services;\n* Enabling you to participate in any interactive features of our websites and communicating with you, including through our newsletter, subject to your preferences;\n* Presenting website content in a manner suitable for the device you are accessing it from Undertaking data analytics to understand how users interact with our websites and online public-facing materials;\n* Monitoring and analyzing the use of our products and services for purposes of developing and improving them;\n* Managing and ensuring the security of our IT systems, including detecting and preventing misuse or abuse of our websites and services, and for backup and disaster recovery purposes; and,\n* We may also process Personal Data for any other purpose described to you at the time your data is collected.\n\nWe may also collect and process Personal Data of visitors to our premises, including for the purposes of ensuring safety and security at those premises, as further detailed in the notices available at our premises.\n\n---\n\n###### **How Long we Keep your Personal Data**\n\nYour Personal Data will be kept only as long as necessary for the purposes set out in this Privacy Notice and in accordance with IDB Invest’s applicable records retention and disposition schedules. The specific length of time will depend on the type of Personal Data, the reasons for which it is processed, and other obligations under IDB Invest’s policies and procedures.\n\n---\n\n###### **International Transfers of Personal Data**\n\nWhen you submit Personal Data to us by any means, that Personal Data may be transferred to a jurisdiction other than the one in which you live. In particular, Personal Data may be transferred to the United States. The data protection and other privacy laws of the United States may not afford the same level of protection as the laws of other countries.\n\n---\n\n###### **To whom we Disclose your Personal Data?**\n\nIDB Invest may disclose your Personal Data to the recipients described below, as reasonably necessary for the purposes outlined in this Privacy Notice.\n\n* IDB Group Institutions: We may disclose your Personal Data to other IDB Group institutions, such as the Inter-American Development Bank, as necessary for the purposes set out in this Privacy Notice.\n* Third parties: Unless otherwise noted below, and subject to contractually agreed conditions of confidentiality and security (where applicable), we may disclose your Personal Data to the categories of parties listed below:\n  + Service providers and suppliers who perform services, such as event vendors and organizers, consulting firms, among others, and providers that support compliance processes, including KYC screening and due diligence processes.\n  + Legal and other advisors that assist, advise or represent an IDB Group Institution as needed, such as attorneys, in connection with litigation, investigations, advising on contractual obligations, or enabling an IDB Group Institution to carry out its development mandate.\n  + Relevant legal, regulatory or administrative authorities, as we believe to be appropriate, for example, public registers involved in the execution and enforcement of relevant transaction documents, and other relevant authorities to protect and defend our rights and property, protect the interests of the IDB Group or others; or enable us to pursue available remedies or limit the damages that we may sustain; and,\n  + Other selected third parties: legal entities, including financial institutions, custodians, brokers, private companies, intermediaries, donors, partners and other organizations with which you are associated or involved (if any) in connection with our Products or Services; and peer researchers from academia, who carry out impact evaluations, among others.\n\nIDB Invest seeks to ensure that all partners and service providers processing Personal Data on its behalf implement appropriate technical and organizational safeguards to protect the privacy and security of such data.\n\n---\n\n###### **How to Request Information on your Personal Data Processed by IDB Invest**\n\nAs part of its data privacy framework, IDB Invest has established a procedure for individuals to request information regarding their Personal Data processed by IDB Invest and, when appropriate, to seek redress if they reasonably believe their Personal Data has not been processed in accordance with the IDB Group Personal Data Privacy Policy.\n\nYou may submit such a request using the webform [available here](https://forms.office.com/r/QAvQqSEBdy).\n\n---\n\n###### **How we Protect your Personal Data**\n\nWe have appropriate technical (e.g., firewalls, malware scans, anti-virus protection, encryption, physical locks) and organizational (e.g., policies and procedures, privacy assessments, due diligence, awareness, and training) safeguards in place to prevent unauthorized processing and accidental loss, damage, or destruction of Personal Data. These safeguards take into account the sensitivity of the data, as well as the current state of technology. We also have procedures in place to deal with data breaches, and we will notify you accordingly when appropriate.\n\n---\n\n###### **Changes to this Privacy Notice**\n\nThis Privacy Notice was last updated on the date listed above. If we change it, we will post the new version to this website.\n\n---\n\n###### **Queries and Complaints**\n\nIf you have any complaints or queries regarding your Personal Data, please contact [[email protected]](/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection#b0c0c2d9c6d1d3c9f0f9f4f2d9dec6d5c3c49edfc2d7).\n\n---\n\n###### **Privileges and Immunities**\n\nNothing contained in this Privacy Notice shall constitute or be considered to be a limitation upon or a waiver of the privileges and immunities of IDB Invest, which are specifically reserved.\n\n\n---\n\n# **<u>IDB GROUP PERSONAL DATA PRIVACY POLICY</u>**<sup>**1**</sup> \n\n# **I. PURPOSE AND APPLICATION** \n\nThis document sets out the Policy for the Processing of Personal Data by IDB Group Institutions. \n\nThis Policy applies to the Processing of Personal Data by, or on behalf of, IDB Group Institutions, and is intended to develop consistent practices across the IDB Group. \n\n# **II. DEFINITIONS** \n\nCapitalized terms or acronyms used in this Policy have the meaning set out below: \n\n**_1._ Board(s)** : the Boards of Executive Directors of IDB and IDB Invest, respectively. \n\n**_2._ Data Subject** : a natural, living person to whom Personal Data pertains, and whose Personal Data is Processed by an IDB Group Institution. Data Subjects may include, without limitation, any current or former: (i) IDB Group Institution staff member, director or their dependents; (ii) IDB Group Institution contractor or consultant; (iii) applicant for a vacancy at an IDB Group Institution; (iv) IDB Group Institution suppliers or vendors; (v) IDB Group Institution client or their representatives; (vi) respondents to IDB Group Institution surveys; or (vii) subscribers to an IDB Group Institution website. \n\n**_3._ IDB** : the Inter-American Development Bank. \n\n**_4._ IDB Group** : the Inter-American Development Bank Group. \n\n**_5._ IDB Group Institution** : any one of the IDB<sup>2</sup> and IDB Invest. \n\n**_6._ IDB Invest** : the Inter-American Investment Corporation. \n\n**_7._ Implementing Instruments** : has the meaning set forth in Section IV below. \n\n**_8._ Personal Data** : any information relating to an identified or identifiable Data Subject. An identifiable Data Subject is one who can be identified by reasonable means, directly or indirectly, by reference to an attribute or combination of attributes within the data, or combination of the data with other available information. Examples of attributes that can be used to identify an identifiable Data Subject include their name, identification number, location data, online identifier, metadata, and factors specific to their physical, physiological, genetic, mental, economic, cultural or social identity. \n\n**_9._ Policy** : this Personal Data Privacy Policy. \n\n**_10._ Principles** : the principles set out in Section III below. \n\n> 1 This Policy is not effective yet pursuant to Section IV below. \n\n> 2 The Multilateral Investment Fund (commercially known as IDB Lab) is a fund administered by the IDB and, therefore, any references to IDB Group Institution include IDB Lab.\n\n**_11._ Processing** : any action or set of actions, automated or not, which is performed on Personal Data, which may include, without limitation, its collection, recording, use, consultation, retrieval, disclosure by transmission, dissemination or otherwise making available, forwarding, organization, storage, structuring, adaptation or alteration, alignment or combination, restriction, erasure or destruction. \n\n**_12._ Processed** : having undertaken the act of Processing. \n\n**_13._ Third Party** or **Third Parties** : a legal person, other than IDB Group Institutions, or a natural person, other than IDB Group Institutions’ personnel and their dependents, as defined within their respective policies and procedures. \n\n# **III. PRINCIPLES** \n\nThe following Principles shall apply to all Processing of Personal Data by IDB Group Institutions: \n\n# **_1. Legitimate, Fair and Transparent Processing_** \n\nPersonal Data shall only be Processed for legitimate purposes and in a fair and transparent manner. Legitimate purposes for Processing mean any purpose: \n\n- a. for which the consent of a Data Subject is obtained, either at the time Personal Data are collected or subsequently; \n\n- b. that is in the vital or best interest of (i) the Data Subject or (ii) another person; \n\n- c. that is reasonably necessary for the performance of a contract; \n\n- d. that is reasonably necessary to enable an IDB Group Institution to satisfy an obligation or undertaking, or to comply with an IDB Group Institution’s policy or procedure; \n\n- e. that is reasonably necessary to establish, exercise or defend an IDB Group Institution’s right or interest; or \n\n- f. that is consistent with, or reasonably necessary to enable an IDB Group Institution to carry out its mission, mandate or purpose as an international organization established by its member countries. \n\n# **_2. Purpose Limitation_** \n\nPersonal Data shall be collected for one or more specific and legitimate purpose(s) listed in Principle 1 above and not further Processed in a manner that is incompatible with such purpose(s). Further Processing for archiving purposes, research, or statistical purposes shall not be considered incompatible with such purpose(s).\n\n# **_3. Data Minimization_** \n\nThe amount and type of Personal Data collected shall be reasonably necessary for, and proportionate to, the legitimate purpose(s) for which it is Processed. \n\n# **_4. Data Accuracy_** \n\nPersonal Data shall be recorded as accurately as possible and, where necessary, updated to fulfill the legitimate purpose(s) for which it is Processed. \n\n# **_5. Storage Limitation_** \n\nPersonal Data shall be kept in a form which permits identification of Data Subjects for no longer than is necessary for the legitimate purpose for which the Personal Data is collected, or for compatible further Processing, in accordance with this Policy. \n\n# **_6. Security_** \n\nPersonal Data shall be protected by appropriate and reasonable technical and organizational safeguards against unauthorized Processing and against accidental loss, destruction or damage. \n\n# **_7. Transfer of Personal Data_** \n\nPersonal Data shall only be transferred to a Third Party for legitimate purposes in accordance with this Policy and with appropriate regard for the protection of Personal Data. \n\n# **_8. Accountability and Review_** \n\nEach IDB Group Institution shall establish appropriate accountability and supervisory mechanism(s) to: \n\n- a) oversee compliance with this Policy: and \n\n- b) provide Data Subjects with a method, subject to reasonable limitations and conditions, to: \n\n   - i. request information regarding the Data Subject’s Personal Data Processed by or on behalf of such IDB Group Institution; and \n\n   - ii. seek redress if the Data Subject reasonably believes that the Data Subject’s Personal Data has been Processed in violation of this Policy. \n\n# **IV. MISCELLANEOUS** \n\n1. This Policy shall be implemented by each IDB Group Institution through guidelines, procedures, and other implementation measures, as applicable, tailored to each IDB Group Institution’s specific activities (the “ **Implementing Instruments** ”). \n\n2. This Policy shall become effective for each IDB Group Institution upon the earlier to occur of the following: (i) a declaration of effectiveness by the President of the IDB, in the case of the IDB, and the General Manager of IDB Invest, in the case of the IDB Invest, or such representative as each shall designate, to be issued upon adoption and effectiveness of Implementing Instruments; and (ii) three years from the date of approval of this Policy by the respective Board. \n\n3. This Policy shall not cover Personal Data collected before its effectiveness.\n\n4. The Processing of Personal Data in accordance with this Policy is without prejudice to the privileges and immunities of the IDB Group Institutions, which privileges and immunities are specifically reserved.\n\n---\n\n[Skip to main content](#main-content)\n\n\n*Last updated on: March 18, 2026*\n\n###### **Overview**\n\nThe Inter-American Investment Corporation (“IDB Invest”, “we”, “us” and “our”) is an international organization founded by international treaty in 1986 and is a member of the Inter-American Development Bank Group (“IDB Group”). As such, it is not subject to any national or supranational laws.\n\nThis Privacy Notice (“Privacy Notice”) explains how IDB Invest collects, uses, stores, transfers or otherwise processes the Personal Data of individuals (other than our own personnel and their dependents) (“you”). For the purposes of this Privacy Notice, Personal Data means any information relating to an identified or identifiable individual, such as a person’s name, contact details, location data, or factors relating to their physical, economic, cultural or social identity, or any other information that may reasonably be linked to that individual.\n\nIf you are either (i) the direct or indirect beneficiary of IDB Invest [Products and Services](https://idbinvest.org/en/solutions), or (ii) a representative of, or otherwise associated with, businesses and other organizations currently or potentially benefiting from or participating in IDB Invest’s [Products or Services](https://idbinvest.org/en/solutions) (for example, employees, officers, shareholders, directors, beneficial owners, guarantors or key vendors or partners of such businesses or organizations), this Privacy Notice applies to the processing of your Personal Data.\n\nPersonal data is processed by IDB Invest in accordance with the [IDB Group Personal Data Privacy Policy](https://idbinvest.org/sites/default/files/2022-11/IDB%20Group%20Personal%20Data%20Privacy%20Policy.pdf) (the “Privacy Policy”). Such processing enables IDB Invest to carry out its mission, mandate and purpose as an international organization established by its member countries.\n\nPlease ensure that you read this Privacy Notice in its entirety, as amended from time to time.\n\n---\n\n###### **What Does this Privacy Notice Cover?**\n\nThis Privacy Notice relates to the Personal Data we collect and process from you, and covers the following aspects:\n\n(Click on the topic you want to read)\n\n* [The contexts in which we process your Personal Data;](#1)\n* [The types of Personal Data that we process about you;](#2)\n* [The sources from which IDB Invest obtain your Personal Data;](#3)\n* [How and why IDB Invest processes your Personal Data;](#4)\n* [How long we keep your Personal Data;](#5)\n* [How, why and to whom we transfer your Personal Data;](#6)\n* [How we protect your Personal Data;](#7)\n* [Changes to this Privacy Notice;](#8)\n* [Explains the application of our privileges and immunities;](#9) and\n* [Explains how you may contact us with queries or complaints.](#10)\n\n---\n\n###### **The Contexts in Which we Process your Personal Data**\n\nThe Personal Data processing activities we undertake will vary based on your relationship with IDB Invest.\n\n**I. Visitors to IDB Invest’s websites**\n\nIDB Invest does not automatically process Personal Data related to the visitors of its website, e.g. idbinvest.org, or official IDB Invest pages on other platforms. However, we will process Personal Data that you submit through any interface of the official websites (for example, when registering for an event). This Privacy Notice does not apply to third party websites. We encourage you to review the privacy notices of any third-party websites you visit.\n\n**II. Subscribers of IDB Invest newsletters or publications**\n\nIf you subscribe to an IDB Invest newsletter or publication, we process your Personal Data (for example, your name and e-mail address) so we can make sure that you receive it.\n\n**III. Registered attendees of IDB Invest events**\n\nIf you register to attend an IDB Invest event, we collect and process your Personal Data in connection with the organization and management of the event.\n\n**IV. Personal Data processed in the course of providing our Products and Services**\n\nIn the course of providing our Products and Services IDB Invest processes Personal Data.\n\n**V. Personal Data in the context of recruitment**\n\nPersonal Data is required to manage job applications and recruitment processes. For detailed information, please refer to the privacy notice provided to job applicants during the application process ([available here](https://www.iadb.org/en/terms-conditions-and-notices/privacy-notice/job-applicant-privacy-notice)).\n\n**VI. Personal Data in the context of procurement**\n\nIn the course of providing our procurement activities, IDB Invest processes Personal Data.\n\n**VII. Business planning, client strategy, communications and analytics activities**\n\nIf you engage with IDB Invest as a business contact, prospective client, or external stakeholder (for example, through meetings, conferences, or professional networking), we may process your Personal Data for business development, client engagement, and institutional communications purposes.\n\n---\n\n###### **What Personal Data do we Process?**\n\nWe may collect and process the following Personal Data about you:\n\n* **Identification and contact data –** name, postal address(es), email address, phone number(s), signature specimen, passport/nationality identity documents (including embedded photographs), age and date of birth, citizenship status, office location, and limited biometric identifiers used for identity verification or security purposes;\n* **Operations data –** information about your involvement in, and/or the development impact on you of, our investment and advisory operations and activities;\n* **Financial data –** relevant financial information of how you benefit directly or indirectly from our Products and Services;\n* **Background data –** relevant background information used for anti-corruption and anti-fraud assessments in accordance with our applicable policies and procedures;\n* **Professional data –** job title, employer details or organizational affiliation, photograph in your CV, professional history, qualification details, information about your experience, participation in meetings, seminars, and conferences, information about your professional relationship with other individuals or institutions, language abilities, and other professional skills;\n* **Correspondence –** records of any correspondence we may have with you, records of your correspondence preferences (including subscription to our newsletters);\n* **Consent records –** records of preferences and permissions you provide to us, including records of consent opt-in/opt-out choices, where applicable. When maintained, such records are used solely to demonstrate compliance with applicable legal, contractual or governance obligations and to respect your stated preferences;\n* **Data relating to our websites –** technical data (device type, operating system, browser type and settings, IP address, language settings), usage and behavioral data, connection information (dates, times, location), analytics, and aggregate statistical information.\n* **Diversity and inclusion data –** salutations, gender identity, race / ethnicity, disability status;\n\nIn limited circumstances, IDB Invest may process special categories of Personal Data, such as information relating to an individual’s health, racial or ethnic origin, or other similarly sensitive characteristics. Such data will be processed only where strictly necessary and in accordance with applicable institutional policies and will be subject to enhanced safeguards designed to ensure an appropriate level of protection for the confidentiality, integrity, and security of the Personal Data.\n\n---\n\n###### **Where we Obtain your Personal Data?**\n\nWe may obtain or receive Personal Data about you from the following sources:\n\n* **Personal Data you or your employer provide to us –** Personal Data provided directly by you (e.g., job applications, correspondence you send us, information you provide to our investment officers, or when you complete an online form or survey), or that is provided to us by your employer or other organization with which you are associated, and information collected during meetings, events, and business interactions.\n* **Personal Data we collect by automated means –** As noted above, we may obtain certain information by automated means when you visit our websites.\n* **Personal Data we collect from third parties –** We may collect or obtain Personal Data from third parties (e.g., counterparties to a transaction, law enforcement authorities, relevant business contacts, specialized databases operated by the private sector, specialized external service providers, consultants or vendors).\n* **Personal Data you make public –** We may collect or obtain Personal Data that you manifestly choose to make public, including via social media (e.g., we may collect information from your social media profile(s), if you make a public post about us).\n\n---\n\n###### **Why we Process your Personal Data?**\n\nIDB Invest processes your Personal Data as reasonably necessary to conduct and manage our activities within the contexts listed above. This includes processing Personal Data for any of the following purposes:\n\n**I. To carry out IDB Invest’s investment, advisory and asset management activities**\n\n* Exploring investment opportunities and conducting due diligence;\n* Executing legal instruments related to investment, advisory and asset management activities;\n* Administering and managing our relationships with counterparties (and potential counterparties) in the context of our investment, advisory and asset management activities (or potential activities that may be of interest);\n* Understanding and monitoring the development impact of our activities;\n* Investigating and responding to complaints, and establishing, exercising, or defending IDB Invest’s legal rights and obligations;\n* Coordinating with other IDB Group Institutions; and,\n* Supporting equality, diversity and inclusion in our projects.\n\n**II. To comply with legal and policy obligations and manage risk**\n\n* Performing internal governance functions;\n* Conducting accounting and financial management;\n* Maintaining appropriate accounting, financial management and other records;\n* Fulfill our policy obligations, confirming and verifying your identity, and screening against government and/or law enforcement agency sanctions lists and other legal restrictions;\n* Carrying out our obligations, and exercising our rights, under applicable legal or regulatory requirements and any contracts entered into between you and IDB Invest;\n* Conducting credit and other risk assessment and control activities, including for the prevention and detection of corruption and fraud; and,\n* Training our staff and maintaining and improving the quality of our internal processes and arrangements.\n\n**III. To manage communications, stakeholder engagement and business development**\n\n* Disseminating information to further IDB Invest’s mission to improve lives in Latin America and the Caribbean, and providing research information;\n* Responding to your queries and feedback (for example, if you have asked a question or submitted feedback through our website);\n* Providing you with information, products or services you have requested or that may be of interest to you, unless you tell us otherwise; and,\n* Conducting business intelligence operations; and conducting business planning and client strategy activities, including organizing and managing events for clients and potential clients; conducting business analysis, planning and monitoring; preparing and disseminating marketing, institutional and business communications; defining communications strategies, guidelines and mechanisms; developing and communicating plans, strategies, strategic initiatives and updates to internal and external stakeholders; understanding client behavior through analytics to design and enhance client experiences; conducting impact evaluations and other in-depth studies (which may include surveys with project beneficiaries and other stakeholders); and supporting business development and client engagement initiatives.\n\n**IV. In connection with the management of IDB Invest’s websites, data analytics and IT security**\n\n* Providing access, maintaining and improving our websites and services;\n* Enabling you to participate in any interactive features of our websites and communicating with you, including through our newsletter, subject to your preferences;\n* Presenting website content in a manner suitable for the device you are accessing it from Undertaking data analytics to understand how users interact with our websites and online public-facing materials;\n* Monitoring and analyzing the use of our products and services for purposes of developing and improving them;\n* Managing and ensuring the security of our IT systems, including detecting and preventing misuse or abuse of our websites and services, and for backup and disaster recovery purposes; and,\n* We may also process Personal Data for any other purpose described to you at the time your data is collected.\n\nWe may also collect and process Personal Data of visitors to our premises, including for the purposes of ensuring safety and security at those premises, as further detailed in the notices available at our premises.\n\n---\n\n###### **How Long we Keep your Personal Data**\n\nYour Personal Data will be kept only as long as necessary for the purposes set out in this Privacy Notice and in accordance with IDB Invest’s applicable records retention and disposition schedules. The specific length of time will depend on the type of Personal Data, the reasons for which it is processed, and other obligations under IDB Invest’s policies and procedures.\n\n---\n\n###### **International Transfers of Personal Data**\n\nWhen you submit Personal Data to us by any means, that Personal Data may be transferred to a jurisdiction other than the one in which you live. In particular, Personal Data may be transferred to the United States. The data protection and other privacy laws of the United States may not afford the same level of protection as the laws of other countries.\n\n---\n\n###### **To whom we Disclose your Personal Data?**\n\nIDB Invest may disclose your Personal Data to the recipients described below, as reasonably necessary for the purposes outlined in this Privacy Notice.\n\n* IDB Group Institutions: We may disclose your Personal Data to other IDB Group institutions, such as the Inter-American Development Bank, as necessary for the purposes set out in this Privacy Notice.\n* Third parties: Unless otherwise noted below, and subject to contractually agreed conditions of confidentiality and security (where applicable), we may disclose your Personal Data to the categories of parties listed below:\n  + Service providers and suppliers who perform services, such as event vendors and organizers, consulting firms, among others, and providers that support compliance processes, including KYC screening and due diligence processes.\n  + Legal and other advisors that assist, advise or represent an IDB Group Institution as needed, such as attorneys, in connection with litigation, investigations, advising on contractual obligations, or enabling an IDB Group Institution to carry out its development mandate.\n  + Relevant legal, regulatory or administrative authorities, as we believe to be appropriate, for example, public registers involved in the execution and enforcement of relevant transaction documents, and other relevant authorities to protect and defend our rights and property, protect the interests of the IDB Group or others; or enable us to pursue available remedies or limit the damages that we may sustain; and,\n  + Other selected third parties: legal entities, including financial institutions, custodians, brokers, private companies, intermediaries, donors, partners and other organizations with which you are associated or involved (if any) in connection with our Products or Services; and peer researchers from academia, who carry out impact evaluations, among others.\n\nIDB Invest seeks to ensure that all partners and service providers processing Personal Data on its behalf implement appropriate technical and organizational safeguards to protect the privacy and security of such data.\n\n---\n\n###### **How to Request Information on your Personal Data Processed by IDB Invest**\n\nAs part of its data privacy framework, IDB Invest has established a procedure for individuals to request information regarding their Personal Data processed by IDB Invest and, when appropriate, to seek redress if they reasonably believe their Personal Data has not been processed in accordance with the IDB Group Personal Data Privacy Policy.\n\nYou may submit such a request using the webform [available here](https://forms.office.com/r/QAvQqSEBdy).\n\n---\n\n###### **How we Protect your Personal Data**\n\nWe have appropriate technical (e.g., firewalls, malware scans, anti-virus protection, encryption, physical locks) and organizational (e.g., policies and procedures, privacy assessments, due diligence, awareness, and training) safeguards in place to prevent unauthorized processing and accidental loss, damage, or destruction of Personal Data. These safeguards take into account the sensitivity of the data, as well as the current state of technology. We also have procedures in place to deal with data breaches, and we will notify you accordingly when appropriate.\n\n---\n\n###### **Changes to this Privacy Notice**\n\nThis Privacy Notice was last updated on the date listed above. If we change it, we will post the new version to this website.\n\n---\n\n###### **Queries and Complaints**\n\nIf you have any complaints or queries regarding your Personal Data, please contact [[email protected]](/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection#b0c0c2d9c6d1d3c9f0f9f4f2d9dec6d5c3c49edfc2d7).\n\n---\n\n###### **Privileges and Immunities**\n\nNothing contained in this Privacy Notice shall constitute or be considered to be a limitation upon or a waiver of the privileges and immunities of IDB Invest, which are specifically reserved.\n\n\n---\n\n# **<u>IDB GROUP PERSONAL DATA PRIVACY POLICY</u>**<sup>**1**</sup> \n\n# **I. PURPOSE AND APPLICATION** \n\nThis document sets out the Policy for the Processing of Personal Data by IDB Group Institutions. \n\nThis Policy applies to the Processing of Personal Data by, or on behalf of, IDB Group Institutions, and is intended to develop consistent practices across the IDB Group. \n\n# **II. DEFINITIONS** \n\nCapitalized terms or acronyms used in this Policy have the meaning set out below: \n\n**_1._ Board(s)** : the Boards of Executive Directors of IDB and IDB Invest, respectively. \n\n**_2._ Data Subject** : a natural, living person to whom Personal Data pertains, and whose Personal Data is Processed by an IDB Group Institution. Data Subjects may include, without limitation, any current or former: (i) IDB Group Institution staff member, director or their dependents; (ii) IDB Group Institution contractor or consultant; (iii) applicant for a vacancy at an IDB Group Institution; (iv) IDB Group Institution suppliers or vendors; (v) IDB Group Institution client or their representatives; (vi) respondents to IDB Group Institution surveys; or (vii) subscribers to an IDB Group Institution website. \n\n**_3._ IDB** : the Inter-American Development Bank. \n\n**_4._ IDB Group** : the Inter-American Development Bank Group. \n\n**_5._ IDB Group Institution** : any one of the IDB<sup>2</sup> and IDB Invest. \n\n**_6._ IDB Invest** : the Inter-American Investment Corporation. \n\n**_7._ Implementing Instruments** : has the meaning set forth in Section IV below. \n\n**_8._ Personal Data** : any information relating to an identified or identifiable Data Subject. An identifiable Data Subject is one who can be identified by reasonable means, directly or indirectly, by reference to an attribute or combination of attributes within the data, or combination of the data with other available information. Examples of attributes that can be used to identify an identifiable Data Subject include their name, identification number, location data, online identifier, metadata, and factors specific to their physical, physiological, genetic, mental, economic, cultural or social identity. \n\n**_9._ Policy** : this Personal Data Privacy Policy. \n\n**_10._ Principles** : the principles set out in Section III below. \n\n> 1 This Policy is not effective yet pursuant to Section IV below. \n\n> 2 The Multilateral Investment Fund (commercially known as IDB Lab) is a fund administered by the IDB and, therefore, any references to IDB Group Institution include IDB Lab.\n\n**_11._ Processing** : any action or set of actions, automated or not, which is performed on Personal Data, which may include, without limitation, its collection, recording, use, consultation, retrieval, disclosure by transmission, dissemination or otherwise making available, forwarding, organization, storage, structuring, adaptation or alteration, alignment or combination, restriction, erasure or destruction. \n\n**_12._ Processed** : having undertaken the act of Processing. \n\n**_13._ Third Party** or **Third Parties** : a legal person, other than IDB Group Institutions, or a natural person, other than IDB Group Institutions’ personnel and their dependents, as defined within their respective policies and procedures. \n\n# **III. PRINCIPLES** \n\nThe following Principles shall apply to all Processing of Personal Data by IDB Group Institutions: \n\n# **_1. Legitimate, Fair and Transparent Processing_** \n\nPersonal Data shall only be Processed for legitimate purposes and in a fair and transparent manner. Legitimate purposes for Processing mean any purpose: \n\n- a. for which the consent of a Data Subject is obtained, either at the time Personal Data are collected or subsequently; \n\n- b. that is in the vital or best interest of (i) the Data Subject or (ii) another person; \n\n- c. that is reasonably necessary for the performance of a contract; \n\n- d. that is reasonably necessary to enable an IDB Group Institution to satisfy an obligation or undertaking, or to comply with an IDB Group Institution’s policy or procedure; \n\n- e. that is reasonably necessary to establish, exercise or defend an IDB Group Institution’s right or interest; or \n\n- f. that is consistent with, or reasonably necessary to enable an IDB Group Institution to carry out its mission, mandate or purpose as an international organization established by its member countries. \n\n# **_2. Purpose Limitation_** \n\nPersonal Data shall be collected for one or more specific and legitimate purpose(s) listed in Principle 1 above and not further Processed in a manner that is incompatible with such purpose(s). Further Processing for archiving purposes, research, or statistical purposes shall not be considered incompatible with such purpose(s).\n\n# **_3. Data Minimization_** \n\nThe amount and type of Personal Data collected shall be reasonably necessary for, and proportionate to, the legitimate purpose(s) for which it is Processed. \n\n# **_4. Data Accuracy_** \n\nPersonal Data shall be recorded as accurately as possible and, where necessary, updated to fulfill the legitimate purpose(s) for which it is Processed. \n\n# **_5. Storage Limitation_** \n\nPersonal Data shall be kept in a form which permits identification of Data Subjects for no longer than is necessary for the legitimate purpose for which the Personal Data is collected, or for compatible further Processing, in accordance with this Policy. \n\n# **_6. Security_** \n\nPersonal Data shall be protected by appropriate and reasonable technical and organizational safeguards against unauthorized Processing and against accidental loss, destruction or damage. \n\n# **_7. Transfer of Personal Data_** \n\nPersonal Data shall only be transferred to a Third Party for legitimate purposes in accordance with this Policy and with appropriate regard for the protection of Personal Data. \n\n# **_8. Accountability and Review_** \n\nEach IDB Group Institution shall establish appropriate accountability and supervisory mechanism(s) to: \n\n- a) oversee compliance with this Policy: and \n\n- b) provide Data Subjects with a method, subject to reasonable limitations and conditions, to: \n\n   - i. request information regarding the Data Subject’s Personal Data Processed by or on behalf of such IDB Group Institution; and \n\n   - ii. seek redress if the Data Subject reasonably believes that the Data Subject’s Personal Data has been Processed in violation of this Policy. \n\n# **IV. MISCELLANEOUS** \n\n1. This Policy shall be implemented by each IDB Group Institution through guidelines, procedures, and other implementation measures, as applicable, tailored to each IDB Group Institution’s specific activities (the “ **Implementing Instruments** ”). \n\n2. This Policy shall become effective for each IDB Group Institution upon the earlier to occur of the following: (i) a declaration of effectiveness by the President of the IDB, in the case of the IDB, and the General Manager of IDB Invest, in the case of the IDB Invest, or such representative as each shall designate, to be issued upon adoption and effectiveness of Implementing Instruments; and (ii) three years from the date of approval of this Policy by the respective Board. \n\n3. This Policy shall not cover Personal Data collected before its effectiveness.\n\n4. The Processing of Personal Data in accordance with this Policy is without prejudice to the privileges and immunities of the IDB Group Institutions, which privileges and immunities are specifically reserved.\n\n---\n\n[Skip to main content](#main-content)\n\n\n*Last updated on: March 18, 2026*\n\n###### **Overview**\n\nThe Inter-American Investment Corporation (“IDB Invest”, “we”, “us” and “our”) is an international organization founded by international treaty in 1986 and is a member of the Inter-American Development Bank Group (“IDB Group”). As such, it is not subject to any national or supranational laws.\n\nThis Privacy Notice (“Privacy Notice”) explains how IDB Invest collects, uses, stores, transfers or otherwise processes the Personal Data of individuals (other than our own personnel and their dependents) (“you”). For the purposes of this Privacy Notice, Personal Data means any information relating to an identified or identifiable individual, such as a person’s name, contact details, location data, or factors relating to their physical, economic, cultural or social identity, or any other information that may reasonably be linked to that individual.\n\nIf you are either (i) the direct or indirect beneficiary of IDB Invest [Products and Services](https://idbinvest.org/en/solutions), or (ii) a representative of, or otherwise associated with, businesses and other organizations currently or potentially benefiting from or participating in IDB Invest’s [Products or Services](https://idbinvest.org/en/solutions) (for example, employees, officers, shareholders, directors, beneficial owners, guarantors or key vendors or partners of such businesses or organizations), this Privacy Notice applies to the processing of your Personal Data.\n\nPersonal data is processed by IDB Invest in accordance with the [IDB Group Personal Data Privacy Policy](https://idbinvest.org/sites/default/files/2022-11/IDB%20Group%20Personal%20Data%20Privacy%20Policy.pdf) (the “Privacy Policy”). Such processing enables IDB Invest to carry out its mission, mandate and purpose as an international organization established by its member countries.\n\nPlease ensure that you read this Privacy Notice in its entirety, as amended from time to time.\n\n---\n\n###### **What Does this Privacy Notice Cover?**\n\nThis Privacy Notice relates to the Personal Data we collect and process from you, and covers the following aspects:\n\n(Click on the topic you want to read)\n\n* [The contexts in which we process your Personal Data;](#1)\n* [The types of Personal Data that we process about you;](#2)\n* [The sources from which IDB Invest obtain your Personal Data;](#3)\n* [How and why IDB Invest processes your Personal Data;](#4)\n* [How long we keep your Personal Data;](#5)\n* [How, why and to whom we transfer your Personal Data;](#6)\n* [How we protect your Personal Data;](#7)\n* [Changes to this Privacy Notice;](#8)\n* [Explains the application of our privileges and immunities;](#9) and\n* [Explains how you may contact us with queries or complaints.](#10)\n\n---\n\n###### **The Contexts in Which we Process your Personal Data**\n\nThe Personal Data processing activities we undertake will vary based on your relationship with IDB Invest.\n\n**I. Visitors to IDB Invest’s websites**\n\nIDB Invest does not automatically process Personal Data related to the visitors of its website, e.g. idbinvest.org, or official IDB Invest pages on other platforms. However, we will process Personal Data that you submit through any interface of the official websites (for example, when registering for an event). This Privacy Notice does not apply to third party websites. We encourage you to review the privacy notices of any third-party websites you visit.\n\n**II. Subscribers of IDB Invest newsletters or publications**\n\nIf you subscribe to an IDB Invest newsletter or publication, we process your Personal Data (for example, your name and e-mail address) so we can make sure that you receive it.\n\n**III. Registered attendees of IDB Invest events**\n\nIf you register to attend an IDB Invest event, we collect and process your Personal Data in connection with the organization and management of the event.\n\n**IV. Personal Data processed in the course of providing our Products and Services**\n\nIn the course of providing our Products and Services IDB Invest processes Personal Data.\n\n**V. Personal Data in the context of recruitment**\n\nPersonal Data is required to manage job applications and recruitment processes. For detailed information, please refer to the privacy notice provided to job applicants during the application process ([available here](https://www.iadb.org/en/terms-conditions-and-notices/privacy-notice/job-applicant-privacy-notice)).\n\n**VI. Personal Data in the context of procurement**\n\nIn the course of providing our procurement activities, IDB Invest processes Personal Data.\n\n**VII. Business planning, client strategy, communications and analytics activities**\n\nIf you engage with IDB Invest as a business contact, prospective client, or external stakeholder (for example, through meetings, conferences, or professional networking), we may process your Personal Data for business development, client engagement, and institutional communications purposes.\n\n---\n\n###### **What Personal Data do we Process?**\n\nWe may collect and process the following Personal Data about you:\n\n* **Identification and contact data –** name, postal address(es), email address, phone number(s), signature specimen, passport/nationality identity documents (including embedded photographs), age and date of birth, citizenship status, office location, and limited biometric identifiers used for identity verification or security purposes;\n* **Operations data –** information about your involvement in, and/or the development impact on you of, our investment and advisory operations and activities;\n* **Financial data –** relevant financial information of how you benefit directly or indirectly from our Products and Services;\n* **Background data –** relevant background information used for anti-corruption and anti-fraud assessments in accordance with our applicable policies and procedures;\n* **Professional data –** job title, employer details or organizational affiliation, photograph in your CV, professional history, qualification details, information about your experience, participation in meetings, seminars, and conferences, information about your professional relationship with other individuals or institutions, language abilities, and other professional skills;\n* **Correspondence –** records of any correspondence we may have with you, records of your correspondence preferences (including subscription to our newsletters);\n* **Consent records –** records of preferences and permissions you provide to us, including records of consent opt-in/opt-out choices, where applicable. When maintained, such records are used solely to demonstrate compliance with applicable legal, contractual or governance obligations and to respect your stated preferences;\n* **Data relating to our websites –** technical data (device type, operating system, browser type and settings, IP address, language settings), usage and behavioral data, connection information (dates, times, location), analytics, and aggregate statistical information.\n* **Diversity and inclusion data –** salutations, gender identity, race / ethnicity, disability status;\n\nIn limited circumstances, IDB Invest may process special categories of Personal Data, such as information relating to an individual’s health, racial or ethnic origin, or other similarly sensitive characteristics. Such data will be processed only where strictly necessary and in accordance with applicable institutional policies and will be subject to enhanced safeguards designed to ensure an appropriate level of protection for the confidentiality, integrity, and security of the Personal Data.\n\n---\n\n###### **Where we Obtain your Personal Data?**\n\nWe may obtain or receive Personal Data about you from the following sources:\n\n* **Personal Data you or your employer provide to us –** Personal Data provided directly by you (e.g., job applications, correspondence you send us, information you provide to our investment officers, or when you complete an online form or survey), or that is provided to us by your employer or other organization with which you are associated, and information collected during meetings, events, and business interactions.\n* **Personal Data we collect by automated means –** As noted above, we may obtain certain information by automated means when you visit our websites.\n* **Personal Data we collect from third parties –** We may collect or obtain Personal Data from third parties (e.g., counterparties to a transaction, law enforcement authorities, relevant business contacts, specialized databases operated by the private sector, specialized external service providers, consultants or vendors).\n* **Personal Data you make public –** We may collect or obtain Personal Data that you manifestly choose to make public, including via social media (e.g., we may collect information from your social media profile(s), if you make a public post about us).\n\n---\n\n###### **Why we Process your Personal Data?**\n\nIDB Invest processes your Personal Data as reasonably necessary to conduct and manage our activities within the contexts listed above. This includes processing Personal Data for any of the following purposes:\n\n**I. To carry out IDB Invest’s investment, advisory and asset management activities**\n\n* Exploring investment opportunities and conducting due diligence;\n* Executing legal instruments related to investment, advisory and asset management activities;\n* Administering and managing our relationships with counterparties (and potential counterparties) in the context of our investment, advisory and asset management activities (or potential activities that may be of interest);\n* Understanding and monitoring the development impact of our activities;\n* Investigating and responding to complaints, and establishing, exercising, or defending IDB Invest’s legal rights and obligations;\n* Coordinating with other IDB Group Institutions; and,\n* Supporting equality, diversity and inclusion in our projects.\n\n**II. To comply with legal and policy obligations and manage risk**\n\n* Performing internal governance functions;\n* Conducting accounting and financial management;\n* Maintaining appropriate accounting, financial management and other records;\n* Fulfill our policy obligations, confirming and verifying your identity, and screening against government and/or law enforcement agency sanctions lists and other legal restrictions;\n* Carrying out our obligations, and exercising our rights, under applicable legal or regulatory requirements and any contracts entered into between you and IDB Invest;\n* Conducting credit and other risk assessment and control activities, including for the prevention and detection of corruption and fraud; and,\n* Training our staff and maintaining and improving the quality of our internal processes and arrangements.\n\n**III. To manage communications, stakeholder engagement and business development**\n\n* Disseminating information to further IDB Invest’s mission to improve lives in Latin America and the Caribbean, and providing research information;\n* Responding to your queries and feedback (for example, if you have asked a question or submitted feedback through our website);\n* Providing you with information, products or services you have requested or that may be of interest to you, unless you tell us otherwise; and,\n* Conducting business intelligence operations; and conducting business planning and client strategy activities, including organizing and managing events for clients and potential clients; conducting business analysis, planning and monitoring; preparing and disseminating marketing, institutional and business communications; defining communications strategies, guidelines and mechanisms; developing and communicating plans, strategies, strategic initiatives and updates to internal and external stakeholders; understanding client behavior through analytics to design and enhance client experiences; conducting impact evaluations and other in-depth studies (which may include surveys with project beneficiaries and other stakeholders); and supporting business development and client engagement initiatives.\n\n**IV. In connection with the management of IDB Invest’s websites, data analytics and IT security**\n\n* Providing access, maintaining and improving our websites and services;\n* Enabling you to participate in any interactive features of our websites and communicating with you, including through our newsletter, subject to your preferences;\n* Presenting website content in a manner suitable for the device you are accessing it from Undertaking data analytics to understand how users interact with our websites and online public-facing materials;\n* Monitoring and analyzing the use of our products and services for purposes of developing and improving them;\n* Managing and ensuring the security of our IT systems, including detecting and preventing misuse or abuse of our websites and services, and for backup and disaster recovery purposes; and,\n* We may also process Personal Data for any other purpose described to you at the time your data is collected.\n\nWe may also collect and process Personal Data of visitors to our premises, including for the purposes of ensuring safety and security at those premises, as further detailed in the notices available at our premises.\n\n---\n\n###### **How Long we Keep your Personal Data**\n\nYour Personal Data will be kept only as long as necessary for the purposes set out in this Privacy Notice and in accordance with IDB Invest’s applicable records retention and disposition schedules. The specific length of time will depend on the type of Personal Data, the reasons for which it is processed, and other obligations under IDB Invest’s policies and procedures.\n\n---\n\n###### **International Transfers of Personal Data**\n\nWhen you submit Personal Data to us by any means, that Personal Data may be transferred to a jurisdiction other than the one in which you live. In particular, Personal Data may be transferred to the United States. The data protection and other privacy laws of the United States may not afford the same level of protection as the laws of other countries.\n\n---\n\n###### **To whom we Disclose your Personal Data?**\n\nIDB Invest may disclose your Personal Data to the recipients described below, as reasonably necessary for the purposes outlined in this Privacy Notice.\n\n* IDB Group Institutions: We may disclose your Personal Data to other IDB Group institutions, such as the Inter-American Development Bank, as necessary for the purposes set out in this Privacy Notice.\n* Third parties: Unless otherwise noted below, and subject to contractually agreed conditions of confidentiality and security (where applicable), we may disclose your Personal Data to the categories of parties listed below:\n  + Service providers and suppliers who perform services, such as event vendors and organizers, consulting firms, among others, and providers that support compliance processes, including KYC screening and due diligence processes.\n  + Legal and other advisors that assist, advise or represent an IDB Group Institution as needed, such as attorneys, in connection with litigation, investigations, advising on contractual obligations, or enabling an IDB Group Institution to carry out its development mandate.\n  + Relevant legal, regulatory or administrative authorities, as we believe to be appropriate, for example, public registers involved in the execution and enforcement of relevant transaction documents, and other relevant authorities to protect and defend our rights and property, protect the interests of the IDB Group or others; or enable us to pursue available remedies or limit the damages that we may sustain; and,\n  + Other selected third parties: legal entities, including financial institutions, custodians, brokers, private companies, intermediaries, donors, partners and other organizations with which you are associated or involved (if any) in connection with our Products or Services; and peer researchers from academia, who carry out impact evaluations, among others.\n\nIDB Invest seeks to ensure that all partners and service providers processing Personal Data on its behalf implement appropriate technical and organizational safeguards to protect the privacy and security of such data.\n\n---\n\n###### **How to Request Information on your Personal Data Processed by IDB Invest**\n\nAs part of its data privacy framework, IDB Invest has established a procedure for individuals to request information regarding their Personal Data processed by IDB Invest and, when appropriate, to seek redress if they reasonably believe their Personal Data has not been processed in accordance with the IDB Group Personal Data Privacy Policy.\n\nYou may submit such a request using the webform [available here](https://forms.office.com/r/QAvQqSEBdy).\n\n---\n\n###### **How we Protect your Personal Data**\n\nWe have appropriate technical (e.g., firewalls, malware scans, anti-virus protection, encryption, physical locks) and organizational (e.g., policies and procedures, privacy assessments, due diligence, awareness, and training) safeguards in place to prevent unauthorized processing and accidental loss, damage, or destruction of Personal Data. These safeguards take into account the sensitivity of the data, as well as the current state of technology. We also have procedures in place to deal with data breaches, and we will notify you accordingly when appropriate.\n\n---\n\n###### **Changes to this Privacy Notice**\n\nThis Privacy Notice was last updated on the date listed above. If we change it, we will post the new version to this website.\n\n---\n\n###### **Queries and Complaints**\n\nIf you have any complaints or queries regarding your Personal Data, please contact [[email protected]](/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection#b0c0c2d9c6d1d3c9f0f9f4f2d9dec6d5c3c49edfc2d7).\n\n---\n\n###### **Privileges and Immunities**\n\nNothing contained in this Privacy Notice shall constitute or be considered to be a limitation upon or a waiver of the privileges and immunities of IDB Invest, which are specifically reserved.\n\n\n---\n\n# **<u>IDB GROUP PERSONAL DATA PRIVACY POLICY</u>**<sup>**1**</sup> \n\n# **I. PURPOSE AND APPLICATION** \n\nThis document sets out the Policy for the Processing of Personal Data by IDB Group Institutions. \n\nThis Policy applies to the Processing of Personal Data by, or on behalf of, IDB Group Institutions, and is intended to develop consistent practices across the IDB Group. \n\n# **II. DEFINITIONS** \n\nCapitalized terms or acronyms used in this Policy have the meaning set out below: \n\n**_1._ Board(s)** : the Boards of Executive Directors of IDB and IDB Invest, respectively. \n\n**_2._ Data Subject** : a natural, living person to whom Personal Data pertains, and whose Personal Data is Processed by an IDB Group Institution. Data Subjects may include, without limitation, any current or former: (i) IDB Group Institution staff member, director or their dependents; (ii) IDB Group Institution contractor or consultant; (iii) applicant for a vacancy at an IDB Group Institution; (iv) IDB Group Institution suppliers or vendors; (v) IDB Group Institution client or their representatives; (vi) respondents to IDB Group Institution surveys; or (vii) subscribers to an IDB Group Institution website. \n\n**_3._ IDB** : the Inter-American Development Bank. \n\n**_4._ IDB Group** : the Inter-American Development Bank Group. \n\n**_5._ IDB Group Institution** : any one of the IDB<sup>2</sup> and IDB Invest. \n\n**_6._ IDB Invest** : the Inter-American Investment Corporation. \n\n**_7._ Implementing Instruments** : has the meaning set forth in Section IV below. \n\n**_8._ Personal Data** : any information relating to an identified or identifiable Data Subject. An identifiable Data Subject is one who can be identified by reasonable means, directly or indirectly, by reference to an attribute or combination of attributes within the data, or combination of the data with other available information. Examples of attributes that can be used to identify an identifiable Data Subject include their name, identification number, location data, online identifier, metadata, and factors specific to their physical, physiological, genetic, mental, economic, cultural or social identity. \n\n**_9._ Policy** : this Personal Data Privacy Policy. \n\n**_10._ Principles** : the principles set out in Section III below. \n\n> 1 This Policy is not effective yet pursuant to Section IV below. \n\n> 2 The Multilateral Investment Fund (commercially known as IDB Lab) is a fund administered by the IDB and, therefore, any references to IDB Group Institution include IDB Lab.\n\n**_11._ Processing** : any action or set of actions, automated or not, which is performed on Personal Data, which may include, without limitation, its collection, recording, use, consultation, retrieval, disclosure by transmission, dissemination or otherwise making available, forwarding, organization, storage, structuring, adaptation or alteration, alignment or combination, restriction, erasure or destruction. \n\n**_12._ Processed** : having undertaken the act of Processing. \n\n**_13._ Third Party** or **Third Parties** : a legal person, other than IDB Group Institutions, or a natural person, other than IDB Group Institutions’ personnel and their dependents, as defined within their respective policies and procedures. \n\n# **III. PRINCIPLES** \n\nThe following Principles shall apply to all Processing of Personal Data by IDB Group Institutions: \n\n# **_1. Legitimate, Fair and Transparent Processing_** \n\nPersonal Data shall only be Processed for legitimate purposes and in a fair and transparent manner. Legitimate purposes for Processing mean any purpose: \n\n- a. for which the consent of a Data Subject is obtained, either at the time Personal Data are collected or subsequently; \n\n- b. that is in the vital or best interest of (i) the Data Subject or (ii) another person; \n\n- c. that is reasonably necessary for the performance of a contract; \n\n- d. that is reasonably necessary to enable an IDB Group Institution to satisfy an obligation or undertaking, or to comply with an IDB Group Institution’s policy or procedure; \n\n- e. that is reasonably necessary to establish, exercise or defend an IDB Group Institution’s right or interest; or \n\n- f. that is consistent with, or reasonably necessary to enable an IDB Group Institution to carry out its mission, mandate or purpose as an international organization established by its member countries. \n\n# **_2. Purpose Limitation_** \n\nPersonal Data shall be collected for one or more specific and legitimate purpose(s) listed in Principle 1 above and not further Processed in a manner that is incompatible with such purpose(s). Further Processing for archiving purposes, research, or statistical purposes shall not be considered incompatible with such purpose(s).\n\n# **_3. Data Minimization_** \n\nThe amount and type of Personal Data collected shall be reasonably necessary for, and proportionate to, the legitimate purpose(s) for which it is Processed. \n\n# **_4. Data Accuracy_** \n\nPersonal Data shall be recorded as accurately as possible and, where necessary, updated to fulfill the legitimate purpose(s) for which it is Processed. \n\n# **_5. Storage Limitation_** \n\nPersonal Data shall be kept in a form which permits identification of Data Subjects for no longer than is necessary for the legitimate purpose for which the Personal Data is collected, or for compatible further Processing, in accordance with this Policy. \n\n# **_6. Security_** \n\nPersonal Data shall be protected by appropriate and reasonable technical and organizational safeguards against unauthorized Processing and against accidental loss, destruction or damage. \n\n# **_7. Transfer of Personal Data_** \n\nPersonal Data shall only be transferred to a Third Party for legitimate purposes in accordance with this Policy and with appropriate regard for the protection of Personal Data. \n\n# **_8. Accountability and Review_** \n\nEach IDB Group Institution shall establish appropriate accountability and supervisory mechanism(s) to: \n\n- a) oversee compliance with this Policy: and \n\n- b) provide Data Subjects with a method, subject to reasonable limitations and conditions, to: \n\n   - i. request information regarding the Data Subject’s Personal Data Processed by or on behalf of such IDB Group Institution; and \n\n   - ii. seek redress if the Data Subject reasonably believes that the Data Subject’s Personal Data has been Processed in violation of this Policy. \n\n# **IV. MISCELLANEOUS** \n\n1. This Policy shall be implemented by each IDB Group Institution through guidelines, procedures, and other implementation measures, as applicable, tailored to each IDB Group Institution’s specific activities (the “ **Implementing Instruments** ”). \n\n2. This Policy shall become effective for each IDB Group Institution upon the earlier to occur of the following: (i) a declaration of effectiveness by the President of the IDB, in the case of the IDB, and the General Manager of IDB Invest, in the case of the IDB Invest, or such representative as each shall designate, to be issued upon adoption and effectiveness of Implementing Instruments; and (ii) three years from the date of approval of this Policy by the respective Board. \n\n3. This Policy shall not cover Personal Data collected before its effectiveness.\n\n4. The Processing of Personal Data in accordance with this Policy is without prejudice to the privileges and immunities of the IDB Group Institutions, which privileges and immunities are specifically reserved.\n\n---\n\n[Skip to main content](#main-content)\n\n\n*Last updated on: March 18, 2026*\n\n###### **Overview**\n\nThe Inter-American Investment Corporation (“IDB Invest”, “we”, “us” and “our”) is an international organization founded by international treaty in 1986 and is a member of the Inter-American Development Bank Group (“IDB Group”). As such, it is not subject to any national or supranational laws.\n\nThis Privacy Notice (“Privacy Notice”) explains how IDB Invest collects, uses, stores, transfers or otherwise processes the Personal Data of individuals (other than our own personnel and their dependents) (“you”). For the purposes of this Privacy Notice, Personal Data means any information relating to an identified or identifiable individual, such as a person’s name, contact details, location data, or factors relating to their physical, economic, cultural or social identity, or any other information that may reasonably be linked to that individual.\n\nIf you are either (i) the direct or indirect beneficiary of IDB Invest [Products and Services](https://idbinvest.org/en/solutions), or (ii) a representative of, or otherwise associated with, businesses and other organizations currently or potentially benefiting from or participating in IDB Invest’s [Products or Services](https://idbinvest.org/en/solutions) (for example, employees, officers, shareholders, directors, beneficial owners, guarantors or key vendors or partners of such businesses or organizations), this Privacy Notice applies to the processing of your Personal Data.\n\nPersonal data is processed by IDB Invest in accordance with the [IDB Group Personal Data Privacy Policy](https://idbinvest.org/sites/default/files/2022-11/IDB%20Group%20Personal%20Data%20Privacy%20Policy.pdf) (the “Privacy Policy”). Such processing enables IDB Invest to carry out its mission, mandate and purpose as an international organization established by its member countries.\n\nPlease ensure that you read this Privacy Notice in its entirety, as amended from time to time.\n\n---\n\n###### **What Does this Privacy Notice Cover?**\n\nThis Privacy Notice relates to the Personal Data we collect and process from you, and covers the following aspects:\n\n(Click on the topic you want to read)\n\n* [The contexts in which we process your Personal Data;](#1)\n* [The types of Personal Data that we process about you;](#2)\n* [The sources from which IDB Invest obtain your Personal Data;](#3)\n* [How and why IDB Invest processes your Personal Data;](#4)\n* [How long we keep your Personal Data;](#5)\n* [How, why and to whom we transfer your Personal Data;](#6)\n* [How we protect your Personal Data;](#7)\n* [Changes to this Privacy Notice;](#8)\n* [Explains the application of our privileges and immunities;](#9) and\n* [Explains how you may contact us with queries or complaints.](#10)\n\n---\n\n###### **The Contexts in Which we Process your Personal Data**\n\nThe Personal Data processing activities we undertake will vary based on your relationship with IDB Invest.\n\n**I. Visitors to IDB Invest’s websites**\n\nIDB Invest does not automatically process Personal Data related to the visitors of its website, e.g. idbinvest.org, or official IDB Invest pages on other platforms. However, we will process Personal Data that you submit through any interface of the official websites (for example, when registering for an event). This Privacy Notice does not apply to third party websites. We encourage you to review the privacy notices of any third-party websites you visit.\n\n**II. Subscribers of IDB Invest newsletters or publications**\n\nIf you subscribe to an IDB Invest newsletter or publication, we process your Personal Data (for example, your name and e-mail address) so we can make sure that you receive it.\n\n**III. Registered attendees of IDB Invest events**\n\nIf you register to attend an IDB Invest event, we collect and process your Personal Data in connection with the organization and management of the event.\n\n**IV. Personal Data processed in the course of providing our Products and Services**\n\nIn the course of providing our Products and Services IDB Invest processes Personal Data.\n\n**V. Personal Data in the context of recruitment**\n\nPersonal Data is required to manage job applications and recruitment processes. For detailed information, please refer to the privacy notice provided to job applicants during the application process ([available here](https://www.iadb.org/en/terms-conditions-and-notices/privacy-notice/job-applicant-privacy-notice)).\n\n**VI. Personal Data in the context of procurement**\n\nIn the course of providing our procurement activities, IDB Invest processes Personal Data.\n\n**VII. Business planning, client strategy, communications and analytics activities**\n\nIf you engage with IDB Invest as a business contact, prospective client, or external stakeholder (for example, through meetings, conferences, or professional networking), we may process your Personal Data for business development, client engagement, and institutional communications purposes.\n\n---\n\n###### **What Personal Data do we Process?**\n\nWe may collect and process the following Personal Data about you:\n\n* **Identification and contact data –** name, postal address(es), email address, phone number(s), signature specimen, passport/nationality identity documents (including embedded photographs), age and date of birth, citizenship status, office location, and limited biometric identifiers used for identity verification or security purposes;\n* **Operations data –** information about your involvement in, and/or the development impact on you of, our investment and advisory operations and activities;\n* **Financial data –** relevant financial information of how you benefit directly or indirectly from our Products and Services;\n* **Background data –** relevant background information used for anti-corruption and anti-fraud assessments in accordance with our applicable policies and procedures;\n* **Professional data –** job title, employer details or organizational affiliation, photograph in your CV, professional history, qualification details, information about your experience, participation in meetings, seminars, and conferences, information about your professional relationship with other individuals or institutions, language abilities, and other professional skills;\n* **Correspondence –** records of any correspondence we may have with you, records of your correspondence preferences (including subscription to our newsletters);\n* **Consent records –** records of preferences and permissions you provide to us, including records of consent opt-in/opt-out choices, where applicable. When maintained, such records are used solely to demonstrate compliance with applicable legal, contractual or governance obligations and to respect your stated preferences;\n* **Data relating to our websites –** technical data (device type, operating system, browser type and settings, IP address, language settings), usage and behavioral data, connection information (dates, times, location), analytics, and aggregate statistical information.\n* **Diversity and inclusion data –** salutations, gender identity, race / ethnicity, disability status;\n\nIn limited circumstances, IDB Invest may process special categories of Personal Data, such as information relating to an individual’s health, racial or ethnic origin, or other similarly sensitive characteristics. Such data will be processed only where strictly necessary and in accordance with applicable institutional policies and will be subject to enhanced safeguards designed to ensure an appropriate level of protection for the confidentiality, integrity, and security of the Personal Data.\n\n---\n\n###### **Where we Obtain your Personal Data?**\n\nWe may obtain or receive Personal Data about you from the following sources:\n\n* **Personal Data you or your employer provide to us –** Personal Data provided directly by you (e.g., job applications, correspondence you send us, information you provide to our investment officers, or when you complete an online form or survey), or that is provided to us by your employer or other organization with which you are associated, and information collected during meetings, events, and business interactions.\n* **Personal Data we collect by automated means –** As noted above, we may obtain certain information by automated means when you visit our websites.\n* **Personal Data we collect from third parties –** We may collect or obtain Personal Data from third parties (e.g., counterparties to a transaction, law enforcement authorities, relevant business contacts, specialized databases operated by the private sector, specialized external service providers, consultants or vendors).\n* **Personal Data you make public –** We may collect or obtain Personal Data that you manifestly choose to make public, including via social media (e.g., we may collect information from your social media profile(s), if you make a public post about us).\n\n---\n\n###### **Why we Process your Personal Data?**\n\nIDB Invest processes your Personal Data as reasonably necessary to conduct and manage our activities within the contexts listed above. This includes processing Personal Data for any of the following purposes:\n\n**I. To carry out IDB Invest’s investment, advisory and asset management activities**\n\n* Exploring investment opportunities and conducting due diligence;\n* Executing legal instruments related to investment, advisory and asset management activities;\n* Administering and managing our relationships with counterparties (and potential counterparties) in the context of our investment, advisory and asset management activities (or potential activities that may be of interest);\n* Understanding and monitoring the development impact of our activities;\n* Investigating and responding to complaints, and establishing, exercising, or defending IDB Invest’s legal rights and obligations;\n* Coordinating with other IDB Group Institutions; and,\n* Supporting equality, diversity and inclusion in our projects.\n\n**II. To comply with legal and policy obligations and manage risk**\n\n* Performing internal governance functions;\n* Conducting accounting and financial management;\n* Maintaining appropriate accounting, financial management and other records;\n* Fulfill our policy obligations, confirming and verifying your identity, and screening against government and/or law enforcement agency sanctions lists and other legal restrictions;\n* Carrying out our obligations, and exercising our rights, under applicable legal or regulatory requirements and any contracts entered into between you and IDB Invest;\n* Conducting credit and other risk assessment and control activities, including for the prevention and detection of corruption and fraud; and,\n* Training our staff and maintaining and improving the quality of our internal processes and arrangements.\n\n**III. To manage communications, stakeholder engagement and business development**\n\n* Disseminating information to further IDB Invest’s mission to improve lives in Latin America and the Caribbean, and providing research information;\n* Responding to your queries and feedback (for example, if you have asked a question or submitted feedback through our website);\n* Providing you with information, products or services you have requested or that may be of interest to you, unless you tell us otherwise; and,\n* Conducting business intelligence operations; and conducting business planning and client strategy activities, including organizing and managing events for clients and potential clients; conducting business analysis, planning and monitoring; preparing and disseminating marketing, institutional and business communications; defining communications strategies, guidelines and mechanisms; developing and communicating plans, strategies, strategic initiatives and updates to internal and external stakeholders; understanding client behavior through analytics to design and enhance client experiences; conducting impact evaluations and other in-depth studies (which may include surveys with project beneficiaries and other stakeholders); and supporting business development and client engagement initiatives.\n\n**IV. In connection with the management of IDB Invest’s websites, data analytics and IT security**\n\n* Providing access, maintaining and improving our websites and services;\n* Enabling you to participate in any interactive features of our websites and communicating with you, including through our newsletter, subject to your preferences;\n* Presenting website content in a manner suitable for the device you are accessing it from Undertaking data analytics to understand how users interact with our websites and online public-facing materials;\n* Monitoring and analyzing the use of our products and services for purposes of developing and improving them;\n* Managing and ensuring the security of our IT systems, including detecting and preventing misuse or abuse of our websites and services, and for backup and disaster recovery purposes; and,\n* We may also process Personal Data for any other purpose described to you at the time your data is collected.\n\nWe may also collect and process Personal Data of visitors to our premises, including for the purposes of ensuring safety and security at those premises, as further detailed in the notices available at our premises.\n\n---\n\n###### **How Long we Keep your Personal Data**\n\nYour Personal Data will be kept only as long as necessary for the purposes set out in this Privacy Notice and in accordance with IDB Invest’s applicable records retention and disposition schedules. The specific length of time will depend on the type of Personal Data, the reasons for which it is processed, and other obligations under IDB Invest’s policies and procedures.\n\n---\n\n###### **International Transfers of Personal Data**\n\nWhen you submit Personal Data to us by any means, that Personal Data may be transferred to a jurisdiction other than the one in which you live. In particular, Personal Data may be transferred to the United States. The data protection and other privacy laws of the United States may not afford the same level of protection as the laws of other countries.\n\n---\n\n###### **To whom we Disclose your Personal Data?**\n\nIDB Invest may disclose your Personal Data to the recipients described below, as reasonably necessary for the purposes outlined in this Privacy Notice.\n\n* IDB Group Institutions: We may disclose your Personal Data to other IDB Group institutions, such as the Inter-American Development Bank, as necessary for the purposes set out in this Privacy Notice.\n* Third parties: Unless otherwise noted below, and subject to contractually agreed conditions of confidentiality and security (where applicable), we may disclose your Personal Data to the categories of parties listed below:\n  + Service providers and suppliers who perform services, such as event vendors and organizers, consulting firms, among others, and providers that support compliance processes, including KYC screening and due diligence processes.\n  + Legal and other advisors that assist, advise or represent an IDB Group Institution as needed, such as attorneys, in connection with litigation, investigations, advising on contractual obligations, or enabling an IDB Group Institution to carry out its development mandate.\n  + Relevant legal, regulatory or administrative authorities, as we believe to be appropriate, for example, public registers involved in the execution and enforcement of relevant transaction documents, and other relevant authorities to protect and defend our rights and property, protect the interests of the IDB Group or others; or enable us to pursue available remedies or limit the damages that we may sustain; and,\n  + Other selected third parties: legal entities, including financial institutions, custodians, brokers, private companies, intermediaries, donors, partners and other organizations with which you are associated or involved (if any) in connection with our Products or Services; and peer researchers from academia, who carry out impact evaluations, among others.\n\nIDB Invest seeks to ensure that all partners and service providers processing Personal Data on its behalf implement appropriate technical and organizational safeguards to protect the privacy and security of such data.\n\n---\n\n###### **How to Request Information on your Personal Data Processed by IDB Invest**\n\nAs part of its data privacy framework, IDB Invest has established a procedure for individuals to request information regarding their Personal Data processed by IDB Invest and, when appropriate, to seek redress if they reasonably believe their Personal Data has not been processed in accordance with the IDB Group Personal Data Privacy Policy.\n\nYou may submit such a request using the webform [available here](https://forms.office.com/r/QAvQqSEBdy).\n\n---\n\n###### **How we Protect your Personal Data**\n\nWe have appropriate technical (e.g., firewalls, malware scans, anti-virus protection, encryption, physical locks) and organizational (e.g., policies and procedures, privacy assessments, due diligence, awareness, and training) safeguards in place to prevent unauthorized processing and accidental loss, damage, or destruction of Personal Data. These safeguards take into account the sensitivity of the data, as well as the current state of technology. We also have procedures in place to deal with data breaches, and we will notify you accordingly when appropriate.\n\n---\n\n###### **Changes to this Privacy Notice**\n\nThis Privacy Notice was last updated on the date listed above. If we change it, we will post the new version to this website.\n\n---\n\n###### **Queries and Complaints**\n\nIf you have any complaints or queries regarding your Personal Data, please contact [[email protected]](/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection#b0c0c2d9c6d1d3c9f0f9f4f2d9dec6d5c3c49edfc2d7).\n\n---\n\n###### **Privileges and Immunities**\n\nNothing contained in this Privacy Notice shall constitute or be considered to be a limitation upon or a waiver of the privileges and immunities of IDB Invest, which are specifically reserved.\n\n\n---\n\n# **<u>IDB GROUP PERSONAL DATA PRIVACY POLICY</u>**<sup>**1**</sup> \n\n# **I. PURPOSE AND APPLICATION** \n\nThis document sets out the Policy for the Processing of Personal Data by IDB Group Institutions. \n\nThis Policy applies to the Processing of Personal Data by, or on behalf of, IDB Group Institutions, and is intended to develop consistent practices across the IDB Group. \n\n# **II. DEFINITIONS** \n\nCapitalized terms or acronyms used in this Policy have the meaning set out below: \n\n**_1._ Board(s)** : the Boards of Executive Directors of IDB and IDB Invest, respectively. \n\n**_2._ Data Subject** : a natural, living person to whom Personal Data pertains, and whose Personal Data is Processed by an IDB Group Institution. Data Subjects may include, without limitation, any current or former: (i) IDB Group Institution staff member, director or their dependents; (ii) IDB Group Institution contractor or consultant; (iii) applicant for a vacancy at an IDB Group Institution; (iv) IDB Group Institution suppliers or vendors; (v) IDB Group Institution client or their representatives; (vi) respondents to IDB Group Institution surveys; or (vii) subscribers to an IDB Group Institution website. \n\n**_3._ IDB** : the Inter-American Development Bank. \n\n**_4._ IDB Group** : the Inter-American Development Bank Group. \n\n**_5._ IDB Group Institution** : any one of the IDB<sup>2</sup> and IDB Invest. \n\n**_6._ IDB Invest** : the Inter-American Investment Corporation. \n\n**_7._ Implementing Instruments** : has the meaning set forth in Section IV below. \n\n**_8._ Personal Data** : any information relating to an identified or identifiable Data Subject. An identifiable Data Subject is one who can be identified by reasonable means, directly or indirectly, by reference to an attribute or combination of attributes within the data, or combination of the data with other available information. Examples of attributes that can be used to identify an identifiable Data Subject include their name, identification number, location data, online identifier, metadata, and factors specific to their physical, physiological, genetic, mental, economic, cultural or social identity. \n\n**_9._ Policy** : this Personal Data Privacy Policy. \n\n**_10._ Principles** : the principles set out in Section III below. \n\n> 1 This Policy is not effective yet pursuant to Section IV below. \n\n> 2 The Multilateral Investment Fund (commercially known as IDB Lab) is a fund administered by the IDB and, therefore, any references to IDB Group Institution include IDB Lab.\n\n**_11._ Processing** : any action or set of actions, automated or not, which is performed on Personal Data, which may include, without limitation, its collection, recording, use, consultation, retrieval, disclosure by transmission, dissemination or otherwise making available, forwarding, organization, storage, structuring, adaptation or alteration, alignment or combination, restriction, erasure or destruction. \n\n**_12._ Processed** : having undertaken the act of Processing. \n\n**_13._ Third Party** or **Third Parties** : a legal person, other than IDB Group Institutions, or a natural person, other than IDB Group Institutions’ personnel and their dependents, as defined within their respective policies and procedures. \n\n# **III. PRINCIPLES** \n\nThe following Principles shall apply to all Processing of Personal Data by IDB Group Institutions: \n\n# **_1. Legitimate, Fair and Transparent Processing_** \n\nPersonal Data shall only be Processed for legitimate purposes and in a fair and transparent manner. Legitimate purposes for Processing mean any purpose: \n\n- a. for which the consent of a Data Subject is obtained, either at the time Personal Data are collected or subsequently; \n\n- b. that is in the vital or best interest of (i) the Data Subject or (ii) another person; \n\n- c. that is reasonably necessary for the performance of a contract; \n\n- d. that is reasonably necessary to enable an IDB Group Institution to satisfy an obligation or undertaking, or to comply with an IDB Group Institution’s policy or procedure; \n\n- e. that is reasonably necessary to establish, exercise or defend an IDB Group Institution’s right or interest; or \n\n- f. that is consistent with, or reasonably necessary to enable an IDB Group Institution to carry out its mission, mandate or purpose as an international organization established by its member countries. \n\n# **_2. Purpose Limitation_** \n\nPersonal Data shall be collected for one or more specific and legitimate purpose(s) listed in Principle 1 above and not further Processed in a manner that is incompatible with such purpose(s). Further Processing for archiving purposes, research, or statistical purposes shall not be considered incompatible with such purpose(s).\n\n# **_3. Data Minimization_** \n\nThe amount and type of Personal Data collected shall be reasonably necessary for, and proportionate to, the legitimate purpose(s) for which it is Processed. \n\n# **_4. Data Accuracy_** \n\nPersonal Data shall be recorded as accurately as possible and, where necessary, updated to fulfill the legitimate purpose(s) for which it is Processed. \n\n# **_5. Storage Limitation_** \n\nPersonal Data shall be kept in a form which permits identification of Data Subjects for no longer than is necessary for the legitimate purpose for which the Personal Data is collected, or for compatible further Processing, in accordance with this Policy. \n\n# **_6. Security_** \n\nPersonal Data shall be protected by appropriate and reasonable technical and organizational safeguards against unauthorized Processing and against accidental loss, destruction or damage. \n\n# **_7. Transfer of Personal Data_** \n\nPersonal Data shall only be transferred to a Third Party for legitimate purposes in accordance with this Policy and with appropriate regard for the protection of Personal Data. \n\n# **_8. Accountability and Review_** \n\nEach IDB Group Institution shall establish appropriate accountability and supervisory mechanism(s) to: \n\n- a) oversee compliance with this Policy: and \n\n- b) provide Data Subjects with a method, subject to reasonable limitations and conditions, to: \n\n   - i. request information regarding the Data Subject’s Personal Data Processed by or on behalf of such IDB Group Institution; and \n\n   - ii. seek redress if the Data Subject reasonably believes that the Data Subject’s Personal Data has been Processed in violation of this Policy. \n\n# **IV. MISCELLANEOUS** \n\n1. This Policy shall be implemented by each IDB Group Institution through guidelines, procedures, and other implementation measures, as applicable, tailored to each IDB Group Institution’s specific activities (the “ **Implementing Instruments** ”). \n\n2. This Policy shall become effective for each IDB Group Institution upon the earlier to occur of the following: (i) a declaration of effectiveness by the President of the IDB, in the case of the IDB, and the General Manager of IDB Invest, in the case of the IDB Invest, or such representative as each shall designate, to be issued upon adoption and effectiveness of Implementing Instruments; and (ii) three years from the date of approval of this Policy by the respective Board. \n\n3. This Policy shall not cover Personal Data collected before its effectiveness.\n\n4. The Processing of Personal Data in accordance with this Policy is without prejudice to the privileges and immunities of the IDB Group Institutions, which privileges and immunities are specifically reserved."", ""veredicto"": ""SI"", ""justificacion"": ""El texto permite el descarga, copia y reimpresión de la información para fines no comerciales, siempre que se cite a IDB Invest como fuente, lo que autoriza el uso con atribución en contextos no comerciales.""}]",,
https://humanidadesmedicas.sld.cu/,Licencia mencionada (ver comentarios),DEPENDE,"Se permite el uso siempre que se dé atribución y no se utilice con fines comerciales (cláusula NonCommercial), pero el veredicto depende de si el uso propuesto es comercial o no, y de cumplir con los requisitos de atribución.","[{""categoria"": null, ""via"": ""footer"", ""url_origen"": ""https://humanidadesmedicas.sld.cu/"", ""markdown_path"": null, ""texto_inline"": ""[Skip to content](#main-content-marker)\n\n\nLanguages available\n\naragonés\n\nAzərbaycanca\n\nBahasa Indonesia\n\nBasque\n\ncatalà\n\ndansk\n\nDeutsch\n\neesti\n\nEnglish\n\nespañol\n\nEsperanto\n\nfrançais\n\nfrysk\n\nGaeilge\n\ngalego\n\nHrvatski\n\nitaliano\n\nlatviešu\n\nLietuviškai\n\nMagyar\n\nMelayu\n\nNederlands\n\nnorsk\n\npolski\n\nPortuguês\n\nPortuguês Brasileiro\n\nRomână\n\nSlovensky\n\nSlovenščina\n\nsrpski (latinica)\n\nsuomi\n\nsvenska\n\nTürkçe\n\nÍslenska\n\nčesky\n\nΕλληνικά\n\nбеларуская\n\nбългарски\n\nРусский\n\nУкраїнська\n\nالعربيّة\n\nفارسی\n\nहिंदी\n\nবাংলা\n\n日本語\n\n简体中文\n\n繁體中文\n\n한국어\n\n\n\n## Canonical URL\n\n<https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/>\n\n[See the legal code](legalcode.en)\n\n## You are free to:\n\n1. **Share** — copy and redistribute the material in any\n   medium or format\n2. **Adapt** — remix, transform, and build upon the\n   material\n3. The licensor cannot revoke these freedoms as long as you follow\n   the license terms.\n\n## Under the following terms:\n\n1. **Attribution** — You must give\n   [appropriate credit](#ref-appropriate-credit), provide a link to the license, and\n   [indicate if changes were made](#ref-indicate-changes). You may do so in any reasonable manner, but not in any way that\n   suggests the licensor endorses you or your use.\n2. **NonCommercial** — You may not use the material for\n   [commercial purposes](#ref-commercial-purposes).\n3. **No additional restrictions** — You may not apply\n   legal terms or\n   [technological measures](